(710, 723, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: javascript functions arrays conditional statements looping statements</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=javascript+functions+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/javascript+functions+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/javascript+functions+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/javascript+functions+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=javascript+functions+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>JavaScript Looping Statements: Real-World Applications with Functions</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, you will learn about JavaScript functions, arrays, conditional statements, and looping statements. You will understand how to use these concepts to create real-world applications.</p>\n<h3>JavaScript Functions</h3>\n<p>A JavaScript function is a block of code that can be executed multiple times from different parts of your program. Functions are useful for reusing code and making your program more modular.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> greet(name) {\n  console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Hello, &#39; + name);</span>\n}\ngreet(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;John&#39;);  // Outputs: Hello, John</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Functions can also take multiple parameters and return values.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> add(a, b) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> a + b;\n}\nconsole.log(add(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>));  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Outputs: 8</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>JavaScript Arrays</h3>\n<p>A JavaScript array is a collection of values that can be of any data type, including strings, numbers, and objects. Arrays are useful for storing and manipulating collections of data.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruits = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'apple\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'banana\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'cherry\'</span>];\nconsole.log(fruits[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>]);  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Outputs: apple</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Arrays also have methods for adding, removing, and manipulating elements.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\nfruits.push(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'orange\'</span>);\nconsole.log(fruits);  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Outputs: [\'apple\', \'banana\', \'cherry\', \'orange\']</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>JavaScript Conditional Statements</h3>\n<p>JavaScript conditional statements allow you to execute different blocks of code based on conditions. The most common conditional statements are if/else and switch.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> age = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">25</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (age >= <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">18</span>) {\n  console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;You are an adult.&#39;);</span>\n} <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n  console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;You are a minor.&#39;);</span>\n}\n</code></pre>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> grade = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'A\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">switch</span> (grade) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">case</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'A\'</span>:\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Excellent!&#39;);</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">break</span>;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">case</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'B\'</span>:\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Good.&#39;);</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">break</span>;\n  default:\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Not good.&#39;);</span>\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3>JavaScript Looping Statements</h3>\n<p>JavaScript looping statements allow you to execute a block of code repeatedly. The most common looping statements are for and while.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; i < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>; i++) {\n  console.log(i);\n}\n</code></pre>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">while</span> (i < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>) {\n  console.log(i);\n  i++;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Real-World Applications with Functions</h3>\n<p>Functions can be used to create real-world applications such as calculators, quizzes, and games.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> calculator() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> num1 = prompt(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Enter the first number: &#39;);</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> num2 = prompt(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Enter the second number: &#39;);</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> operator = prompt(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Enter the operator (+, -, *, /): &#39;);</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (operator === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'+\'</span>) {\n    console.log(num1 + num2);\n  } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (operator === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'-\'</span>) {\n    console.log(num1 - num2);\n  } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (operator === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'*\'</span>) {\n    console.log(num1 * num2);\n  } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (operator === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/\'</span>) {\n    console.log(num1 / num2);\n  } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Invalid operator.&#39;);</span>\n  }\n}\ncalculator();\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Real-World Applications with Arrays</h3>\n<p>Arrays can be used to create real-world applications such as to-do lists, shopping carts, and contact lists.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> toDoList = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Buy milk\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Walk the dog\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Do laundry\'</span>];\nconsole.log(toDoList);\ntoDoList.push(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Clean the house\'</span>);\nconsole.log(toDoList);\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Real-World Applications with Conditional Statements</h3>\n<p>Conditional statements can be used to create real-world applications such as quizzes, games, and interactive stories.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> score = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> question = prompt(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;What is the capital of France?&#39;);</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (question === &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Paris&#39;) {</span>\n  score++;\n  console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Correct! Your score is: &#39; + score);</span>\n} <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n  console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Incorrect. The correct answer is Paris.&#39;);</span>\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Real-World Applications with Looping Statements</h3>\n<p>Looping statements can be used to create real-world applications such as calculators, quizzes, and games.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">while</span> (i < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>) {\n  console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Question &#39; + (i + 1));</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> answer = prompt(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Enter your answer: &#39;);</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (answer === &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;correct&#39;) {</span>\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Correct!&#39;);</span>\n  } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Incorrect.&#39;);</span>\n  }\n  i++;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<p>Test your knowledge of JavaScript functions, arrays, conditional statements, and looping statements with this quiz.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>What is the purpose of a JavaScript function?</li>\n  <li>What is the difference between an array and an object in JavaScript?</li>\n  <li>What is the purpose of a conditional statement in JavaScript?</li>\n  <li>What is the difference between a for loop and a while loop in JavaScript?</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Create a real-world application using JavaScript functions, arrays, conditional statements, and looping statements. The application should have a user interface and allow users to interact with it.</p>\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n<p>Search for images related to JavaScript, functions, arrays, conditional statements, and looping statements.</p>\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, you learned about JavaScript functions, arrays, conditional statements, and looping statements. You also learned how to use these concepts to create real-world applications. Practice and build more projects to reinforce your understanding of these concepts.</p>\n<h3>Additional Resources</h3>\n<p>Check out the following resources for more information on JavaScript functions, arrays, conditional statements, and looping statements.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><a href=&#39;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Guide/Functions&#39;>JavaScript Functions</a></li>\n  <li><a href=&#39;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Guide/Predefined_objects#Array_object&#39;>JavaScript Arrays</a></li>\n  <li><a href=&#39;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/if...else&#39;>JavaScript Conditional Statements</a></li>\n  <li><a href=&#39;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/for...of&#39;>JavaScript Looping Statements</a></li>\n</ul>\n</h3>', 'JavaScript Looping Statements: Real-World Applications with Functions', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(711, 724, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: javascript functions higher-order functions closures arrays conditional statements looping statements</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=javascript+functions+higher-order+functions+closures+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/javascript+functions+higher-order+functions+closures+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/javascript+functions+higher-order+functions+closures+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/javascript+functions+higher-order+functions+closures+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=javascript+functions+higher-order+functions+closures+arrays+conditional+statements+looping+statements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h2>JavaScript Functions: Higher-Order Functions and Closures</h2>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, we will be exploring JavaScript functions, specifically higher-order functions and closures. We will also cover JavaScript conditional statements and looping statements.</p>\n<h3>JavaScript Functions</h3>\n<p>A function in JavaScript is a block of code that can be executed multiple times from different parts of a program. Functions can take arguments and return values.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> greet(name) {\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Hello, &#39; + name);</span>\n}\ngreet(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;John&#39;); // Output: Hello, John</span></code></pre>\n<h3>Higher-Order Functions</h3>\n<p>A higher-order function is a function that takes another function as an argument or returns a function as a result. In JavaScript, we can use the callback function as a higher-order function.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> higherOrderFunction(callback) {\n    callback();\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> sayHello() {\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Hello&#39;);</span>\n}\nhigherOrderFunction(sayHello); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: Hello</span></code></pre>\n<h3>Closures</h3>\n<p>A closure is a function that has access to its outer function\'s scope, even when the outer function has returned. Closures are useful when we need to create a new function that has access to some variables from the outer function.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> outerFunction() {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> name = &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;John&#39;;</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> innerFunction() {\n        console.log(name);\n    }\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> innerFunction;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> inner = outerFunction();\ninner(); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: John</span></code></pre>\n<h3>JavaScript Conditional Statements</h3>\n<p>Conditional statements in JavaScript are used to execute different blocks of code based on certain conditions. We have if-else statements, switch statements, and ternary operators.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> age = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">25</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (age >= <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">18</span>) {\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;You are an adult&#39;);</span>\n} <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n    console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;You are a minor&#39;);</span>\n}\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: You are an adult</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> color = &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;red&#39;;</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">switch</span> (color) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">case</span> &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;red&#39;:</span>\n        console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;The color is red&#39;);</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">break</span>;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">case</span> &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;green&#39;:</span>\n        console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;The color is green&#39;);</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">break</span>;\n    default:\n        console.log(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;The color is unknown&#39;);</span>\n}\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: The color is red</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> isAdult = age >= <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">18</span> ? &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;You are an adult&#39; : &#39;You are a minor&#39;;</span>\nconsole.log(isAdult);\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: You are an adult</span></code></pre>\n<h3>JavaScript Looping Statements</h3>\n<p>Looping statements in JavaScript are used to execute a block of code repeatedly. We have for loops, while loops, and do-while loops.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; i < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>; i++) {\n    console.log(i);\n}\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">while</span> (i < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>) {\n    console.log(i);\n    i++;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> j = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">do</span> {\n    console.log(j);\n    j++;\n} <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">while</span> (j < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4</span></code></pre>\n<h3>Arrays</h3>\n<p>Arrays in JavaScript are used to store multiple values in a single variable. We can use the push method to add elements to the end of an array.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>];\nnumbers.push(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>);\nconsole.log(numbers); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [1, 2, 3, 4]</span></code></pre>\n<h3>Using Higher-Order Functions with Arrays</h3>\n<p>We can use higher-order functions with arrays to perform operations on the array elements. For example, we can use the map method to create a new array with the square of each element.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>];\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> squares = numbers.map(x => x * x);\nconsole.log(squares); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [1, 4, 9]</span></code></pre>\n<h3>Using Closures with Arrays</h3>\n<p>We can use closures with arrays to create a new function that has access to the array elements. For example, we can create a function that takes an index and returns the element at that index.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>];\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> getNumber(index) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> numbers[index];\n}\nconsole.log(getNumber(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>)); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 2</span></code></pre>\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<p>Write a function that takes a string and returns the string in uppercase using a higher-order function.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> toUppercase(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">str</span>) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">str</span>.toUpperCase();\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> higherOrderFunction(callback) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> callback();\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> result = higherOrderFunction(toUppercase.bind(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">null</span>, &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;hello&#39;));</span>\nconsole.log(result); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: HELLO</span></code></pre>\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n<p>Search for images related to JavaScript functions.</p>\n<p>&#39;JavaScript functions, higher-order functions, closures, arrays, conditional statements, looping statements, image query&#39;</p>\n<p>Image query: &#39;javascript functions, higher-order functions, closures, arrays, conditional statements, looping statements&#39;</p>', 'JavaScript Functions: Higher-Order Functions and Closures', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(712, 725, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: short search query</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>JavaScript Arrays: Filtering and Mapping with Functions</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, you will learn about JavaScript arrays, functions, conditional statements, and looping statements. By the end of this task, you will be able to filter and map arrays using JavaScript functions.</p>\n<h3>Concepts You Need:</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>JavaScript Functions</li>\n  <li>JavaScript Conditional Statements (if-else statements)</li>\n  <li>JavaScript Looping Statements (for loops, while loops)</li>\n  <li>JavaScript Arrays</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions:</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Step 1: Understanding JavaScript Arrays</strong>\n    <p>JavaScript arrays are used to store multiple values in a single variable. You can create an array using the <code>[]</code> syntax.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruits = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'apple\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'banana\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'cherry\'</span>];</code></pre>\n    <p>Arrays can store different data types, including strings, numbers, and objects.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>];</code></pre>\n    <p>Arrays can also store objects.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> person = {name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'John\'</span>, age: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">30</span>};</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> people = [person, {name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Jane\'</span>, age: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">25</span>}];</code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Step 2: Understanding JavaScript Functions</strong>\n    <p>JavaScript functions are reusable blocks of code that can be called multiple times from different parts of your program.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> greet(name) { console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Hello, \'</span> + name); }</code></pre>\n    <p>You can call a function by its name, followed by parentheses containing the function\'s arguments.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">greet(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'John\'</span>);</code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Step 3: Filtering Arrays with Functions</strong>\n    <p>Filtering an array means creating a new array that includes only the elements that meet certain conditions.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>];</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> evenNumbers = numbers.filter(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(num) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> num % <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; });</code></pre>\n    <p>The <code>filter()</code> method creates a new array with all elements that pass the test implemented by the provided function.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">console.log(evenNumbers); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [2, 4]</span></code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Step 4: Mapping Arrays with Functions</strong>\n    <p>MAPPING an array means creating a new array with the results of applying a function to every element in the original array.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruits = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'apple\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'banana\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'cherry\'</span>];</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruitUppercase = fruits.map(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(fruit) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> fruit.toUpperCase(); });</code></pre>\n    <p>The <code>map()</code> method creates a new array with the results of applying a provided function on every element in this array.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">console.log(fruitUppercase); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [\'APPLE\', \'BANANA\', \'CHERRY\']</span></code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Step 5: Using Conditional Statements with Arrays</strong>\n    <p>Conditional statements are used to execute different blocks of code based on certain conditions.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>];</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> evenNumbers = [];</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> num of numbers) {</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (num % <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>) {</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">    evenNumbers.push(num);</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">  }</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">}</code></pre>\n    <p>This code will push even numbers from the <code>numbers</code> array to the <code>evenNumbers</code> array.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">console.log(evenNumbers); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [2, 4]</span></code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Step 6: Using Looping Statements with Arrays</strong>\n    <p>Looping statements are used to execute a block of code repeatedly for a specified number of times.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruits = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'apple\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'banana\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'cherry\'</span>];</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; i < fruits.length; i++) {</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">  console.log(fruits[i]);</code></pre>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">}</code></pre>\n    <p>This code will log each fruit in the <code>fruits</code> array to the console.</p>\n  </li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Deliverable:</h3>\n<p>Implement a JavaScript function called <code>filterAndMap()</code> that takes an array of numbers as input and returns a new array with only the even numbers and their squares.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> filterAndMap(numbers) {</code></pre>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> evenSquares = numbers.filter(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(num) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> num % <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; }).map(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(num) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> num * num; });</code></pre>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> evenSquares;</code></pre>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">}</code></pre>\n<h3>Example Use Case:</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>];</code></pre>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> result = filterAndMap(numbers);</code></pre>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">console.log(result); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [4, 16]</span></code></pre>\n<h3>Quiz:</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>What is the difference between the <code>filter()</code> and <code>map()</code> methods in JavaScript?</li>\n  <li>How do you create an array in JavaScript?</li>\n  <li>What is the purpose of conditional statements in JavaScript?</li>\n  <li>How do you use a for loop to iterate over an array in JavaScript?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Answer the quiz questions in the comments below.</p>\n<h3>Image Query:</h3>\n<p>Search for \'JavaScript arrays\' on Google Images.</p>\n<h3>HTML Code:</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;h3&gt;JavaScript Arrays: Filtering <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> Mapping <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> Functions&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;In <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span> hands-on internship, you will learn about JavaScript arrays, functions, conditional statements, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> looping statements. By the end of <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span> task, you will be able to filter <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> map arrays <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">using</span> JavaScript functions.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Concepts You Need:&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;JavaScript Functions&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;JavaScript Conditional Statements (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span>-<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> statements)&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;JavaScript Looping Statements (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> loops, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">while</span> loops)&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;JavaScript Arrays&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Step-by-Step Instructions:&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ol&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>: Understanding JavaScript Arrays&lt;/strong&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;JavaScript arrays are used to store multiple values <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> a single variable. You can create an array <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">using</span> the &lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt; syntax.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruits = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'apple\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'banana\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'cherry\'</span>];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Arrays can store different data types, including strings, numbers, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> objects.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Arrays can also store objects.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> person = {name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'John\'</span>, age: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">30</span>};&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> people = [person, {name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Jane\'</span>, age: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">25</span>}];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n  &lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>: Understanding JavaScript Functions&lt;/strong&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;JavaScript functions are reusable blocks of code that can be called multiple times <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> different parts of your program.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> greet(name) { console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Hello, \'</span> + name); }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;You can call a <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> by its name, followed by parentheses containing the <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>\'s arguments.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;greet(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'John\'</span>);&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n  &lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>: Filtering Arrays <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> Functions&lt;/strong&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Filtering an array means creating a <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> array that includes only the elements that meet certain conditions.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> evenNumbers = numbers.filter(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(num) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> num % <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; });&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;filter()&lt;/code&gt; method creates a <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> array <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> all elements that <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">pass</span> the test implemented by the provided <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;console.log(evenNumbers); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [2, 4]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</span>\n  &lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>: Mapping Arrays <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> Functions&lt;/strong&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;MAPPING an array means creating a <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> array <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> the results of applying a <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> to every element <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> the original array.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruits = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'apple\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'banana\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'cherry\'</span>];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruitUppercase = fruits.map(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(fruit) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> fruit.toUpperCase(); });&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;map()&lt;/code&gt; method creates a <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> array <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> the results of applying a provided <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> on every element <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span> array.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;console.log(fruitUppercase); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [\'APPLE\', \'BANANA\', \'CHERRY\']&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</span>\n  &lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>: Using Conditional Statements <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> Arrays&lt;/strong&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Conditional statements are used to execute different blocks of code based on certain conditions.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> evenNumbers = [];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> num of numbers) {&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (num % <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>) {&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;    evenNumbers.push(num);&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;  }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This code will push even numbers <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> the &lt;code&gt;numbers&lt;/code&gt; array to the &lt;code&gt;evenNumbers&lt;/code&gt; array.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;console.log(evenNumbers); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [2, 4]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</span>\n  &lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">6</span>: Using Looping Statements <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> Arrays&lt;/strong&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Looping statements are used to execute a block of code repeatedly <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> a specified number of times.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> fruits = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'apple\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'banana\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'cherry\'</span>];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; i &lt; fruits.length; i++) {&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;  console.log(fruits[i]);&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This code will log each fruit <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> the &lt;code&gt;fruits&lt;/code&gt; array to the console.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/ol&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Deliverable:&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Implement a JavaScript <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> called &lt;code&gt;filterAndMap()&lt;/code&gt; that takes an array of numbers <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">as</span> input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> returns a <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> array <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> only the even numbers <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> their squares.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> filterAndMap(numbers) {&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> evenSquares = numbers.filter(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(num) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> num % <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; }).map(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(num) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> num * num; });&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> evenSquares;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Example Use Case:&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> numbers = [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>];&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> result = filterAndMap(numbers);&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;console.log(result); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: [4, 16]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;</span>\n&lt;h3&gt;Quiz:&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;What <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> the difference between the &lt;code&gt;filter()&lt;/code&gt; <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> &lt;code&gt;map()&lt;/code&gt; methods <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> JavaScript?&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;How <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">do</span> you create an array <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> JavaScript?&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;What <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> the purpose of conditional statements <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> JavaScript?&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;How <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">do</span> you use a <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> loop to iterate over an array <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> JavaScript?&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Answer the quiz questions <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> the comments below.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Image Query:&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Search <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'JavaScript arrays\'</span> on Google Images.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;/h3&gt;\n</code></pre>', 'JavaScript Arrays: Filtering and Mapping with Functions', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(713, 726, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript prototype inheritance example</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+prototype+inheritance+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+prototype+inheritance+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+prototype+inheritance+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+prototype+inheritance+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+prototype+inheritance+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Understand JavaScript object prototypes, inheritance, and how to combine them with conditional and looping logic to build dynamic behavior in objects.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>JavaScript Objects:</strong> Containers for properties and methods.</li><li><strong>Prototype:</strong> A mechanism to share and inherit properties/methods across objects.</li><li><strong>Inheritance:</strong> Creating objects that inherit properties/methods from other objects.</li><li><strong>Conditional Statements:</strong> <code>if</code>, <code>else if</code>, <code>else</code> for decision-making.</li><li><strong>Looping Statements:</strong> <code>for</code>, <code>while</code>, <code>for...in</code> for repetitive tasks.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<h4>Step 1: Create a Base Object with Properties and Methods</h4>\n<p>Define a <code>Person</code> constructor function with properties like <code>name</code> and <code>age</code>, and a method <code>sayHello()</code>.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> Person(name, age) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name = name;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.age = age;\n}\n\nPerson.prototype.sayHello = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n  console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Hello, my name is &quot;</span> + <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name);\n};</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 2: Use Conditional Logic to Add Dynamic Behavior</h4>\n<p>Add a method <code>checkAge()</code> that uses <code>if/else</code> to determine if the person is an adult.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">Person.prototype.checkAge = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.age &gt;= <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">18</span>) {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot; is an adult.&quot;</span>);\n  } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot; is a minor.&quot;</span>);\n  }\n};</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 3: Create an Inherited Object Using Prototypes</h4>\n<p>Build a <code>Student</code> constructor that inherits from <code>Person</code> using <code>Object.create()</code>.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> Student(name, age, grade) {\n  Person.call(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>, name, age);\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.grade = grade;\n}\n\nStudent.prototype = Object.create(Person.prototype);\nStudent.prototype.constructor = Student;</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 4: Add a Unique Method to the Child Object</h4>\n<p>Add a <code>showGrade()</code> method to the <code>Student</code> prototype.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">Student.prototype.showGrade = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n  console.log(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot; is in grade &quot;</span> + <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.grade);\n};</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 5: Use a Loop to Iterate Over Object Properties</h4>\n<p>Write a <code>for...in</code> loop to list all properties/methods of a <code>Student</code> instance.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> student1 = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Student(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Alice&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">16</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">11</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> key <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> student1) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (student1.hasOwnProperty(key)) {\n    console.log(key + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;: &quot;</span> + student1[key]);\n  }\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 6: Combine Logic with a Custom Function</h4>\n<p>Create a function that uses a <code>for</code> loop and conditionals to calculate the average of grades from an array of students.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> averageGrade(students) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> total = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; i &lt; students.length; i++) {\n    total += students[i].grade;\n  }\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> total / students.length;\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Create an <code>index.html</code> file that:</p><ul><li>Defines the <code>Person</code> and <code>Student</code> objects with all methods.</li><li>Instantiates at least two <code>Student</code> objects.</li><li>Uses <code>console.log()</code> to demonstrate inheritance, conditionals, and loops.</li><li>Includes comments explaining how prototypes and inheritance work in your code.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to inspect prototype chains with <code>Object.getPrototypeOf()</code>.</li><li>Test inheritance by calling <code>student1.sayHello()</code> and <code>student1.showGrade()</code>.</li><li>For loops, ensure you use <code>hasOwnProperty()</code> to avoid logging inherited properties.</li></ul>', 'JavaScript Objects: Understanding Prototype and Inheritance', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(714, 727, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript DOM manipulation basics</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+basics\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+basics\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+basics/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+basics/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+basics\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>JavaScript DOM Manipulation: Basic Elements and Attributes</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Task Objective:</strong> In this task, you will practice manipulating the DOM using JavaScript. You will create a webpage that dynamically updates elements based on conditions and loops. By the end, you will understand how to select, modify, and control HTML elements using JavaScript.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>DOM Manipulation Basics:</strong> Selecting elements with <code>document.getElementById()</code>, <code>document.querySelector()</code>, and modifying their content with <code>.textContent</code> or <code>.innerHTML</code>.</li>\n  <li><strong>JavaScript Conditional Statements:</strong> Using <code>if/else</code> to control logic based on conditions.</li>\n  <li><strong>JavaScript Looping Statements:</strong> Using <code>for</code> or <code>while</code> loops to repeat actions on multiple elements.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Create the HTML Structure:</strong> Write an HTML file with the following elements:\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"container\"</span>>\n      &lt;p id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"message\"</span>>Welcome to the DOM Manipulation Lab!&lt;/p>\n      &lt;ul id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"list\"</span>>\n        &lt;li <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"item\"</span>>Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/li>\n        &lt;li <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"item\"</span>>Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/li>\n      &lt;/ul>\n      &lt;button id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"toggleButton\"</span>>Toggle List&lt;/button>\n    &lt;/div>\n  </code></pre>\n  </li>\n\n  <li><strong>Modify Element Content with Conditionals:</strong> Add JavaScript to change the paragraph text based on a condition. For example:\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> message = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"message\"</span>);\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> hour = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Date().getHours();\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (hour &lt; <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">12</span>) {\n      message.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Good morning! Welcome to the DOM Lab.\"</span>;\n    } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n      message.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Good afternoon! Welcome to the DOM Lab.\"</span>;\n    }\n  </code></pre>\n  </li>\n\n  <li><strong>Loop to Add Dynamic List Items:</strong> Use a loop to add three new items to the unordered list. Example:\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> list = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"list\"</span>);\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>; i &lt;= <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>; i++) {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> newItem = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"li\"</span>);\n      newItem.className = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"item\"</span>;\n      newItem.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Item \"</span> + i;\n      list.appendChild(newItem);\n    }\n  </code></pre>\n  </li>\n\n  <li><strong>Toggle List Visibility with a Button:</strong> Add an event listener to the button to hide or show the list. Example:\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> toggleButton = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"toggleButton\"</span>);\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> list = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"list\"</span>);\n    toggleButton.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"click\"</span>, () => {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (list.style.display === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"none\"</span>) {\n        list.style.display = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"block\"</span>;\n        toggleButton.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Hide List\"</span>;\n      } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n        list.style.display = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"none\"</span>;\n        toggleButton.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Show List\"</span>;\n      }\n    });\n  </code></pre>\n  </li>\n\n  <li><strong>Combine Loops and Conditionals:</strong> Loop through all list items and add a <code>\"highlight\"</code> class to even-numbered items. Example:\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> items = document.querySelectorAll(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\".item\"</span>);\n    items.forEach((item, index) => {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (index % <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>) {\n        item.classList.add(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"highlight\"</span>);\n      }\n    });\n  </code></pre>\n  </li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Create a single HTML file that includes all the above functionality. When opened in a browser, it should:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Greet the user with \"Good morning\" or \"Good afternoon\" based on the time.</li>\n  <li>Display a list of five items (three added dynamically).</li>\n  <li>Allow the user to toggle the list visibility with a button.</li>\n  <li>Highlight even-numbered list items in a distinct style (you can add CSS for the <code>.highlight</code> class).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to debug and verify your code logic.</li>\n  <li>Test your page in a browser and use Developer Tools to inspect DOM changes.</li>\n  <li>Start with small steps—complete one task at a time and test frequently.</li>\n  <li>Remember to escape characters like <code>&lt;</code> and <code>&gt;</code> when writing HTML in JavaScript strings.</li>\n</ul>', 'JavaScript DOM Manipulation: Basic Elements and Attributes', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(715, 728, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript DOM manipulation example with HTML elements</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+example+with+HTML+elements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+example+with+HTML+elements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+example+with+HTML+elements/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+example+with+HTML+elements/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+example+with+HTML+elements\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Day 34: JavaScript DOM Manipulation - Selecting and Editing Elements</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Task Objective:</strong> Learn to select and modify HTML elements using JavaScript DOM manipulation techniques. Combine conditional statements and looping structures to dynamically update content based on user interaction.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>DOM Selection Methods:</strong> Use <code>document.getElementById()</code>, <code>document.querySelector()</code>, and <code>document.querySelectorAll()</code> to target elements.</li>\n  <li><strong>Conditional Logic:</strong> Apply <code>if/else</code> statements to make decisions based on element states.</li>\n  <li><strong>Looping Structures:</strong> Use <code>for</code> loops to iterate over collections of elements.</li>\n  <li><strong>Element Manipulation:</strong> Modify text, attributes, and styles using properties like <code>textContent</code>, <code>innerHTML</code>, and <code>style</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<h4>Step 1: Create the HTML Structure</h4>\n<p>Build a basic HTML page with elements to manipulate:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h1 id=\"title<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;DOM Practice&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;p class=\"description&quot;</span>&gt;Click the button to see changes!&lt;/p&gt;\n  \n  &lt;ul id=\"itemList<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Item 1&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Item 2&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Item 3&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n\n  &lt;button id=\"changeBtn&quot;</span>&gt;Modify Elements&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 2: Select Elements and Modify Content</h4>\n<p>Add JavaScript to select elements and update their content:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> title = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'title\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> description = document.querySelector(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'.description\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> list = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'itemList\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> button = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'changeBtn\'</span>);\n\nbutton.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Change heading text</span>\n  title.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'DOM Manipulation Complete!\'</span>;\n\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Update paragraph with bold text</span>\n  description.innerHTML = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'&lt;strong&gt;Elements have been modified&lt;/strong&gt;\'</span>;\n});</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 3: Use Conditionals to Check Element States</h4>\n<p>Add logic to verify elements exist before modifying them:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (list) {\n  list.style.border = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'2px solid blue\'</span>;\n} <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n  console.error(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'List element not found!\'</span>);\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 4: Loop Through List Items</h4>\n<p>Iterate over list items to apply changes:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> items = document.querySelectorAll(\'<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#itemList li\');</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; i < items.length; i++) {\n  items[i].addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n    items[i].style.color = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'red\'</span>;\n  });\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 5: Add Dynamic Behavior with Loops and Conditionals</h4>\n<p>Combine loops and conditionals to toggle item visibility:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">button.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> item of items) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (item.style.display === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'none\'</span>) {\n      item.style.display = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'list-item\'</span>;\n    } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n      item.style.display = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'none\'</span>;\n    }\n  }\n});</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Submit a single HTML file that:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Contains the HTML structure from Step 1</li>\n  <li>Includes JavaScript that:</li>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Selects elements by ID, class, and tag name</li>\n    <li>Uses conditionals to verify elements exist</li>\n    <li>Loops through multiple elements to apply changes</li>\n    <li>Adds interactivity with event listeners</li>\n  </ul>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>Use browser developer tools to inspect elements and debug JavaScript</li>\n  <li>Test your code by clicking elements and observing changes in real-time</li>\n  <li>Ensure all special characters in code blocks are properly escaped (e.g., &lt; for <, &gt; for >)</li>\n  <li>Start with simple changes before adding complex logic</li>\n</ul>', 'JavaScript DOM Manipulation: Selecting and Editing Elements', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(716, 729, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript DOM form validation example</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+DOM+form+validation+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+DOM+form+validation+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+DOM+form+validation+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+DOM+form+validation+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+DOM+form+validation+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>JavaScript DOM Manipulation: Real-World Example with Forms</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Task Objective:</strong> Build a dynamic form validation system using JavaScript DOM manipulation, conditional logic, and loops. The form will collect user data and validate inputs in real-time.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>DOM Manipulation:</strong> Select elements, update content, and respond to user events.</li>\n  <li><strong>Conditional Statements:</strong> Validate form inputs using <code>if/else</code> logic.</li>\n  <li><strong>Looping Statements:</strong> Iterate through form fields to apply validation rules.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<ol>\n  <li>Create an HTML form with fields for name, email, password, and a list of hobbies (checkboxes).</li>\n  <li>Use <code>document.getElementById()</code> and <code>querySelectorAll()</code> to select form elements.</li>\n  <li>Add an event listener for <code>submit</code> to prevent default form submission.</li>\n  <li>Write a function to validate each field using conditionals:</li>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Name must not be empty.</li>\n    <li>Email must contain an <code>@</code> symbol.</li>\n    <li>Password must be at least 8 characters.</li>\n    <li>At least one hobby checkbox must be selected.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <li>Use a <code>for...of</code> loop to iterate through checkboxes and check selections.</li>\n  <li>Display error messages dynamically using <code>textContent</code> or <code>innerHTML</code>.</li>\n  <li>Log valid form data to the console using <code>JSON.stringify()</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Example Code</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;form id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"userForm\"</span>>\n  &lt;label&gt;Name: &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"text\"</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"name\"</span>&gt;&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;p id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"nameError\"</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"error\"</span>&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;label&gt;Email: &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"email\"</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"email\"</span>&gt;&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;p id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"emailError\"</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"error\"</span>&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;label&gt;Password: &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"password\"</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"password\"</span>&gt;&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;p id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"passwordError\"</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"error\"</span>&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;label&gt;Hobbies:\n    &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"checkbox\"</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"hobby\"</span> value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Reading\"</span>> Reading\n    &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"checkbox\"</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"hobby\"</span> value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Gaming\"</span>> Gaming\n    &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"checkbox\"</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"hobby\"</span> value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Sports\"</span>> Sports\n  &lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;p id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"hobbyError\"</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"error\"</span>&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;button <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"submit\"</span>>Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> form = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'userForm\'</span>);\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> hobbies = document.querySelectorAll(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'.hobby\'</span>);\n\n  form.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'submit\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(e) {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">true</span>;\n\n    <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Validate name</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> name = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'name\'</span>).value;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (name.trim() === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>) {\n      document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'nameError\'</span>).textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Name is required\'</span>;\n      isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n    }\n\n    <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Validate email</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> email = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'email\'</span>).value;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (!email.includes(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@\'</span>)) {\n      document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'emailError\'</span>).textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Valid email required\'</span>;\n      isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n    }\n\n    <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Validate password</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> password = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'password\'</span>).value;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (password.length < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">8</span>) {\n      document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'passwordError\'</span>).textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Password must be 8+ characters\'</span>;\n      isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n    }\n\n    <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Validate hobbies</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> hobbySelected = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> hobby of hobbies) {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (hobby.checked) {\n        hobbySelected = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">true</span>;\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">break</span>;\n      }\n    }\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (!hobbySelected) {\n      document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'hobbyError\'</span>).textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Select at least one hobby\'</span>;\n      isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n    }\n\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (isValid) {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> formData = {\n        name, \n        email, \n        password, \n        hobbies: Array.<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span>(hobbies).filter(h => h.checked).map(h => h.value)\n      };\n      console.log(JSON.stringify(formData, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">null</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>));\n    }\n  });\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n\n<p>Submit a single HTML file containing:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>A fully functional form with real-time validation</li>\n  <li>JavaScript that prevents invalid submissions</li>\n  <li>Console output of valid form data in JSON format</li>\n  <li>Clear error messages for each validation rule</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to debug validation logic</li>\n  <li>Test each validation rule independently</li>\n  <li>Use <code>textContent</code> instead of <code>innerHTML</code> for security</li>\n  <li>Add CSS to highlight invalid fields (optional)</li>\n</ul>', 'JavaScript DOM Manipulation: Real-World Example with Forms', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(717, 730, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript event handling diagram</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+event+handling+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+event+handling+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+event+handling+diagram/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+event+handling+diagram/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+event+handling+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>By the end of this task, you will understand how to handle user interactions on a webpage using JavaScript. You will learn to manipulate the DOM (Document Object Model) and respond to events like clicks, key presses, and form submissions.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li>Basic HTML structure and elements</li><li>JavaScript fundamentals (variables, functions)</li><li>Understanding of the DOM tree</li><li>Event types and their lifecycle</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><ol><li><strong>Create an HTML file</strong> with buttons, text fields, and a paragraph element.<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;html&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;&lt;title&gt;Event Handling&lt;/title&gt;&lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;button id=\"clickBtn<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;Click Me&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;p id=\"output&quot;</span>&gt;Output here&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;script src=\"script.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre></li>\n\n<li><strong>Add JavaScript to handle a click event</strong>. Use <code>addEventListener</code> to detect button clicks.<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"clickBtn\"</span>).addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"click\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n  document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"output\"</span>).textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Button clicked!\"</span>;\n});</code></pre></li>\n\n<li><strong>Experiment with other events</strong> like <code>mouseover</code> and <code>keydown</code>.<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"keydown\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(event) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (event.key === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Enter\"</span>) {\n    alert(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"You pressed Enter!\"</span>);\n  }\n});</code></pre></li>\n\n<li><strong>Prevent default actions</strong> using <code>event.preventDefault()</code>.<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.querySelector(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"form\"</span>).addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"submit\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(event) {\n  event.preventDefault();\n  alert(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Form submission blocked!\"</span>);\n});</code></pre></li>\n\n<li><strong>Remove event listeners</strong> dynamically.<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> handleClick() {\n  console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Single click\"</span>);\n}\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> btn = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"clickBtn\"</span>);\nbtn.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"click\"</span>, handleClick);\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Later remove it:</span>\nbtn.removeEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"click\"</span>, handleClick);</code></pre></li></ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a single HTML file that demonstrates all the following:<ul><li>A button that changes text when clicked</li><li>A keydown event that logs the pressed key</li><li>A form with prevented default submission</li></ul></p>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to debug event triggers</li><li>Test events in multiple browsers (Chrome/Firefox)</li><li>Use <code>event.target</code> to access the element that triggered the event</li></ul>', 'JavaScript Event Handling', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(718, 731, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: javascript event handling</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=javascript+event+handling\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/javascript+event+handling\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/javascript+event+handling/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/javascript+event+handling/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=javascript+event+handling\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>JavaScript Event Handling: Real-World Examples</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, we will explore JavaScript event handling and its real-world applications. We will cover the basics of event handling, event types, and how to handle events in a JavaScript application.</p>\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>JavaScript</li>\n  <li>DOM (Document Object Model)</li>\n  <li>Events</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li>Create an HTML file called `index.html` and add the following code:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;JavaScript Event Handling&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;JavaScript Event Handling&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> a paragraph that will be used <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">as</span> an example.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;button&gt;Click me&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;script src=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;script.js&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n  <li>Create a JavaScript file called `script.js` and add the following code:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;DOMContentLoaded&#x27;, function() {</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> button = document.querySelector(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;button&#x27;);</span>\n  button.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;click&#x27;, function() {</span>\n    alert(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;Button clicked!&#x27;);</span>\n  });\n});</code></pre>\n  <li>Open the `index.html` file in a web browser and click on the button. You should see an alert box with the message \"Button clicked!\". This is an example of event handling in JavaScript.</li>\n  <li>Now, let\'s add an event listener to the paragraph. Add the following code to the `script.js` file:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> paragraph = document.querySelector(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;p&#x27;);</span>\nparagraph.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;mouseover&#x27;, function() {</span>\n  paragraph.style.backgroundColor = &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;yellow&#x27;;</span>\n});</code></pre>\n  <li>Save the `script.js` file and refresh the web page. Move your mouse over the paragraph. The background color of the paragraph should change to yellow.</li>\n  <li>Next, let\'s add an event listener to the button to change its text when it\'s clicked. Add the following code to the `script.js` file:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">button.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;click&#x27;, function() {</span>\n  button.textContent = &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;Button clicked again!&#x27;;</span>\n});</code></pre>\n  <li>Save the `script.js` file and refresh the web page. Click on the button. The text of the button should change to \"Button clicked again!\"</li>\n  <li>Finally, let\'s add an event listener to the document to handle a custom event. Add the following code to the `script.js` file:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;customEvent&#x27;, function(event) {</span>\n  alert(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;Custom event received!&#x27;);</span>\n});</code></pre>\n  <li>Save the `script.js` file and refresh the web page. Create a custom event using the following code:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.dispatchEvent(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> CustomEvent(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;customEvent&#x27;));</span></code></pre>\n  <li>Save the `script.js` file and refresh the web page. You should see an alert box with the message \"Custom event received!\"</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>You should have a working HTML file (`index.html`) and a JavaScript file (`script.js`) that demonstrates event handling in JavaScript.</p>\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>Make sure to save the `script.js` file before refreshing the web page.</li>\n  <li>Use the browser\'s developer tools to inspect the HTML and JavaScript code.</li>\n  <li>Experiment with different event types and event listeners to learn more about event handling in JavaScript.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>What is the difference between `addEventListener` and `attachEvent`?</li>\n  <li>How do you create a custom event in JavaScript?</li>\n  <li>What is the purpose of the `event` object in event handling?</li>\n</ul>\n', 'JavaScript Event Handling: Real-World Examples', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(719, 732, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: short search query</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>JavaScript Forms: Handling User Input</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, we will explore how to handle user input using JavaScript. We will create a simple form and use JavaScript to validate and display the input values.</p>\n<h3>Concepts You Need:</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>HTML Forms</li>\n    <li>JavaScript Event Listeners</li>\n    <li>DOM Manipulation</li>\n    <li>Form Validation</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions:</h3>\n<ol>\n    <li>Create an HTML file and add the following code:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;en&quot;</span>&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;UTF-8&quot;</span>&gt;\n    &lt;meta name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;viewport&quot;</span> content=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;</span>&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;JavaScript Forms&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Form Example&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;form id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;myForm&quot;</span>&gt;\n        &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;name&quot;</span>&gt;Name:&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;text&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;name&quot;</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;name&quot;</span> /&gt;\n        &lt;br /&gt;\n        &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span>&gt;Email:&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span> /&gt;\n        &lt;br /&gt;\n        &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;message&quot;</span>&gt;Message:&lt;/label&gt;\n        &lt;textarea id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;message&quot;</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;message&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;\n        &lt;br /&gt;\n        &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submit&quot;</span> value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Submit&quot;</span> /&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n    &lt;div id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;output&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n    <li>Open the HTML file in a web browser and fill out the form.</li>\n    <li>Use the following JavaScript code to handle the form submission:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> form = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;myForm&#39;);</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> output = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;output&#39;);</span>\n\n    form.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;submit&#39;, (e) =&gt; {</span>\n        e.preventDefault();\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> name = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;name&#39;).value;</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> email = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;email&#39;).value;</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> message = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;message&#39;).value;</span>\n\n        output.innerHTML = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Name: ${name}<br>Email: ${email}<br>Message: ${message}`</span>;\n    });\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>\n    <li>Run the JavaScript code by pressing F12 and selecting the console tab in your web browser.</li>\n    <li>Fill out the form and submit it. The output should display the input values in the div with the id &quot;output&quot;.</li>\n    <li>Quiz:</li>\n    <ul>\n        <li>What is the purpose of the `preventDefault()` method in the JavaScript code?</li>\n        <li>How can you modify the JavaScript code to display the input values in a more visually appealing way?</li>\n    </ul>\n</ol>\n<h3>Deliverable:</h3>\n<p>Complete the JavaScript code to handle the form submission and display the input values in a div with the id &quot;output&quot;.</p>\n<h3>Tips:</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>Use the `addEventListener()` method to attach an event listener to the form submission event.</li>\n    <li>Use the `preventDefault()` method to prevent the default form submission behavior.</li>\n    <li>Use the `innerHTML` property to set the content of the div with the id &quot;output&quot;.</li>\n    <li>Use the `value` property to get the input values from the form fields.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Quiz Answers:</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>The purpose of the `preventDefault()` method is to prevent the default form submission behavior and allow the JavaScript code to handle the form submission.</li>\n    <li>You can modify the JavaScript code to display the input values in a more visually appealing way by using HTML elements such as `h2`, `p`, and `ul` to format the output.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Search Query:</h3>\n<p>short search query: &quot;JavaScript forms handling user input&quot;</p>\n', 'JavaScript Forms: Handling User Input', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(720, 733, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: form validation error handling</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=form+validation+error+handling\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/form+validation+error+handling\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/form+validation+error+handling/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/form+validation+error+handling/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=form+validation+error+handling\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>JavaScript Forms: Validation and Error Handling</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, you will learn how to create a simple form using HTML and validate it using JavaScript. You will also learn how to handle errors and provide feedback to the user.</p>\n<h4>Concepts You Need</h4>\n<ul>\n  <li>HTML forms</li>\n  <li>JavaScript event listeners</li>\n  <li>Regular expressions</li>\n  <li>Error handling</li>\n  <li>Form validation</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Step-by-Step Instructions</h4>\n<h5>Step 1: Create the HTML Form</h5>\n<p>Create an HTML file and add the following code:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Form Validation&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Form Validation&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;form id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;myForm&quot;</span>&gt;\n      &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;username&quot;</span>&gt;Username&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;text&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;username&quot;</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;username&quot;</span> /&gt;\n      &lt;span id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;usernameError&quot;</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;error&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span>&gt;Email&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span> /&gt;\n      &lt;span id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;emailError&quot;</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;error&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;password&quot;</span>&gt;Password&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;password&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;password&quot;</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;password&quot;</span> /&gt;\n      &lt;span id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;passwordError&quot;</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;error&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submit&quot;</span> value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Submit&quot;</span> /&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n    &lt;script src=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;script.js&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n<h5>Step 2: Add JavaScript Event Listener</h5>\n<p>Add the following JavaScript code to the script.js file:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;DOMContentLoaded&#x27;, function() {</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> form = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;myForm&#x27;);</span>\n  form.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;submit&#x27;, function(event) {</span>\n    event.preventDefault();\n    validateForm();\n  });\n});\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> validateForm() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> username = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;username&#x27;).value;</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> email = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;email&#x27;).value;</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> password = document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;password&#x27;).value;</span>\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (username === &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;&#x27;) {</span>\n    document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;usernameError&#x27;).innerHTML = &#x27;Please enter a username&#x27;;</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (!/^[a-zA-Z0-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">9</span>]+$/.test(username)) {\n    document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;usernameError&#x27;).innerHTML = &#x27;Username can only contain letters and numbers&#x27;;</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (email === &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;&#x27;) {</span>\n    document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;emailError&#x27;).innerHTML = &#x27;Please enter an email address&#x27;;</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (!/^[a-zA-Z0-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">9</span>._%+-]+@[a-zA-Z0-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">9</span>.-]+\\.[a-zA-Z]{<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>,}$/.test(email)) {\n    document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;emailError&#x27;).innerHTML = &#x27;Invalid email address&#x27;;</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (password === &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;&#x27;) {</span>\n    document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;passwordError&#x27;).innerHTML = &#x27;Please enter a password&#x27;;</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (password.length < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">8</span>) {\n    document.getElementById(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#x27;passwordError&#x27;).innerHTML = &#x27;Password must be at least 8 characters long&#x27;;</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">true</span>;\n}</code></pre>\n<h5>Step 3: Test the Form</h5>\n<p>Save the HTML and JavaScript files and open the HTML file in a web browser. Test the form by entering different values and submitting it. You should see error messages displayed below each field.</p>\n<h4>Deliverable</h4>\n<p>Copy and paste the HTML and JavaScript code into a new file and submit it as your deliverable.</p>\n<h4>Quiz</h4>\n<p>Test your understanding of form validation and error handling by answering the following questions:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>What is the purpose of the `validateForm()` function?</li>\n  <li>What is the regular expression used to validate the username field?</li>\n  <li>What is the regular expression used to validate the email field?</li>\n  <li>What is the condition used to check if the password is at least 8 characters long?</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Tips</h4>\n<p>Remember to test your form thoroughly to ensure that all fields are validated correctly. You can use tools like the W3C Validator to check for HTML and JavaScript errors. Also, make sure to handle errors in a user-friendly way by displaying clear and concise error messages.</p>\n<h4>Image Query</h4>\n<p>Search for images related to form validation and error handling.</p>\n<h5>Example Search Query:</h5>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">form validation error handling</code></pre>\n<h4>Conclusion</h4>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, you learned how to create a simple form using HTML and validate it using JavaScript. You also learned how to handle errors and provide feedback to the user. Remember to test your form thoroughly and handle errors in a user-friendly way.</p>', 'JavaScript Forms: Validation and Error Handling', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(721, 734, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: responsive web design media queries example</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=responsive+web+design+media+queries+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/responsive+web+design+media+queries+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/responsive+web+design+media+queries+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/responsive+web+design+media+queries+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=responsive+web+design+media+queries+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Today you will learn to implement <strong>responsive web design</strong> using <code>media queries</code>. You will create a simple webpage that adapts its layout based on the screen size of the device viewing it.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> A web design approach ensuring websites render well on all devices (desktops, tablets, mobiles).</li><li><strong>Media Queries:</strong> A CSS technique to apply styles conditionally based on screen characteristics like width.</li><li><strong>Viewport Meta Tag:</strong> Ensures proper scaling on mobile devices.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Create a basic HTML structure with a viewport meta tag.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;meta name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"viewport\"</span> content=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    /* Base styles <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> desktop */\n    body { font-family: Arial; }\n    .container { width: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">80</span>%; margin: auto; }\n    .box { width: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">100</span>%; background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f0f0f0; padding: 20px; }</span>\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=\"container<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=\"box&quot;</span>&gt;This <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> a responsive box&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Add a media query for tablets (max-width: 768px).</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">@media screen <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> (max-width: 768px) {\n  .container { width: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">95</span>%; }\n  .box { background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#d0eaff; }</span>\n}</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Add a media query for mobile phones (max-width: 480px).</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">@media screen <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> (max-width: 480px) {\n  .container { width: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">100</span>%; }\n  .box { font-size: 14px; }\n}</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Test your page by resizing your browser window or using browser developer tools (Ctrl+Shift+M on Windows, Cmd+Option+M on Mac).</p>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a single HTML file demonstrating the three styles applied at different screen sizes. Include comments in your CSS explaining each breakpoint.</p>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>min-width</code> and <code>max-width</code> to define specific ranges.</li><li>Always include the viewport meta tag for mobile compatibility.</li><li>Use browser developer tools to simulate different device sizes.</li></ul>', 'Introduction to Responsive Web Design: Media Queries', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(722, 735, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: mobile-first responsive design example</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=mobile-first+responsive+design+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/mobile-first+responsive+design+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/mobile-first+responsive+design+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/mobile-first+responsive+design+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=mobile-first+responsive+design+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Build a responsive webpage that adapts to mobile and larger screens using mobile-first design principles. You will learn to prioritize mobile layouts, then enhance the design for tablets and desktops using CSS media queries, flexible grids, and responsive images.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Mobile-first approach:</strong> Start with styles for small screens, then add media queries for larger breakpoints.</li><li><strong>Media queries:</strong> Use <code>@media</code> to apply CSS based on screen width.</li><li><strong>Fluid layouts:</strong> Use percentage-based widths or CSS Grid/Flexbox for flexible grids.</li><li><strong>Responsive images:</strong> Use <code>srcset</code> and <code>picture</code> elements for adaptive image loading.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><p><strong>Step 1: Set up your project</strong></p><p>Create an <code>index.html</code> file and a <code>style.css</code> file. Link the CSS in your HTML:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;link rel=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"stylesheet\"</span> href=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"style.css\"</span>&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 2: Write the HTML structure</strong></p><p>Create a simple webpage with a header, navigation, main content, and footer:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;header&gt;&lt;h1&gt;My Responsive Site&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;/header&gt;\n&lt;nav&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Home&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;About&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Contact&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/nav&gt;\n&lt;main&gt;\n  &lt;section&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Welcome&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> a responsive webpage.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/section&gt;\n&lt;/main&gt;\n&lt;footer&gt;&lt;p&gt;© <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2025</span>&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/footer&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 3: Apply mobile-first CSS</strong></p><p>Add base styles for mobile (max-width: 768px):</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">body {\n  margin: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  font-family: sans-serif;\n}\n\nheader {\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#333;</span>\n  color: white;\n  padding: 1rem;\n}\n\nnav {\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f4f4f4;</span>\n}\n\nnav ul {\n  list-style: none;\n  padding: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n}\n\nnav li {\n  padding: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>.5rem;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#ccc;</span>\n}</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 4: Add media queries for tablets</strong></p><p>Create a media query for tablets (min-width: 769px) to switch to a horizontal navigation bar:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">@media (min-width: 769px) {\n  nav ul {\n    flex-direction: row;\n    justify-content: space-around;\n  }\n}</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 5: Add responsive images</strong></p><p>Include an image with <code>srcset</code> to serve different resolutions:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;picture&gt;\n  &lt;source srcset=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"large.jpg\"</span> media=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"(min-width: 1024px)\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;source srcset=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"medium.jpg\"</span> media=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"(min-width: 768px)\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;img src=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"small.jpg\"</span> alt=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Responsive Image\"</span>&gt;\n&lt;/picture&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 6: Test responsiveness</strong></p><p>Use browser developer tools to simulate mobile, tablet, and desktop views. Ensure text resizes, layouts adjust, and images load correctly.</p>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a ZIP file containing your <code>index.html</code> and <code>style.css</code> files. The webpage must:</p><ul><li>Render properly on mobile (max-width: 480px).</li><li>Switch to a tablet layout at 768px.</li><li>Display a desktop layout at 1024px+.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>max-width: 100%</code> for images to prevent overflow on small screens.</li><li>Start with small-screen styles, then progressively enhance for larger screens.</li><li>Test with real devices or browser tools like Chrome DevTools\' device toggle.</li></ul>', 'Responsive Web Design: Mobile-First Design Principles', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(723, 736, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: CSS Grid and Flexbox layout examples</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+examples\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+examples\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+examples/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+examples/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+examples\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Day 42: Introduction to CSS Grid and Flexbox</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Task Objective:</strong> Learn to create responsive layouts using CSS Grid and Flexbox. Build a simple webpage with a navigation bar (Flexbox) and a dashboard layout (Grid).</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Flexbox:</strong> A one-dimensional layout system for aligning items horizontally or vertically.</li>\n  <li><strong>CSS Grid:</strong> A two-dimensional layout system for creating complex grid-based designs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Key Properties:</strong>\n    <ul>\n      <li><code>display: flex</code> / <code>display: grid</code></li>\n      <li><code>justify-content</code>, <code>align-items</code> (Flexbox)</li>\n      <li><code>grid-template-columns</code>, <code>grid-gap</code> (Grid)</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Create HTML Structure:</strong>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;header <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"navbar\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=\"logo<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;MySite&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;nav class=\"links&quot;</span>&gt;\n    &lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#\"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;</span>\n    &lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#\"&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;</span>\n    &lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#\"&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;</span>\n  &lt;/nav&gt;\n&lt;/header&gt;\n\n&lt;main <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=\"dashboard<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;section class=\"sidebar&quot;</span>&gt;Sidebar&lt;/section&gt;\n  &lt;section <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=\"content<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;Main Content&lt;/section&gt;\n  &lt;section class=\"widgets&quot;</span>&gt;Widgets&lt;/section&gt;\n&lt;/main&gt;</code></pre>\n  </li>\n\n  <li><strong>Style Navigation Bar with Flexbox:</strong>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">.navbar {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  align-items: center;\n  padding: 1rem;\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f0f0f0;</span>\n}\n\n.links {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 1rem;\n}\n\n.links a {\n  text-decoration: none;\n  color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#333;</span>\n}</code></pre>\n  </li>\n\n  <li><strong>Create Dashboard Layout with Grid:</strong>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">.dashboard {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr 250px;\n  grid-gap: 1rem;\n  padding: 1rem;\n}\n\n.sidebar {\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#e0e0e0;</span>\n}\n\n.content {\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f8f8f8;</span>\n}\n\n.widgets {\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#d0d0d0;</span>\n}</code></pre>\n  </li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n\n<p>Submit an HTML file with working Flexbox navigation and Grid dashboard. Include comments explaining your layout choices.</p>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Use <code>flex-wrap: wrap</code> for responsive navigation bars.</li>\n  <li>Test grid layouts with <code>grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr))</code> for responsiveness.</li>\n  <li>Use browser developer tools to inspect grid lines and flex item spacing.</li>\n</ul>', 'Introduction to CSS Grid and Flexbox', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(724, 737, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: responsive web design media queries</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=responsive+web+design+media+queries\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/responsive+web+design+media+queries\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/responsive+web+design+media+queries/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/responsive+web+design+media+queries/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=responsive+web+design+media+queries\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3>\n<p>The goal of today’s internship task is to <strong>implement responsive design using CSS media queries</strong>. By the end of the day you should be able to create a simple web page that adapts its layout and styling to different screen sizes, from mobile phones to large desktop monitors. You will learn how to write clean, maintainable CSS that responds to viewport changes, and you will practice the workflow of testing across devices.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Responsive Web Design (RWD)</strong> – the practice of making web content look good on all devices.</li>\n<li><strong>Viewport</strong> – the visible area of a web page on a device.</li>\n<li><strong>Media Queries</strong> – CSS rules that apply only when certain conditions (like screen width) are met.</li>\n<li><strong>Breakpoints</strong> – the specific viewport widths at which the layout changes.</li>\n<li><strong>Flexbox & Grid</strong> – modern CSS layout modules that simplify responsive design.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n<p>Follow these steps to build a responsive page:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Create the HTML skeleton</strong> – start with a basic structure that includes a header, navigation, main content area, and footer.</li>\n<li><strong>Style the page with base CSS</strong> – write styles that work on a typical desktop view.</li>\n<li><strong>Define breakpoints</strong> – decide at which widths you want the layout to change. Common breakpoints are 480px (mobile), 768px (tablet), and 1024px (desktop).</li>\n<li><strong>Write media queries</strong> – add CSS rules inside <code>@media</code> blocks that target each breakpoint.</li>\n<li><strong>Test on multiple devices</strong> – use browser dev tools or real devices to verify that the layout adapts correctly.</li>\n<li><strong>Refine and document</strong> – clean up your CSS, comment the media queries, and prepare a brief report.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Code Example – Basic HTML</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"en\"</span>&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;meta charset=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"UTF-8\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;meta name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"viewport\"</span> content=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Responsive Demo&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;link rel=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"stylesheet\"</span> href=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"styles.css\"</span>&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;header&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;My Responsive Site&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;/header&gt;\n  &lt;nav&gt;\n    &lt;ul&gt;\n      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#\"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#\"&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#\"&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n    &lt;/ul&gt;\n  &lt;/nav&gt;\n  &lt;main&gt;\n    &lt;section&gt;\n      &lt;h2&gt;Welcome&lt;/h2&gt;\n      &lt;p&gt;This <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> a paragraph that will resize based on the viewport.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;/section&gt;\n  &lt;/main&gt;\n  &lt;footer&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;© <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2026</span> My Site&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/footer&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Code Example – Base CSS (Desktop First)</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">body {\n  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n  margin: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  padding: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  line-height: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1.6</span>;\n}\n\nheader, nav, main, footer {\n  padding: 1rem;\n}\n\nnav ul {\n  list-style: none;\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 1rem;\n}\n\nnav a {\n  text-decoration: none;\n  color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#333;</span>\n}\n\n/* Layout <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">using</span> Flexbox */\nmain {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: row;\n  gap: 2rem;\n}\n\nsection {\n  flex: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>;\n}\n\naside {\n  flex: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>;\n}\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Code Example – Media Queries</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">@media (max-width: 1024px) {\n  /* Tablet view: stack main content */\n  main {\n    flex-direction: column;\n  }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n  /* Small tablet / large phone */\n  nav ul {\n    flex-direction: column;\n  }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n  /* Mobile view: reduce padding */\n  header, nav, main, footer {\n    padding: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>.5rem;\n  }\n\n  nav a {\n    font-size: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>.9rem;\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Your final deliverable is a zipped folder containing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>index.html</code> – the HTML page.</li>\n<li><code>styles.css</code> – the CSS with media queries.</li>\n<li><code>README.md</code> – a short explanation of the breakpoints you chose and why.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Use the mobile-first approach</strong> – write base styles for the smallest screen, then add media queries for larger screens. This keeps the CSS lean.</li>\n<li><strong>Test often</strong> – use the browser’s device toolbar (Ctrl+Shift+M in Chrome) to simulate different widths.</li>\n<li><strong>Keep breakpoints logical</strong> – align them with content needs, not just arbitrary numbers.</li>\n<li><strong>Comment your media queries</strong> – add a brief note before each block so future developers know its purpose.</li>\n<li><strong>Leverage Flexbox/Grid</strong> – they automatically adjust spacing, reducing the need for many width-specific rules.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'Responsive Web Design: Implementing Media Queries', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(725, 738, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: css grid layout</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=css+grid+layout\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/css+grid+layout\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/css+grid+layout/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/css+grid+layout/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=css+grid+layout\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h2>CSS Grid: Building a Grid Layout</h2>\n\n<p>In this hands-on internship, you will learn how to create a grid layout using CSS Grid. Grid layout is a powerful layout system that allows you to create complex and responsive layouts with ease.</p>\n\n<h3>Task Objective</h3>\n\n<p>The objective of this task is to create a grid layout that displays a list of items in a responsive and visually appealing way. You will learn how to use CSS Grid to create a grid container, define grid items, and use grid properties to control the layout.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n\n<ul>\n    <li>CSS Grid</li>\n    <li>Grid Container</li>\n    <li>Grid Items</li>\n    <li>Grid Properties</li>\n    <li>Responsive Design</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<ol>\n    <li><strong>Create an HTML File</strong>: Create a new HTML file and add the following code:</pre><code>&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;CSS Grid Example&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;grid-container&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;Item 1&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;Item 2&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;Item 3&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;Item 4&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;Item 5&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre></li>\n    <li><strong>Add CSS Grid Styles</strong>: Add the following CSS code to your HTML file:</pre><code>&lt;style&gt;\n.grid-container {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);\n    grid-gap: 10px;\n}\n\n.grid-item {\n    background-color: #f0f0f0;\n    padding: 20px;\n    border: 1px solid #ddd;\n}\n\n.grid-item:hover {\n    background-color: #ccc;\n}\n&lt;/style&gt;</code></pre></li>\n    <li><strong>Define Grid Items</strong>: Define the grid items by adding the following code:</pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;&lt;code&gt;Item 1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This is item 1.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;&lt;code&gt;Item 2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This is item 2.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;&lt;code&gt;Item 3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This is item 3.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;&lt;code&gt;Item 4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This is item 4.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;&lt;code&gt;Item 5&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This is item 5.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre></li>\n    <li><strong>Make it Responsive</strong>: Make the grid layout responsive by adding the following code:</pre><code>&lt;style&gt;\n@media only screen and (max-width: 600px) {\n    .grid-container {\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(1, 1fr);\n    }\n}\n&lt;/style&gt;</code></pre></li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n\n<p>Deliver a working HTML file that displays a grid layout with 5 items. The grid layout should be responsive and visually appealing.</p>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n\n<ul>\n    <li>Use the CSS Grid properties to control the layout of your grid items.</li>\n    <li>Use the grid-template-columns property to define the number of columns in your grid.</li>\n    <li>Use the grid-gap property to add space between grid items.</li>\n    <li>Use the @media query to make your grid layout responsive.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n\n<p>Quiz: What is the purpose of the grid-gap property in CSS Grid?</p>\n\n<ul>\n    <li>To define the number of columns in a grid.</li>\n    <li>To add space between grid items.</li>\n    <li>To define the width of a grid item.</li>\n    <li>To define the height of a grid item.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Answer: <strong>2. To add space between grid items.</strong></p>\n\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n\n<p>Image Query: <code>css grid layout</code></p>\n\n<h3>Code Snippet</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;grid-container&quot;</span>&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;grid-item&quot;</span>&gt;Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;grid-item&quot;</span>&gt;Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;grid-item&quot;</span>&gt;Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;grid-item&quot;</span>&gt;Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;grid-item&quot;</span>&gt;Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Code Explanation</h3>\n\n<p>This code snippet defines a grid container with 5 grid items. The grid items are defined using the grid-item class, which adds a background color, padding, and border to each item.</p>\n\n<h3>Code Solution</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;style&gt;\n.grid-container {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>, 1fr);\n    grid-gap: 10px;\n}\n\n.grid-item {\n    background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f0f0f0;</span>\n    padding: 20px;\n    border: 1px solid <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#ddd;</span>\n}\n\n.grid-item:hover {\n    background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#ccc;</span>\n}\n&lt;/style&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>This code solution defines the CSS styles for the grid container and grid items. The grid-template-columns property defines the number of columns in the grid, and the grid-gap property adds space between grid items.</p>\n\n<h3>Code Discussion</h3>\n\n<p>This code discussion explains the purpose of the code solution and how it achieves the desired outcome. It also provides tips and best practices for using CSS Grid in your projects.</p>', 'CSS Grid: Building a Grid Layout', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(726, 739, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: flexbox layout</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=flexbox+layout\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/flexbox+layout\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/flexbox+layout/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/flexbox+layout/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=flexbox+layout\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Flexbox: Creating a Flexible Layout</h3>\n\n<p>Today, we will be learning about Flexbox, a powerful layout system in CSS that allows us to create flexible and responsive layouts. Flexbox is a game-changer for web developers, and it\'s essential to understand how it works.</p>\n\n<h3>What is Flexbox?</h3>\n\n<p>Flexbox is a one-dimensional layout system that allows us to create flexible and responsive layouts. It\'s designed to be used on the web, and it\'s supported by all modern browsers. Flexbox is based on a flexible container and its items, which can be laid out in a flexible way.</p>\n\n<h3>Key Concepts</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Flex Container</strong>: The parent element that contains the flexible items. It\'s the element that we apply the flexbox styles to.</li>\n  <li><strong>Flex Items</strong>: The child elements that are contained within the flex container. They can be laid out in a flexible way.</li>\n  <li><strong>Flex Direction</strong>: The direction in which the flex items are laid out. It can be row or column.</li>\n  <li><strong>Flex Wrap</strong>: Whether the flex items should wrap to a new line or not.</li>\n  <li><strong>Flex Grow</strong> and <strong>Flex Shrink</strong>: How the flex items should grow or shrink to fill the available space.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>HTML Structure</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-container&quot;</span>&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>CSS Styles</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">.flex-container {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: row;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n\n.flex-item {\n  width: 200px;\n  height: 100px;\n  background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f0f0f0;</span>\n  margin: 10px;\n  padding: 20px;\n  border: 1px solid <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#ddd;</span>\n}\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<ol>\n  <li>Create an HTML file and add the flex container and items.</li>\n  <li>Add the CSS styles to the flex container and items.</li>\n  <li>Experiment with different flex direction, wrap, grow, and shrink properties.</li>\n  <li>Test the layout on different screen sizes and devices.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n\n<p>By the end of this task, you should have a basic understanding of Flexbox and how to create a flexible layout using CSS. You should also have a working example of a flexbox layout that you can test and experiment with.</p>\n\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">quiz: [\n  {\n    question: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is Flexbox?\"</span>,\n    options: [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A CSS layout system\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A JavaScript library\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A HTML element\"</span>],\n    answer: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A CSS layout system\"</span>\n  },\n  {\n    question: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the purpose of the flex container?\"</span>,\n    options: [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To contain the flex items\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To style the flex items\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To layout the flex items\"</span>],\n    answer: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To contain the flex items\"</span>\n  },\n  {\n    question: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the default value of the flex direction property?\"</span>,\n    options: [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Row\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Column\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Row or Column\"</span>],\n    answer: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Row\"</span>\n  }\n]\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n\n<p>Search for \"flexbox layout\" on Google to see examples of flexbox layouts in action.</p>\n\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n\n<p>In this task, we learned about Flexbox, a powerful layout system in CSS that allows us to create flexible and responsive layouts. We covered the key concepts of Flexbox, including the flex container, flex items, flex direction, flex wrap, flex grow, and flex shrink. We also created a basic example of a flexbox layout and experimented with different properties to see how they affect the layout.</p>\n\n<h3>Next Steps</h3>\n\n<p>Now that you have a basic understanding of Flexbox, you can continue to experiment with different properties and layouts to create more complex and responsive designs. You can also use Flexbox to create layouts for mobile devices, tablets, and desktops.</p>\n\n<h3>Additional Resources</h3>\n\n<p>Check out the following resources for more information on Flexbox:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_Flexible_Box_Layout\">MDN Web Docs: CSS Flexible Box Layout</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"https://css-tricks.com/snippets/css/a-guide-to-flexbox/\">CSS-Tricks: A Guide to Flexbox</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"https://flexboxfroggy.com/\">Flexbox Froggy: A game to help you learn Flexbox</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Final Thoughts</h3>\n\n<p>Flexbox is a powerful tool that can help you create flexible and responsive layouts. With practice and experimentation, you can master Flexbox and create complex and beautiful designs. Remember to always test your layouts on different screen sizes and devices to ensure that they work as expected.</p>\n\n<h3>Code Example</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-container&quot;</span>&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;style&gt;\n  .flex-container {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: row;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    align-items: center;\n  }\n\n  .flex-item {\n    width: 200px;\n    height: 100px;\n    background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f0f0f0;</span>\n    margin: 10px;\n    padding: 20px;\n    border: 1px solid <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#ddd;</span>\n  }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>HTML Structure</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-container&quot;</span>&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;flex-item&quot;</span>&gt;Flex Item <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>CSS Styles</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">.flex-container {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: row;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n\n.flex-item {\n  width: 200px;\n  height: 100px;\n  background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f0f0f0;</span>\n  margin: 10px;\n  padding: 20px;\n  border: 1px solid <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#ddd;</span>\n}\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">quiz: [\n  {\n    question: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is Flexbox?\"</span>,\n    options: [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A CSS layout system\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A JavaScript library\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A HTML element\"</span>],\n    answer: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A CSS layout system\"</span>\n  },\n  {\n    question: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the purpose of the flex container?\"</span>,\n    options: [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To contain the flex items\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To style the flex items\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To layout the flex items\"</span>],\n    answer: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To contain the flex items\"</span>\n  },\n  {\n    question: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the default value of the flex direction property?\"</span>,\n    options: [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Row\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Column\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Row or Column\"</span>],\n    answer: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Row\"</span>\n  }\n]\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n\n<p>Search for \"flexbox layout\" on Google to see examples of flexbox layouts in action.</p>\n\n<p>This is the end of the task. Please submit your work and any questions you may have.</p>\n\n', 'Flexbox: Creating a Flexible Layout', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(727, 740, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: responsive web design screen sizes</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=responsive+web+design+screen+sizes\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/responsive+web+design+screen+sizes\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/responsive+web+design+screen+sizes/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/responsive+web+design+screen+sizes/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=responsive+web+design+screen+sizes\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Responsive Web Design: Adapting to Different Screen Sizes</h3>\n<p>In this task, you will learn how to create a responsive web design that adapts to different screen sizes using CSS. Responsive web design is an approach to web development that focuses on creating a website that looks great on all devices, from desktop computers to mobile phones.</p>\n<h3>Screen Sizes</h3>\n<p>There are several screen sizes that you need to consider when designing a responsive website. These include:</p>\n<ul>\n    <li>Desktop: 1024px or larger</li>\n    <li>Tablet: 768px to 1023px</li>\n    <li>Mobile: 768px or smaller</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>CSS</h3>\n<p>CSS is used to add styles to your HTML elements. To create a responsive web design, you can use CSS media queries to target specific screen sizes. Here is an example of how you can use CSS media queries:</pre><code>/* Desktop screen size */</code><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n    /* styles <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> desktop screen size */\n    body {\n        background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f2f2f2;</span>\n    }\n    h1 {\n        font-size: 36px;\n    }\n}\n\n/* Tablet screen size */\n@media (min-width: 768px) <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> (max-width: 1023px) {\n    /* styles <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> tablet screen size */\n    body {\n        background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#ccc;</span>\n    }\n    h1 {\n        font-size: 24px;\n    }\n}\n\n/* Mobile screen size */\n@media (max-width: 767px) {\n    /* styles <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> mobile screen size */\n    body {\n        background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#aaa;</span>\n    }\n    h1 {\n        font-size: 18px;\n    }\n}</code></pre><p>This code uses CSS media queries to target specific screen sizes. The @media rule is used to define the media query, and the (min-width) and (max-width) properties are used to specify the screen size range.</p>\n<h3>HTML</h3>\n<p>Here is an example of how you can use HTML to create a responsive web design:</pre><code>&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Responsive Web Design&lt;/title&gt;\n    &lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;style.css&quot;&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;Responsive Web Design&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This is a responsive web design example.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;ul&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Desktop&lt;/li&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Tablet&lt;/li&gt;\n        &lt;li&gt;Mobile&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre><p>This code uses HTML to create a basic web page with a title, heading, paragraph, and unordered list. The link to the CSS file is included in the head section.</p>\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Your deliverable for this task is to create a responsive web design that adapts to different screen sizes using CSS. You should include the following features:</p>\n<ul>\n    <li>A CSS file that uses media queries to target specific screen sizes</li>\n    <li>An HTML file that includes a link to the CSS file and uses HTML elements to create a responsive web design</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<p>What is the purpose of CSS media queries in responsive web design?</p>\n<ul>\n    <li>To target specific screen sizes</li>\n    <li>To apply styles to all screen sizes</li>\n    <li>To create a fixed layout</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Answer: <strong>To target specific screen sizes</strong></p>\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n<p>Search for images related to responsive web design and screen sizes.</p>\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n<p>In this task, you learned how to create a responsive web design that adapts to different screen sizes using CSS. You also learned how to use CSS media queries to target specific screen sizes. Remember to include a link to your CSS file in your HTML file and use HTML elements to create a responsive web design.</p>\n<p>Quiz: [{}]\nImage Query: responsive web design screen sizes</p>\n', 'Responsive Web Design: Adapting to Different Screen Sizes', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(728, 741, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: css grid flexbox comparison</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=css+grid+flexbox+comparison\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/css+grid+flexbox+comparison\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/css+grid+flexbox+comparison/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/css+grid+flexbox+comparison/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=css+grid+flexbox+comparison\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective:</h3>\n<p>In this task, you will gain hands-on experience with CSS Grid and Flexbox, two powerful layout systems in CSS. You will learn how to create complex layouts using these systems and compare their features.</p>\n<h3>Concepts You Need:</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>CSS Grid</li>\n    <li>Flexbox</li>\n    <li>Layout systems</li>\n    <li>CSS</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions:</h3>\n<ol>\n    <li>Create an HTML file named <code>index.html</code> and add the following code:</pre><code>&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;CSS Grid and Flexbox Comparison&lt;/title&gt;\n    &lt;style&gt;\n        /* Import necessary CSS files */\n        @import url(&#39;https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Open+Sans:wght@400;600;700&display=swap&#39;);\n        @import url(&#39;https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Raleway:wght@400;600;700&display=swap&#39;);\n    &lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;CSS Grid and Flexbox Comparison&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;grid-container&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;\n            &lt;h2&gt;CSS Grid&lt;/h2&gt;\n            &lt;p&gt;CSS Grid is a two-dimensional layout system that allows you to create complex layouts using rows and columns.&lt;/p&gt;\n            &lt;ul&gt;\n                &lt;li&gt;Grid is a powerful tool for creating complex layouts.&lt;/li&gt;\n                &lt;li&gt;Grid is supported by most modern browsers.&lt;/li&gt;\n            &lt;/ul&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;grid-item&quot;&gt;\n            &lt;h2&gt;Flexbox&lt;/h2&gt;\n            &lt;p&gt;Flexbox is a one-dimensional layout system that allows you to create flexible layouts using flex containers and flex items.&lt;/p&gt;\n            &lt;ul&gt;\n                &lt;li&gt;Flexbox is a powerful tool for creating flexible layouts.&lt;/li&gt;\n                &lt;li&gt;Flexbox is supported by most modern browsers.&lt;/li&gt;\n            &lt;/ul&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;flex-container&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;flex-item&quot;&gt;\n            &lt;h2&gt;CSS Grid&lt;/h2&gt;\n            &lt;p&gt;CSS Grid is a two-dimensional layout system that allows you to create complex layouts using rows and columns.&lt;/p&gt;\n            &lt;ul&gt;\n                &lt;li&gt;Grid is a powerful tool for creating complex layouts.&lt;/li&gt;\n                &lt;li&gt;Grid is supported by most modern browsers.&lt;/li&gt;\n            &lt;/ul&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;flex-item&quot;&gt;\n            &lt;h2&gt;Flexbox&lt;/h2&gt;\n            &lt;p&gt;Flexbox is a one-dimensional layout system that allows you to create flexible layouts using flex containers and flex items.&lt;/p&gt;\n            &lt;ul&gt;\n                &lt;li&gt;Flexbox is a powerful tool for creating flexible layouts.&lt;/li&gt;\n                &lt;li&gt;Flexbox is supported by most modern browsers.&lt;/li&gt;\n            &lt;/ul&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code>&lt;/pre&gt;\n    <li>Add the following CSS code to the <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block:</pre><code>&lt;style&gt;\n    /* Grid styles */\n    .grid-container {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);\n        grid-gap: 20px;\n    }\n    .grid-item {\n        background-color: #f0f0f0;\n        padding: 20px;\n    }\n    /* Flexbox styles */\n    .flex-container {\n        display: flex;\n        flex-direction: row;\n        justify-content: space-between;\n        align-items: center;\n    }\n    .flex-item {\n        background-color: #f0f0f0;\n        padding: 20px;\n        width: 45%;\n    }\n&lt;/style&gt;</code>&lt;/pre&gt;\n    <li>Open the <code>index.html</code> file in a web browser to see the comparison of CSS Grid and Flexbox.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Deliverable:</h3>\n<p>Complete the task by creating the HTML and CSS files as described above.</p>\n<h3>Tips:</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>Make sure to test the layout in different browsers to ensure compatibility.</li>\n    <li>Experiment with different grid and flexbox properties to create different layouts.</li>\n    <li>Use the developer tools in your web browser to inspect the layout and identify areas for improvement.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Quiz:</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>What is the main difference between CSS Grid and Flexbox?</li>\n    <li>Which layout system is more suitable for creating complex layouts?</li>\n    <li>How do you create a grid container using CSS Grid?</li>\n    <li>How do you create a flex container using Flexbox?</li>\n</ul>', 'CSS Grid and Flexbox: Comparing Layout Systems', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(729, 742, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: responsive images</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=responsive+images\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/responsive+images\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/responsive+images/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/responsive+images/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=responsive+images\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><!DOCTYPE html>...</html>', 'Best Practices for Responsive Web Design', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
