(730, 743, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: mobile-first design responsive web design css media queries</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=mobile-first+design+responsive+web+design+css+media+queries\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/mobile-first+design+responsive+web+design+css+media+queries\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/mobile-first+design+responsive+web+design+css+media+queries/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/mobile-first+design+responsive+web+design+css+media+queries/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=mobile-first+design+responsive+web+design+css+media+queries\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Implementing Mobile-First Design Principles</h3>\n  <p>Mobile-first design is an approach to web development where we design and develop the website for mobile devices first, and then scale up to larger screens.</p>\n  <p>This approach has several benefits, including:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Improved user experience on smaller screens</li>\n    <li>Reduced development time and costs</li>\n    <li>Increased flexibility and scalability</li>\n  </ul>\n  <h3>Responsive Web Design</h3>\n  <p>Responsive web design is a key concept in mobile-first design. It involves using CSS media queries to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type.</p>\n  <p>Here is an example of a basic responsive design using CSS media queries:</p>\n  <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n    &lt;style&gt;\n      /* Default styles <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> all devices */\n      body {\n        font-size: 16px;\n        line-height: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1.5</span>;\n      }\n      \n      /* Media query <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> small screens (mobile devices) */\n      @media only screen <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> (max-width: 768px) {\n        body {\n          font-size: 14px;\n          line-height: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1.2</span>;\n        }\n      }\n      \n      /* Media query <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> medium screens (tablets) */\n      @media only screen <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> (min-width: 769px) <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> (max-width: 1024px) {\n        body {\n          font-size: 16px;\n          line-height: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1.5</span>;\n        }\n      }\n      \n      /* Media query <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> large screens (desktop devices) */\n      @media only screen <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> (min-width: 1025px) {\n        body {\n          font-size: 18px;\n          line-height: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1.7</span>;\n        }\n      }\n    &lt;/style&gt;\n  </code></pre>\n  <h3>Implementing Mobile-First Design</h3>\n  <p>To implement mobile-first design, we need to follow these steps:</p>\n  <ol>\n    <li>Design the website for mobile devices first</li>\n    <li>Use CSS media queries to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type</li>\n    <li>Use responsive images and videos to ensure that they are displayed correctly on different devices</li>\n    <li>Test the website on different devices and screen sizes to ensure that it is responsive and user-friendly</li>\n  </ol>\n  <p>Here is an example of a basic HTML structure for a mobile-first design:</p>\n  <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n    &lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n    &lt;html&gt;\n      &lt;head&gt;\n        &lt;title&gt;Mobile-First Design&lt;/title&gt;\n        &lt;style&gt;\n          /* Default styles <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> all devices */\n          body {\n            font-size: 16px;\n            line-height: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1.5</span>;\n          }\n          \n          /* Media query <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> small screens (mobile devices) */\n          @media only screen <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> (max-width: 768px) {\n            body {\n              font-size: 14px;\n              line-height: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1.2</span>;\n            }\n          }\n        &lt;/style&gt;\n      &lt;/head&gt;\n      &lt;body&gt;\n        &lt;h1&gt;Mobile-First Design&lt;/h1&gt;\n        &lt;p&gt;This <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> a basic example of a mobile-first design.&lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;/body&gt;\n    &lt;/html&gt;\n  </code></pre>\n  <h3>Quiz</h3>\n  <p>Test your knowledge of mobile-first design and responsive web design with the following quiz:</p>\n  <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">var</span> quiz = [\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is mobile-first design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A Designing for desktop devices first\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B Designing for mobile devices first\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C Designing for tablets first\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D Designing for laptops first\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Mobile-first design is an approach to web development where we design and develop the website for mobile devices first, and then scale up to larger screens.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is responsive web design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A A design approach that only works on desktop devices\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B A design approach that works on all devices and screen sizes\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C A design approach that uses CSS media queries to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D A design approach that uses JavaScript to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Responsive web design is a key concept in mobile-first design. It involves using CSS media queries to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the purpose of using CSS media queries in mobile-first design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A To apply different styles based on the screen size and device type\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B To apply the same styles on all devices and screen sizes\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C To use JavaScript to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D To use HTML to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"CSS media queries are used to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type in mobile-first design.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the benefit of using mobile-first design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A Reduced development time and costs\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B Increased development time and costs\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C Improved user experience on smaller screens\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D Decreased user experience on smaller screens\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Mobile-first design has several benefits, including reduced development time and costs, improved user experience on smaller screens, and increased flexibility and scalability.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the benefit of using responsive web design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A Improved user experience on smaller screens\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B Decreased user experience on smaller screens\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C Increased development time and costs\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D Reduced development time and costs\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Responsive web design has several benefits, including improved user experience on smaller screens, reduced development time and costs, and increased flexibility and scalability.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the purpose of using responsive images and videos in mobile-first design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A To ensure that they are displayed correctly on different devices\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B To ensure that they are displayed incorrectly on different devices\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C To use JavaScript to display them correctly on different devices\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D To use HTML to display them correctly on different devices\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Responsive images and videos are used to ensure that they are displayed correctly on different devices in mobile-first design.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the step to implement mobile-first design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A Design the website for desktop devices first\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B Use CSS media queries to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C Use responsive images and videos to ensure that they are displayed correctly on different devices\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D Test the website on different devices and screen sizes to ensure that it is responsive and user-friendly\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To implement mobile-first design, we need to follow these steps: design the website for mobile devices first, use CSS media queries to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type, use responsive images and videos to ensure that they are displayed correctly on different devices, and test the website on different devices and screen sizes to ensure that it is responsive and user-friendly.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the step to implement responsive web design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A Design the website for desktop devices first\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B Use CSS media queries to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C Use responsive images and videos to ensure that they are displayed correctly on different devices\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D Test the website on different devices and screen sizes to ensure that it is responsive and user-friendly\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"To implement responsive web design, we need to follow these steps: design the website for mobile devices first, use CSS media queries to apply different styles based on the screen size and device type, use responsive images and videos to ensure that they are displayed correctly on different devices, and test the website on different devices and screen sizes to ensure that it is responsive and user-friendly.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the benefit of testing the website on different devices and screen sizes in mobile-first design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A To ensure that the website is responsive and user-friendly\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B To ensure that the website is not responsive and user-friendly\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C To use JavaScript to test the website\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D To use HTML to test the website\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Testing the website on different devices and screen sizes in mobile-first design ensures that it is responsive and user-friendly.\"</span>}\n      {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"question\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"What is the purpose of using HTML to create a basic structure for a mobile-first design?\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"options\"</span>:[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"A To create a basic structure for a desktop design\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"B To create a basic structure for a mobile-first design\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"C To use JavaScript to create a basic structure for a mobile-first design\"</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"D To use CSS to create a basic structure for a mobile-first design\"</span>],<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"correct_index\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>,<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"explanation\"</span>:<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"HTML is used to create a basic structure for a mobile-first design.\"</span>}\n    ];\n  </code></pre>', 'Implementing Mobile-First Design Principles', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(731, 744, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: advanced CSS Grid and Flexbox layout example</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=advanced+CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/advanced+CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/advanced+CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/advanced+CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=advanced+CSS+Grid+and+Flexbox+layout+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Create a responsive dashboard layout using advanced CSS Grid and Flexbox techniques. The layout should include a header with navigation, a main content area with a dynamic grid, and a footer. The design must adapt to different screen sizes using media queries.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>CSS Grid Advanced:</strong> Use <code>grid-template-areas</code>, <code>auto-fit</code>, and <code>minmax()</code> for flexible layouts.</li><li><strong>Flexbox Complex Layouts:</strong> Implement nested Flexbox for alignment, wrapping, and spacing.</li><li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Apply media queries and fluid units (<code>fr</code>, <code>vw</code>) for cross-device compatibility.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Set up the HTML structure with semantic elements:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;header <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"header\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;h1&gt;Dashboard&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;nav <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"nav\"</span>&gt;\n    &lt;ul&gt;\n      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#\"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#\"&gt;Profile&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n    &lt;/ul&gt;\n  &lt;/nav&gt;\n&lt;/header&gt;\n\n&lt;main <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"dashboard\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;aside <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"sidebar\"</span>&gt;Sidebar&lt;/aside&gt;\n  &lt;section <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"grid-container\"</span>&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"card\"</span>&gt;Card <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"card\"</span>&gt;Card <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"card\"</span>&gt;Card <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/section&gt;\n&lt;/main&gt;\n\n&lt;footer <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"footer\"</span>&gt;Footer&lt;/footer&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Apply Flexbox to the header and footer:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">.header {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  align-items: center;\n  padding: 1rem;\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f0f0f0;</span>\n}\n\n.nav ul {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 1rem;\n  list-style: none;\n}</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Use CSS Grid for the main content area:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">.dashboard {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-areas: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"sidebar content\"</span>;\n  grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;\n  gap: 1rem;\n  padding: 1rem;\n}\n\n.sidebar {\n  grid-area: sidebar;\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#e0e0e0;</span>\n}\n\n.grid-container {\n  grid-area: content;\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));\n  gap: 1rem;\n}</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Add responsiveness with media queries:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">@media (max-width: 768px) {\n  .dashboard {\n    grid-template-areas: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"content\"</span>;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n  }\n\n  .nav ul {\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: flex-start;\n  }\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit an HTML file with embedded CSS that demonstrates:</p><ul><li>A header and footer aligned with Flexbox.</li><li>A responsive CSS Grid layout with auto-adjusting cards.</li><li>Adaptive behavior on screens smaller than 768px.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><p><strong>1.</strong> Use browser developer tools to test responsiveness. <br><strong>2.</strong> Start with mobile-first design principles. <br><strong>3.</strong> Use <code>gap</code> and <code>auto-fit</code> to simplify spacing and layout adjustments.</p>', 'Advanced CSS Grid and Flexbox Project', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(732, 745, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript DOM manipulation dynamic content example</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+dynamic+content+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+dynamic+content+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+dynamic+content+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+dynamic+content+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+DOM+manipulation+dynamic+content+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>JavaScript DOM Manipulation: Dynamic Content Generation</h3>\n<p><strong>Task Objective:</strong> Create a dynamic web page that generates content using JavaScript, integrates CSS for styling, and manipulates the DOM to add/remove elements in real-time.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>DOM Element Creation:</strong> Use <code>document.createElement()</code> to build new HTML elements programmatically.</li>\n  <li><strong>Dynamic Content Insertion:</strong> Add/remove elements using <code>appendChild()</code>, <code>innerHTML</code>, and event listeners.</li>\n  <li><strong>JavaScript-CSS Integration:</strong> Modify element styles dynamically using <code>element.style</code> or class manipulation.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<h4>1. Create the HTML Structure</h4>\n<p>Start with a basic HTML template. Include a container for dynamic content and a button to trigger actions:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h1&gt;Dynamic Content Generator&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;button id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"addBtn\"</span>&gt;Add Item&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;div id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"contentContainer\"</span>&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;script src=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"script.js\"</span>&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h4>2. Write JavaScript to Generate Elements</h4>\n<p>Use <code>document.createElement()</code> to create new elements and append them to the container:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> addBtn = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'addBtn\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> container = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'contentContainer\'</span>);\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> itemCount = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n\naddBtn.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> newItem = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'div\'</span>);\n  newItem.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Item ${++itemCount}`</span>;\n  newItem.className = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'item\'</span>;\n  container.appendChild(newItem);\n});</code></pre>\n\n<h4>3. Add CSS for Styling</h4>\n<p>Define styles in a <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> tag or external CSS file. Use JavaScript to toggle classes:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">/* In &lt;style&gt; tag <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">or</span> CSS file */\n.item {\n  padding: 10px;\n  margin: 5px;\n  background-color: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f0f0f0;</span>\n  border: 1px solid <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#ccc;</span>\n}\n\n.highlight {\n  background-color: yellow;\n  font-weight: bold;\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h4>4. Enhance with Dynamic Styling</h4>\n<p>Modify element styles directly or toggle classes using JavaScript:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">addBtn.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> newItem = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'div\'</span>);\n  newItem.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Item ${++itemCount}`</span>;\n  newItem.className = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'item\'</span>;\n  \n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Toggle highlight on click</span>\n  newItem.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n    newItem.classList.toggle(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'highlight\'</span>);\n  });\n\n  container.appendChild(newItem);\n});</code></pre>\n\n<h4>5. Remove Elements Dynamically</h4>\n<p>Add a delete button to each item and remove it from the DOM:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">addBtn.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> newItem = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'div\'</span>);\n  newItem.className = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'item\'</span>;\n  \n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> deleteBtn = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'button\'</span>);\n  deleteBtn.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Delete\'</span>;\n  deleteBtn.onclick = () => container.removeChild(newItem);\n\n  newItem.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Item ${++itemCount}`</span>;\n  newItem.appendChild(deleteBtn);\n  container.appendChild(newItem);\n});</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Create a working example with the following features:\n<ul>\n  <li>A button to add new items to the page</li>\n  <li>Each item has a delete button</li>\n  <li>Clicking an item toggles a highlight style</li>\n  <li>Responsive layout using CSS</li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to debug DOM elements</li>\n  <li>Prefer <code>appendChild()</code> over <code>innerHTML</code> for security</li>\n  <li>Use <code>classList.toggle()</code> for clean class manipulation</li>\n  <li>Test in browser developer tools to see live DOM changes</li>\n</ol>', 'JavaScript DOM Manipulation: Dynamic Content Generation', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(733, 746, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript DOM event listener example</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+DOM+event+listener+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+DOM+event+listener+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+DOM+event+listener+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+DOM+event+listener+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+DOM+event+listener+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Build an interactive web page that demonstrates JavaScript DOM event listeners and real-time DOM updates. Create a simple counter application with buttons to increment, decrement, and reset a counter value displayed on the page.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Event Listeners:</strong> Use <code>addEventListener()</code> to respond to user actions like clicks.</li><li><strong>DOM Manipulation:</strong> Update text content dynamically using <code>textContent</code> or <code>innerHTML</code>.</li><li><strong>Interactive UI Components:</strong> Link HTML elements (buttons, display) to JavaScript logic.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Create the HTML structure with buttons and a display area.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div&gt;\n  &lt;button id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"increment\"</span>&gt;Increment&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"decrement\"</span>&gt;Decrement&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"reset\"</span>&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Current Count: &lt;span id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"counter\"</span>><span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Add JavaScript to select elements and initialize variables.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> count = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> counterDisplay = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'counter\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> incrementBtn = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'increment\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> decrementBtn = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'decrement\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> resetBtn = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'reset\'</span>);</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Implement event listeners for each button.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">incrementBtn.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  count++;\n  counterDisplay.textContent = count;\n});\n\ndecrementBtn.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  count<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">--;</span>\n  counterDisplay.textContent = count;\n});\n\nresetBtn.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  count = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  counterDisplay.textContent = count;\n});</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 4:</strong> Add validation to prevent negative counts.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">decrementBtn.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (count > <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>) {\n    count<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">--;</span>\n    counterDisplay.textContent = count;\n  } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">else</span> {\n    alert(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Count cannot be negative!\'</span>);\n  }\n});</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a single HTML file that includes:</p><ul><li>Three buttons for incrementing, decrementing, and resetting the counter</li><li>A real-time display of the counter value</li><li>Validation to prevent negative numbers</li><li>Properly escaped JavaScript and HTML syntax</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to debug event triggers and variable values</li><li>Test your code in multiple browsers to ensure compatibility</li><li>Use <code>event.preventDefault()</code> if you add form elements later</li><li>Organize your JavaScript code with clear variable names</li></ul>', 'JavaScript DOM Event Listeners and Interactivity', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(734, 747, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: javascript form validation example</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=javascript+form+validation+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/javascript+form+validation+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/javascript+form+validation+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/javascript+form+validation+example/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=javascript+form+validation+example\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>By the end of this session, you will learn to create a functional HTML form with JavaScript validation that checks user inputs, displays error messages, and prevents form submission until all requirements are met.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li>HTML form elements (<code>&lt;form&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>)</li><li>JavaScript DOM manipulation</li><li>Regular expressions for pattern validation</li><li>Event handling (<code>submit</code>, <code>blur</code>)</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<h4>1. Create the HTML Form Structure</h4>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;form id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"registrationForm\"</span> novalidate&gt;\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"form-group\"</span>&gt;\n    &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=\"username<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;Username&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input type=\"text\" id=\"username\" name=\"username\" required&gt;\n    &lt;div class=\"error-message&quot;</span> id=\"usernameError<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=\"form-group&quot;</span>&gt;\n    &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=\"email<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;Email&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input type=\"email\" id=\"email\" name=\"email\" required&gt;\n    &lt;div class=\"error-message\" id=\"emailError&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=\"form-group<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;label for=\"password&quot;</span>&gt;Password&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"password\"</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"password\"</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"password\"</span> required&gt;\n    &lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"error-message\"</span> id=\"passwordError<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;button type=\"submit&quot;</span>&gt;Register&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<h4>2. Add Basic CSS for Error Styling</h4>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">.form-group { margin-bottom: 1rem; }\ninput:invalid { border-color: red; }\n.error-message { color: red; font-size: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>.875rem; margin-top: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>.25rem; }</code></pre>\n\n<h4>3. Implement JavaScript Validation</h4>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'registrationForm\'</span>).addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'submit\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(e) {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  clearErrors();\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> username = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'username\'</span>).value.trim();\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> email = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'email\'</span>).value.trim();\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> password = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'password\'</span>).value;\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">true</span>;\n\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Username validation</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (username.length < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>) {\n    showError(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'usernameError\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Username must be at least 3 characters\'</span>);\n    isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Email validation</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (!validateEmail(email)) {\n    showError(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'emailError\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Please enter a valid email address\'</span>);\n    isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Password validation</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (password.length < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">8</span>) {\n    showError(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'passwordError\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Password must be at least 8 characters\'</span>);\n    isValid = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Submit if valid</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (isValid) {\n    alert(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Form submitted successfully!\'</span>);\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.reset();\n  }\n});\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> showError(elementId, message) {\n  document.getElementById(elementId).textContent = message;\n}\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> clearErrors() {\n  document.querySelectorAll(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'.error-message\'</span>).forEach(el => {\n    el.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>;\n  });\n}\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> validateEmail(email) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> re = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> re.test(String(email).toLowerCase());\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h4>4. Add Real-time Validation (Optional)</h4>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.querySelectorAll(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'input\'</span>).forEach(input => {\n  input.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'blur\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> id = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.id;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (id === <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'email\'</span>) {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (!validateEmail(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.value)) {\n        showError(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'emailError\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Please enter a valid email address\'</span>);\n      }\n    }\n    <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Add other field validations as needed</span>\n  });\n});</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a single HTML file that:</p><ul><li>Displays a form with username, email, and password fields</li><li>Shows specific error messages for invalid inputs</li><li>Prevents submission until all validation rules are met</li><li>Resets the form after successful submission</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to debug validation logic</li><li>Test edge cases like empty fields, short passwords, and invalid email formats</li><li>Add more validation rules later (e.g., password complexity, username uniqueness)</li></ul>', 'JavaScript Form Handling and Validation', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(735, 748, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript To-Do List App Interface</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+To-Do+List+App+Interface\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+To-Do+List+App+Interface\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+To-Do+List+App+Interface/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+To-Do+List+App+Interface/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+To-Do+List+App+Interface\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Build a functional To-Do List web application using JavaScript DOM manipulation, localStorage for persistent storage, and user interaction features like adding, deleting, and clearing tasks.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>DOM Manipulation:</strong> Dynamically create and modify HTML elements using JavaScript</li><li><strong>LocalStorage:</strong> Store and retrieve data in the browser</li><li><strong>Event Handling:</strong> Respond to user actions like button clicks and form submissions</li><li><strong>List Management:</strong> Add/remove list items and update the UI</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><p><strong>Step 1: Create the HTML Structure</strong></p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"todo-container\"</span>>&lt;h3>To-Do List App&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"text\"</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"task-input\"</span> placeholder=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Enter a new task...\"</span> /&gt;&lt;button id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"add-btn\"</span>>Add Task&lt;/button&gt;&lt;ul id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"task-list\"</span>>&lt;!<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">-- Tasks will appear here --&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;button id=\"clear-btn\">Clear All&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</span></code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 2: Add Basic CSS Styling</strong></p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">body { font-family: Arial; } <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#task-input { padding: 8px; width: 300px; } #add-btn, #clear-btn { padding: 8px 12px; margin-left: 10px; } #task-list { margin-top: 20px; list-style-type: none; } #task-list li { padding: 10px; background: #f0f0f0; margin-bottom: 5px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }</span></code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 3: JavaScript - Add Task Functionality</strong></p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'add-btn\'</span>).addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> taskText = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'task-input\'</span>).value.trim(); <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (taskText !== <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> li = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'li\'</span>); li.innerHTML = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`${taskText} &lt;button class=\"delete-btn\">Delete&lt;/button&gt;`</span>; document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'task-list\'</span>).appendChild(li); document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'task-input\'</span>).value = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>; saveTasks(); } });</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 4: JavaScript - Delete Task Functionality</strong></p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'task-list\'</span>).addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(e) { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (e.target.classList.contains(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'delete-btn\'</span>)) { e.target.parentElement.remove(); saveTasks(); } });</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 5: JavaScript - Clear All Tasks</strong></p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'clear-btn\'</span>).addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() { document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'task-list\'</span>).innerHTML = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>; saveTasks(); });</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 6: JavaScript - Save to LocalStorage</strong></p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> saveTasks() { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> tasks = []; document.querySelectorAll(\'<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#task-list li\').forEach(li => { tasks.push(li.firstChild.textContent); }); localStorage.setItem(\'tasks\', JSON.stringify(tasks)); }</span></code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 7: Load Tasks on Page Load</strong></p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> loadTasks() { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> tasks = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'tasks\'</span>)) || []; <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> taskList = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'task-list\'</span>); tasks.forEach(task => { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> li = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'li\'</span>); li.innerHTML = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`${task} &lt;button class=\"delete-btn\">Delete&lt;/button&gt;`</span>; taskList.appendChild(li); }); }</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 8: Call Load Function on Window Load</strong></p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">window.onload = loadTasks;</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><ul><li>A working To-Do List app with: <ul><li>Input field for new tasks</li><li>Add/Delete task buttons</li><li>Clear All functionality</li><li>Persistent storage using localStorage</li></ul></li><li>Three files: <code>index.html</code>, <code>style.css</code>, and <code>script.js</code></li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Test localStorage by refreshing the page - tasks should remain</li><li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to debug task arrays</li><li>Add keyboard event listener for Enter key submission</li><li>Make sure to escape special characters in task text</li></ul>', 'JavaScript DOM Project: Build a To-Do List App', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(736, 749, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: developer tools debugging</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=developer+tools+debugging\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/developer+tools+debugging\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/developer+tools+debugging/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/developer+tools+debugging/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=developer+tools+debugging\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3>\n<p>In today’s hands‑on internship you will learn how to locate, isolate, and fix bugs that arise in the Document Object Model (DOM) while also learning how to make the DOM run faster and smoother. By the end of the session you should be able to use the Browser Developer Tools to pinpoint errors, apply performance‑optimizing techniques, and implement robust error handling that prevents crashes in production.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Browser Developer Tools</strong> – the inspector, console, network, performance, and memory panels.</li>\n<li><strong>Performance Optimization</strong> – minimizing reflows, using requestAnimationFrame, debouncing, and event delegation.</li>\n<li><strong>Error Handling</strong> – try/catch, promise rejection handling, and graceful degradation.</li>\n<li><strong>DOM APIs</strong> – querySelector, addEventListener, createDocumentFragment, and innerHTML.</li>\n<li><strong>Profiling Techniques</strong> – recording a performance trace, analyzing frame rates, and memory snapshots.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step‑by‑Step Instructions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1. Set Up a Simple Page</strong>\n<p>Create a file named <code>debug.html</code> with a few nested elements, a button, and a script that manipulates the DOM. Include a <code>div</code> that will be updated when the button is clicked.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'en\'</span>&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;meta charset=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'UTF-8\'</span>&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;Debugging Demo&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;div id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'container\'</span>&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Initial content.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;button id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'updateBtn\'</span>&gt;Update&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Script will be added later</span>\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>2. Open Developer Tools</strong>\n<p>Press <code>F12</code> or right‑click and choose <em>Inspect</em>. Familiarize yourself with the <strong>Elements</strong> panel to see the live DOM tree.</p></li>\n<li><strong>3. Inspect Variables in the Console</strong>\n<p>In the <strong>Console</strong> panel type:\n</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">var</span> btn = document.querySelector(\'<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#updateBtn\');</span>\nconsole.log(btn);\n</code></pre>\n<p>Use <code>console.dir()</code> to explore the object structure.</p></li>\n<li><strong>4. Add a Breakpoint</strong>\n<p>In the <strong>Sources</strong> panel open the script file, click the line number to add a breakpoint. Reload the page; execution pauses, allowing you to step through each line.</p></li>\n<li><strong>5. Identify a Reflow‑Heavy Operation</strong>\n<p>Modify the script to add many <code>p</code> elements inside the container. Observe that the page freezes. Use the <strong>Performance</strong> panel: record a 5‑second trace, then look at the <em>Layout</em> section to see how many reflows occur.</p></li>\n<li><strong>6. Optimize with DocumentFragment</strong>\n<p>Rewrite the code to build elements in a <code>DocumentFragment</code> before appending once.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">var</span> frag = document.createDocumentFragment();\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> (<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">var</span> i = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>; i < <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1000</span>; i++) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">var</span> p = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'p\'</span>);\n  p.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Line \'</span> + i;\n  frag.appendChild(p);\n}\ncontainer.appendChild(frag);\n</code></pre>\n<p>Re‑record the performance trace; reflows should drop dramatically.</p></li>\n<li><strong>7. Use requestAnimationFrame for Animations</strong>\n<p>If you animate the container’s opacity, wrap the style change inside <code>requestAnimationFrame</code> to sync with the browser’s paint cycle.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> fadeOut() {\n  requestAnimationFrame(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n    container.style.opacity = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  });\n}\n</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>8. Implement Debouncing for Resize Events</strong>\n<p>Resize listeners can fire many times per second. Debounce the handler to run once after resizing stops.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">var</span> resizeTimer;\nwindow.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'resize\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n  clearTimeout(resizeTimer);\n  resizeTimer = setTimeout(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Resize finished\'</span>);\n  }, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">200</span>);\n});\n</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>9. Add Robust Error Handling</strong>\n<p>Wrap DOM manipulation in <code>try/catch</code> blocks and log errors to the console. For asynchronous code, attach <code>.catch</code> to promises.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">try</span> {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">var</span> nonExistent = document.querySelector(\'<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#doesNotExist\');</span>\n  nonExistent.textContent = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Test\'</span>;\n} <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">catch</span> (e) {\n  console.error(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'DOM error:\'</span>, e);\n}\n\nfetch(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/api/data\'</span>)\n  .then(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(response) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> response.json();\n  })\n  .<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">catch</span>(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(err) {\n    console.warn(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Fetch failed:\'</span>, err);\n  });\n</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>10. Verify Improvements</strong>\n<p>Use the <strong>Performance</strong> panel again to compare before and after metrics. Check the <strong>Console</strong> for any uncaught errors.</p></li>\n<li><strong>11. Document Your Findings</strong>\n<p>Write a short report (1‑2 paragraphs) summarizing the bugs you found, the steps you took to fix them, and the performance gains measured.</p></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Your submission should include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <code>debug.html</code> file with the optimized script.</li>\n<li>A screenshot of the Performance panel showing reduced layout thrashing.</li>\n<li>A one‑page PDF or Markdown file that explains the debugging process, the optimizations applied, and the error‑handling strategy.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Use DevTools Shortcuts</strong> – <code>Ctrl+Shift+I</code> opens DevTools, <code>Ctrl+Shift+C</code> toggles the element selector, and <code>Ctrl+Shift+P</code> opens the command palette.</li>\n<li><strong>Leverage the Coverage Panel</strong> to identify unused CSS and JavaScript that can be removed.</li>\n<li><strong>Profile in Real Devices</strong> – use Chrome Remote Debugging to test on mobile, where performance constraints are tighter.</li>\n<li><strong>Keep the DOM Light</strong> – avoid deep nesting; use <code>DocumentFragment</code> for bulk inserts.</li>\n<li><strong>Graceful Degradation</strong> – always check for feature support (e.g., <code>if (\'requestAnimationFrame\' in window)</code>) before using modern APIs.</li>\n</ul>', 'Debugging and Optimizing DOM Code', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(737, 750, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: short search query</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div>[HTML content here]', 'Introduction to Advanced JavaScript Concepts', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(738, 751, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: JavaScript Closures and Context</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=JavaScript+Closures+and+Context\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/JavaScript+Closures+and+Context\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/JavaScript+Closures+and+Context/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/JavaScript+Closures+and+Context/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=JavaScript+Closures+and+Context\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Understanding JavaScript Closures and Context</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, we will delve into the advanced JavaScript topics of closures and context.</p>\n<h3>Closures</h3>\n<p>A closure is a function that has access to its outer scope\'s variables, even when the outer function has returned.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> outer() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> x = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">10</span>;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> inner() {\n    console.log(x);\n  }\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> inner;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> f = outer();\nf(); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 10</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>This is an example of a closure because the inner function has access to the variable x, even though the outer function has returned.</p>\n<p>Here\'s another example:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> makeCounter() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> count = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n    count++;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> count;\n  }\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> counter = makeCounter();\nconsole.log(counter()); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 1</span>\nconsole.log(counter()); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 2</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>This is also an example of a closure because the returned function has access to the variable count, even though the makeCounter function has returned.</p>\n<h3>Context</h3>\n<p>Context refers to the execution context of a function, which includes the value of this, the function\'s arguments, and the scope chain.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> sayHello(name) {\n  console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Hello, ${name}!`</span>);\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> obj = { name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'John\'</span> };\nsayHello.call(obj, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Jane\'</span>); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: Hello, Jane!</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>In this example, the this keyword refers to the obj object, even though it\'s not explicitly passed as an argument.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> sayHello(name) {\n  console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Hello, ${name}!`</span>);\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> obj = { name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'John\'</span> };\nsayHello.apply(obj, [<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Jane\'</span>]); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: Hello, Jane!</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>This is another way to set the context of a function using the apply method.</p>\n<h3>Using Closures and Context in Real-World Scenarios</h3>\n<p>Closures and context are essential concepts in JavaScript that can be used in a variety of real-world scenarios.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Private Variables:</strong> Closures can be used to create private variables that are not accessible from outside the closure.</li>\n  <li><strong>Event Listeners:</strong> Context can be used to set the this keyword to the element that triggered the event.</li>\n  <li><strong>Dependency Injection:</strong> Closures can be used to create functions that depend on other functions or variables.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Here\'s an example of using closures to create private variables:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> createCounter() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> count = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> {\n    increment: <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n      count++;\n    },\n    getCount: <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> count;\n    }\n  }\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> counter = createCounter();\ncounter.increment();\nconsole.log(counter.getCount()); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 1</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>This is an example of using closures to create private variables, in this case, the count variable is not accessible from outside the closure.</p>\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<p>What is the output of the following code?</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> outer() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> x = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">10</span>;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> inner() {\n    console.log(x);\n  }\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> inner;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> f = outer();\nf(); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: ?</span>\n</code></pre>\n<p>Answer: 10</p>\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, we learned about closures and context in JavaScript. Closures are functions that have access to their outer scope\'s variables, even when the outer function has returned. Context refers to the execution context of a function, which includes the value of this, the function\'s arguments, and the scope chain. We also learned about using closures and context in real-world scenarios, such as creating private variables, event listeners, and dependency injection.</p>\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n<p>short search query: JavaScript Closures and Context</p>\n<h3>Deliverables</h3>\n<p>Write a short paragraph explaining the difference between a closure and a context in JavaScript. Use an example to illustrate the difference.</p>\n<p>Write a short paragraph explaining how closures and context can be used in real-world scenarios. Use an example to illustrate the use of closures and context in a real-world scenario.</p>\n<p>Write a short paragraph explaining why closures and context are essential concepts in JavaScript. Use an example to illustrate the importance of closures and context in JavaScript.</p>', 'Understanding JavaScript Closures and Context', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(739, 752, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: short search query</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Exploring JavaScript Prototypes and Inheritance</h3>\n<p>In this task, we will delve into the world of JavaScript prototypes and inheritance. Prototypes are a fundamental concept in JavaScript that allows us to create objects that inherit properties and methods from other objects.</p>\n<h3>What are Prototypes?</h3>\n<p>A prototype in JavaScript is an object that serves as a template for other objects. When we create a new object, it inherits the properties and methods of its prototype. This allows us to create a hierarchy of objects where child objects inherit from parent objects.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Creating a prototype</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> Animal(name) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name = name;\n}\n\nAnimal.prototype.eat = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\' is eating\'</span>);\n};\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Creating an object that inherits from the Animal prototype</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> dog = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Animal(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Buddy\'</span>);\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Calling the eat method on the dog object</span>\ndog.eat(); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: Buddy is eating</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>What is Inheritance?</h3>\n<p>Inheritance in JavaScript is the ability of one object to inherit the properties and methods of another object. This is achieved through the prototype chain, where an object\'s prototype is linked to its parent object\'s prototype.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Creating a parent object</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> Animal(name) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name = name;\n}\n\nAnimal.prototype.eat = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\' is eating\'</span>);\n};\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Creating a child object that inherits from the Animal parent</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> Dog(name) {\n    Animal.call(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>, name);\n}\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Setting the prototype of the Dog object to the Animal prototype</span>\nDog.prototype = Object.create(Animal.prototype);\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Adding a new method to the Dog prototype</span>\nDog.prototype.bark = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\' is barking\'</span>);\n};\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Creating a new Dog object</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> myDog = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Dog(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Max\'</span>);\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Calling the eat and bark methods on the myDog object</span>\nmyDog.eat(); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: Max is eating</span>\nmyDog.bark(); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: Max is barking</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Prototypal Inheritance</h3>\n<p>Prototypal inheritance is a technique used to implement inheritance in JavaScript. It involves creating a new object that inherits from another object\'s prototype. This is achieved through the use of the Object.create() method.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Creating a parent object</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> Animal(name) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name = name;\n}\n\nAnimal.prototype.eat = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.name + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\' is eating\'</span>);\n};\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Creating a child object that inherits from the Animal parent using prototypal inheritance</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> dog = Object.create(Animal.prototype);\ndog.name = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Buddy\'</span>;\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Calling the eat method on the dog object</span>\ndog.eat(); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: Buddy is eating</span>\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n<p>In this task, we explored the concepts of prototypes and inheritance in JavaScript. We learned how to create prototypes, implement inheritance, and use prototypal inheritance to create a hierarchy of objects. With this knowledge, you can create more complex and maintainable JavaScript applications.</p>\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>What is a prototype in JavaScript?</li>\n    <li>How does inheritance work in JavaScript?</li>\n    <li>What is prototypal inheritance?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Answer the following questions in the comments section below:</p>\n<ul>\n    <li>What is the output of the following code:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> animal = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Animal(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Buddy\'</span>);\nanimal.eat();\n</code></pre>\n    <li>What is the output of the following code:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> dog = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Dog(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Max\'</span>);\ndog.eat();\ndog.bark();\n</code></pre>\n    <li>What is the output of the following code:</li>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">let</span> myDog = Object.create(Animal.prototype);\nmyDog.name = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Buddy\'</span>;\nmyDog.eat();\n</code></pre>\n</ul>\n<h3>Deliverables</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>Write a short paragraph explaining the difference between a constructor function and a prototype.</li>\n    <li>Implement a simple inheritance hierarchy using prototypes and inheritance.</li>\n    <li>Use prototypal inheritance to create a new object that inherits from a parent object.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Learning Outcomes</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>Understand the concept of prototypes and inheritance in JavaScript.</li>\n    <li>Learn how to implement inheritance using prototypes and inheritance.</li>\n    <li>Understand how to use prototypal inheritance to create a hierarchy of objects.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n<p>Short search query: \'JavaScript prototypes and inheritance\'</p>\n', 'Exploring JavaScript Prototypes and Inheritance', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(740, 753, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: higher-order functions in JavaScript</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=higher-order+functions+in+JavaScript\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/higher-order+functions+in+JavaScript\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/higher-order+functions+in+JavaScript/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/higher-order+functions+in+JavaScript/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=higher-order+functions+in+JavaScript\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><html>\n<head>\n    <title>Implementing Higher-Order Functions in JavaScript</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <h3>Higher-Order Functions in JavaScript</h3>\n    <p>Higher-order functions are functions that take other functions as arguments or return functions as output. They are a fundamental concept in functional programming and are widely used in JavaScript.</p>\n    <h3>Concepts You Need to Understand</h3>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Higher-Order Functions</li>\n        <li>Function Composition</li>\n    </ul>\n    <h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n    <ol>\n        <li><strong>Understanding Higher-Order Functions</strong></li>\n        <p>A higher-order function is a function that takes another function as an argument or returns a function as output. This is different from a regular function that only takes data as input and returns data as output.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> add(x, y) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> x + y;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> multiply(x, y) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> x * y;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> higherOrderFunction(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">func</span>, x, y) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">func</span>(x, y);\n}\nconsole.log(higherOrderFunction(add, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">10</span>)); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 15</span>\nconsole.log(higherOrderFunction(multiply, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">10</span>)); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 50</span>\n        </code></pre>\n        <li><strong>Function Composition</strong></li>\n        <p>Function composition is the process of combining two or more functions to create a new function. This is useful when you need to perform multiple operations on data.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">double</span>(x) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> x * <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> addFive(x) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> x + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> compose(f, g) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(x) {\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> f(g(x));\n    };\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> doubleAndAddFive = compose(addFive, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">double</span>);\nconsole.log(doubleAndAddFive(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">10</span>)); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 25</span>\n        </code></pre>\n        <li><strong>Implementing Higher-Order Functions in JavaScript</strong></li>\n        <p>Higher-order functions are implemented in JavaScript using the function keyword and the arguments keyword. The arguments keyword is used to pass arguments to the inner function.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> higherOrderFunction(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">func</span>, ...args) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">func</span>(...args);\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> add(x, y) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> x + y;\n}\nconsole.log(higherOrderFunction(add, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">10</span>)); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 15</span>\n        </code></pre>\n    </ol>\n    <h3>Deliverable</h3>\n    <p>Implement a higher-order function in JavaScript that takes another function as an argument and returns the result of calling that function with the provided arguments.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> higherOrderFunction(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">func</span>, ...args) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">func</span>(...args);\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> add(x, y) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> x + y;\n}\nconsole.log(higherOrderFunction(add, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">10</span>)); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 15</span>\n        </code></pre>\n    <h3>Quiz</h3>\n    <p>Implement a function composition function in JavaScript that takes two functions as arguments and returns a new function that composes the two input functions.</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> compose(f, g) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span>(x) {\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> f(g(x));\n    };\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> addFive(x) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> x + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">double</span>(x) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> x * <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> doubleAndAddFive = compose(addFive, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">double</span>);\nconsole.log(doubleAndAddFive(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">10</span>)); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 25</span>\n        </code></pre>\n    <h3>Image Query</h3>\n    <p>Search for images related to higher-order functions in JavaScript.</p>\n    <p>Search query: \"higher-order functions in JavaScript\"</p>\n</body>\n</html>', 'Implementing Higher-Order Functions in JavaScript', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(741, 754, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: react list component</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=react+list+component\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/react+list+component\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/react+list+component/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/react+list+component/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=react+list+component\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>React List</h3><ul><li><strong>Item 1</strong><p>This is item 1</p></li><li><strong>Item 2</strong><p>This is item 2</p></li><li><strong>Item 3</strong><p>This is item 3</p></li></ul>', 'Learning Front-end Frameworks: Introduction to React', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(742, 755, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: Angular framework introduction diagram</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=Angular+framework+introduction+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/Angular+framework+introduction+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/Angular+framework+introduction+diagram/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/Angular+framework+introduction+diagram/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=Angular+framework+introduction+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>By the end of this task, you will understand the basics of <strong>Angular</strong>—a popular front-end framework—and how <strong>modules</strong> organize Angular applications. You will create a simple Angular project, explore its structure, and implement a basic feature using Angular concepts.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>HTML/CSS/JavaScript</strong>: Basic web development skills</li><li><strong>Front-end frameworks</strong>: Familiarity with frameworks like React or Vue.js (optional)</li><li><strong>Angular CLI</strong>: Command-line tool for scaffolding Angular projects</li><li><strong>Angular modules</strong>: How modules organize components, services, and dependencies</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><ol>\n  <li><strong>Install Angular CLI</strong><p>Run the following command in your terminal to install Angular CLI globally:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npm install -g @angular/cli</code></pre></li>\n\n  <li><strong>Create a New Angular Project</strong><p>Generate a new project named <code>angular-intro</code> using:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">ng <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> angular-intro</code></pre><p>Select <code>Yes</code> for routing and choose <code>JavaScript</code> or <code>TypeScript</code> (beginners can choose JavaScript).</p></li>\n\n  <li><strong>Run the Development Server</strong><p>Navigate into the project folder and start the server:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">cd angular-intro\nng serve <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">--open</span></code></pre><p>This opens the default Angular app in your browser at <code>http://localhost:4200</code>.</p></li>\n\n  <li><strong>Explore the Project Structure</strong><p>Locate the following key files:</p><ul><li><code>src/app/app.module.js</code>: The root module of the application.</li><li><code>src/app/app.component.js</code>: The root component containing logic (component class).</li><li><code>src/app/app.component.html</code>: The template for the root component.</li></ul></li>\n\n  <li><strong>Create a New Component</strong><p>Generate a component named <code>hello-world</code> using:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">ng generate component hello-world</code></pre><p>This creates four files: <code>hello-world.component.js</code>, <code>.html</code>, <code>.css</code>, and <code>.spec.js</code>.</p></li>\n\n  <li><strong>Update the Module</strong><p>Open <code>app.module.js</code> and verify that <code>HelloWorldComponent</code> is declared in the <code>declarations</code> array. Angular modules group related components, directives, and pipes.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { HelloWorldComponent } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'./hello-world/hello-world.component\'</span>;\n\n@NgModule({\n  declarations: [\n    AppComponent,\n    HelloWorldComponent\n  ],\n  ...</code></pre></li>\n\n  <li><strong>Display the Component</strong><p>Edit <code>app.component.html</code> to include the new component:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;app-hello-world&gt;&lt;/app-hello-world&gt;</code></pre><p>Run <code>ng serve</code> to see the updated app.</p></li>\n\n  <li><strong>Add Interactivity</strong><p>Open <code>hello-world.component.js</code> and add a method to toggle a message:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">export <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span> HelloWorldComponent {\n  message = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Hello, Angular!\'</span>;\n  showMessage = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">true</span>;\n\n  toggleMessage() {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.showMessage = !<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.showMessage;\n  }\n}</code></pre><p>In <code>hello-world.component.html</code>, add:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;p *ngIf=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"showMessage\"</span>>{{ message }}&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;button (click)=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"toggleMessage()\"</span>>Toggle Message&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre></li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><ul><li>A working Angular project with the <code>hello-world</code> component and toggle functionality.</li><li>A screenshot of the running app showing the toggled message.</li><li>A brief explanation (100-200 words) of how Angular modules organize components.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>ng serve</code> to automatically rebuild the app when files change.</li><li>Check the browser console for errors if the app fails to load.</li><li>Refer to the <a href=\\\"https://angular.io\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Angular documentation</a> for CLI commands and module syntax.</li></ul>', 'Learning Front-end Frameworks: Introduction to Angular', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(743, 756, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: Vue.js lifecycle diagram</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=Vue.js+lifecycle+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/Vue.js+lifecycle+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/Vue.js+lifecycle+diagram/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/Vue.js+lifecycle+diagram/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=Vue.js+lifecycle+diagram\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Build a simple Vue.js application that demonstrates the use of lifecycle hooks. Students will create a component that logs messages during different stages of the Vue instance lifecycle (created, mounted, updated, destroyed). The final application should display dynamic content and show console logs when lifecycle events occur.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Front-end Frameworks:</strong> Understand how frameworks like Vue.js simplify DOM manipulation and state management</li><li><strong>Vue.js Basics:</strong> Create a Vue instance, bind data to the DOM using directives like <code>v-bind</code> and <code>v-on</code></li><li><strong>Vue Lifecycle Hooks:</strong> Know the purpose of <code>created</code>, <code>mounted</code>, <code>updated</code>, and <code>destroyed</code> hooks</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Setup Project</strong><p>Create an HTML file with basic structure. Include Vue.js via CDN:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script src=\"https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vue@2.6.14/dist/vue.js\"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</span></code></pre>\n</li>\n\n<li><strong>Create Vue Instance</strong><p>Add a <code>div</code> container and initialize a Vue instance:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"app\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Current Count: {{ count }}&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;button @click=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"increment\"</span>>Add <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Vue({\n  el: \'<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#app\',</span>\n  data: { count: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span> },\n  methods: {\n    increment() { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.count++ }\n  }\n})\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>\n</li>\n\n<li><strong>Add Lifecycle Hooks</strong><p>Update the Vue instance to include lifecycle hooks that log messages to the console:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Vue({\n  el: \'<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#app\',</span>\n  data: { count: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span> },\n  methods: {\n    increment() { <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.count++ }\n  },\n  created() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Instance created!\'</span>);\n  },\n  mounted() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Instance mounted!\'</span>);\n  },\n  updated() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Data updated!\'</span>);\n  },\n  destroyed() {\n    console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Instance destroyed!\'</span>);\n  }\n})</code></pre>\n</li>\n\n<li><strong>Test Lifecycle Events</strong><p>Open the browser console and:</p><ul><li>Refresh the page to see <code>created</code> and <code>mounted</code> logs</li><li>Click the button to see <code>updated</code> logs</li><li>Add JavaScript to destroy the instance: <code>app.$destroy()</code> to see the <code>destroyed</code> log</li></ul></li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a single HTML file containing:</p><ul><li>A working Vue instance with at least 3 lifecycle hooks implemented</li><li>Console logs that demonstrate each hook firing correctly</li><li>Clear comments explaining each hook\'s purpose</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use browser DevTools to monitor console output and DOM changes</li><li>Test your code incrementally - add one hook at a time</li><li>Experiment with different hook combinations to see how they interact</li></ul>', 'Learning Front-end Frameworks: Introduction to Vue.js', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(744, 757, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: simple web app with React Angular Vue.js</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=simple+web+app+with+React+Angular+Vue.js\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/simple+web+app+with+React+Angular+Vue.js\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/simple+web+app+with+React+Angular+Vue.js/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/simple+web+app+with+React+Angular+Vue.js/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=simple+web+app+with+React+Angular+Vue.js\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Build a simple web application using a front-end framework (React, Angular, or Vue.js). Learn core concepts like components, state management, and event handling while creating a functional user interface.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><p>1. <strong>Components</strong>: Reusable UI elements that encapsulate logic and presentation.<br>2. <strong>State</strong>: Dynamic data that drives UI updates.<br>3. <strong>Props/Events</strong>: Data flow between parent and child components.<br>4. <strong>Virtual DOM (React)</strong>: Efficient UI updates through reconciliation.<br>5. <strong>Directives (Vue.js)</strong>: Special attributes for DOM manipulation.<br>6. <strong>Data Binding (Angular)</strong>: Two-way synchronization between UI and data.</p>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><p><strong>Step 1: Choose a Framework</strong><br>Select one framework: React, Angular, or Vue.js. For this example, we’ll use React.</p>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npx create-react-app todo-app<br>cd todo-app<br>npm start</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 2: Create a Component</strong><br>Build a <code>TodoList</code> component to display tasks.</p>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> React, { useState } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'react\'</span>;<br><br><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> TodoList() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> [tasks, setTasks] = useState([]);\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> [input, setInput] = useState(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>);\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> addTask = () => {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (input.trim()) {\n      setTasks([...tasks, input]);\n      setInput(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>);\n    }\n  };\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;div&gt;\n      &lt;h1&gt;To-Do List&lt;/h1&gt;\n      &lt;input\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"text\"</span>\n        value={input}\n        onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)}\n        placeholder=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Add a task\"</span>\n      /&gt;\n      &lt;button onClick={addTask}&gt;Add&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;ul&gt;\n        {tasks.map((task, index) => (\n          &lt;li key={index}&gt;{task}&lt;/li&gt;\n        ))}\n      &lt;/ul&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  );\n}\n\nexport default TodoList;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 3: Integrate with Parent Component</strong><br>Render <code>TodoList</code> in <code>App.js</code>.</p>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> React <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'react\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> TodoList <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'./TodoList\'</span>;\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> App() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;div&gt;\n      &lt;TodoList /&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  );\n}\n\nexport default App;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 4: Test and Debug</strong><br>Add tasks to verify state updates and UI rendering.</p>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>A working to-do list application with the following features:<br>- Input field for adding tasks<br>- Dynamic task list updates<br>- Clean, responsive UI</p>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul>\n  <li>Use <code>console.log()</code> to debug state changes.</li>\n  <li>Refer to the official framework documentation for syntax specifics.</li>\n  <li>Start with a minimal design and add complexity incrementally.</li>\n</ul>', 'Building a Simple Web Application with a Front-end Framework', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(745, 758, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: React complex web application with routing and state management</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=React+complex+web+application+with+routing+and+state+management\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/React+complex+web+application+with+routing+and+state+management\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/React+complex+web+application+with+routing+and+state+management/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/React+complex+web+application+with+routing+and+state+management/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=React+complex+web+application+with+routing+and+state+management\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Build a feature-rich web application using React that demonstrates dynamic components, state management, and integration with an external API. The app will include navigation, user interaction, and data display from a mock API.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>React Components:</strong> Functional components, props, and component composition</li><li><strong>State Management:</strong> useState and useContext hooks</li><li><strong>Routing:</strong> React Router v6 for navigation</li><li><strong>API Integration:</strong> Fetching data from a REST API</li><li><strong>Event Handling:</strong> Form inputs and user interactions</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<h4>1. Project Setup</h4><p>Create a new React project using Create React App:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npx create-react-app complex-app</code></pre><p>Install required dependencies:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npm install react-router-dom axios</code></pre>\n\n<h4>2. Component Structure</h4><p>Create the following component files in <code>src/components/</code>:</p><ul><li><code>Header.js</code></li><li><code>ProductList.js</code></li><li><code>ProductDetail.js</code></li><li><code>Cart.js</code></li></ul>\n\n<h4>3. State Management</h4><p>Create a context for cart state in <code>src/context/CartContext.js</code>:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> React, { createContext, useState } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'react\'</span>;\n\nexport <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> CartContext = createContext();\n\nexport <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> CartProvider = ({ children }) => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> [cart, setCart] = useState([]);\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> addToCart = (product) => {\n    setCart([...cart, product]);\n  };\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;CartContext.Provider value={{ cart, addToCart }}&gt;\n      {children}\n    &lt;/CartContext.Provider&gt;\n  );\n};</code></pre>\n\n<h4>4. Routing Configuration</h4><p>Update <code>App.js</code> with React Router:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { BrowserRouter <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">as</span> Router, Routes, Route } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'react-router-dom\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> Header <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'./components/Header\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> ProductList <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'./components/ProductList\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> ProductDetail <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'./components/ProductDetail\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> Cart <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'./components/Cart\'</span>;\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> App = () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;Router&gt;\n      &lt;Header /&gt;\n      &lt;Routes&gt;\n        &lt;Route path=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/\'</span> element={&lt;ProductList /&gt;} /&gt;\n        &lt;Route path=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/product/:id\'</span> element={&lt;ProductDetail /&gt;} /&gt;\n        &lt;Route path=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/cart\'</span> element={&lt;Cart /&gt;} /&gt;\n      &lt;/Routes&gt;\n    &lt;/Router&gt;\n  );\n};</code></pre>\n\n<h4>5. API Integration</h4><p>Create <code>src/api.js</code> to fetch mock data:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> axios <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'axios\'</span>;\n\nexport <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> fetchProducts = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">async</span> () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> response = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">await</span> axios.get(\'https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//fakestoreapi.com/products\');</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> response.data;\n};\n\nexport <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> fetchProductById = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">async</span> (id) => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> response = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">await</span> axios.get(`https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//fakestoreapi.com/products/${id}`);</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> response.data;\n};</code></pre>\n\n<h4>6. ProductList Component</h4><p>Implement <code>ProductList.js</code> with API call:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> React, { useEffect, useState } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'react\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { fetchProducts } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'../api\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { useNavigate } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'react-router-dom\'</span>;\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> ProductList = () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> [products, setProducts] = useState([]);\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> navigate = useNavigate();\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    fetchProducts().then((data) => setProducts(data));\n  }, []);\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;div&gt;\n      {products.map((product) => (\n        &lt;div key={product.id} onClick={() => navigate(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`/product/${product.id}`</span>)}&gt;\n          &lt;h3&gt;{product.name}&lt;/h3&gt;\n          &lt;p&gt;${product.price}&lt;/p&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n      ))}\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  );\n};</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>A fully functional React application with:</p><ul><li>Product listing page with clickable items</li><li>Product detail page showing full information</li><li>Shopping cart that persists across routes</li><li>Working navigation between pages</li><li>Integration with external API for data</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>React Developer Tools</code> for debugging component hierarchies</li><li>Implement loading states for API calls</li><li>Add error handling for failed API requests</li><li>Use modular CSS for component-specific styling</li><li>Test routing with different URL parameters</li></ul>', 'Building a Complex Web Application with React', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(746, 759, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: Angular complex web application components</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=Angular+complex+web+application+components\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/Angular+complex+web+application+components\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/Angular+complex+web+application+components/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/Angular+complex+web+application+components/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=Angular+complex+web+application+components\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Build a complex Angular web application with multiple components, services, and routing. Create a <strong>Task Manager</strong> application that includes task creation, display, and navigation between views.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li>Angular CLI project setup</li><li>Component creation and data binding</li><li>Angular services and dependency injection</li><li>Routing between components</li><li>Two-way data binding with forms</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n\n<h4>Step 1: Set Up Angular Project</h4><p>Generate a new Angular project using Angular CLI:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">ng <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> task-manager-app <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">--routing</span></code></pre><p>Select <code>Y</code> for Angular routing and <code>Y</code> for CSS styling.</p>\n\n<h4>Step 2: Create Components</h4><p>Generate three components: <code>TaskList</code>, <code>TaskDetail</code>, and <code>CreateTask</code>:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">cd task-manager-app\nng generate component task-list\ng generate component task-detail\ng generate component create-task</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 3: Create a Task Service</h4><p>Generate a service to manage task data:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">ng generate service task</code></pre><p>Update <code>task.service.ts</code> with this code:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { Injectable } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@angular/core\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { BehaviorSubject } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'rxjs\'</span>;\n\n@Injectable({ providedIn: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'root\'</span> })\nexport <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span> TaskService {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">private</span> tasks = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> BehaviorSubject&lt;any[]&gt;([]);\n\n  constructor() { }\n\n  getTasks() {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.tasks.asObservable();\n  }\n\n  addTask(task: any) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> currentTasks = [...<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.tasks.getValue(), task];\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.tasks.next(currentTasks);\n  }\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 4: Configure Routing</h4><p>Update <code>app-routing.module.ts</code>:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> routes: Routes = [\n  { path: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'tasks\'</span>, component: TaskListComponent },\n  { path: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'task/:id\'</span>, component: TaskDetailComponent },\n  { path: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'create\'</span>, component: CreateTaskComponent },\n  { path: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>, redirectTo: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/tasks\'</span>, pathMatch: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'full\'</span> }\n];</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 5: Implement TaskList Component</h4><p>Update <code>task-list.component.ts</code>:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { Component, OnInit } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@angular/core\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { TaskService } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'../task.service\'</span>;\n\n@Component({ selector: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'app-task-list\'</span>, templateUrl: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'./task-list.component.html\'</span> })\nexport <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span> TaskListComponent <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">implements</span> OnInit {\n  tasks: any[] = [];\n\n  constructor(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">private</span> taskService: TaskService) {}\n\n  ngOnInit() {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.taskService.getTasks().subscribe(tasks => {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.tasks = tasks;\n    });\n  }\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 6: Create Task Detail View</h4><p>Update <code>task-detail.component.ts</code> to display task details using route parameters:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { ActivatedRoute } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@angular/router\'</span>;\n\nconstructor(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">private</span> route: ActivatedRoute, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">private</span> taskService: TaskService) {}\n\nngOnInit() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.route.params.subscribe(params => {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> taskId = params[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'id\'</span>];\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.task = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.taskService.getTaskById(taskId);\n  });\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 7: Build CreateTask Form</h4><p>Update <code>create-task.component.html</code> with a form using two-way binding:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;form (ngSubmit)=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"onSubmit()\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;input [(ngModel)]=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"task.title\"</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"title\"</span> required&gt;\n  &lt;textarea [(ngModel)]=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"task.description\"</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"description\"</span>&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;\n  &lt;button <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=\"submit&quot;&gt;Create Task&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 8: Connect Components</h4><p>Add navigation links in <code>app.component.html</code>:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;nav&gt;\n  &lt;a routerLink=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"/tasks\"</span>>Tasks&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;a routerLink=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"/create\"</span>>Create Task&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;/nav&gt;\n&lt;router-outlet&gt;&lt;/router-outlet&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a GitHub repository with a fully functional Task Manager app that includes:</p><ul><li>Task list view</li><li>Task detail view with routing</li><li>Create task form with data binding</li><li>Service for data sharing</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><p><strong>Tip 1:</strong> Use Angular CLI commands like <code>ng serve</code> to test the app locally.</p><p><strong>Tip 2:</strong> Add <code>FormsModule</code> to <code>app.module.ts</code> for ngModel to work.</p><p><strong>Tip 3:</strong> Use <code>ng build</code> to generate a production-ready build.</p>', 'Building a Complex Web Application with Angular', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(747, 760, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: Vue.js complex application illustration</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=Vue.js+complex+application+illustration\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/Vue.js+complex+application+illustration\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/Vue.js+complex+application+illustration/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/Vue.js+complex+application+illustration/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=Vue.js+complex+application+illustration\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3>\n<p>In today’s hands‑on session you will build a small but fully functional complex web application using <strong>Vue.js</strong>. The goal is to demonstrate how a front‑end framework can manage state, routing, component composition, and API integration in a cohesive project. By the end of the day you should have a live demo that showcases a multi‑page application with nested components, form handling, and data persistence to a mock backend.</p>\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Vue.js Basics</strong> – Components, props, events, and reactivity.</li>\n<li><strong>Vue Router</strong> – Declarative routing and navigation guards.</li>\n<li><strong>Vuex (or Pinia)</strong> – Centralized state management for complex data flows.</li>\n<li><strong>Composition API</strong> – <code>ref</code>, <code>reactive</code>, <code>computed</code>, and <code>watch</code> for cleaner logic.</li>\n<li><strong>Axios</strong> – HTTP client for API requests.</li>\n<li><strong>Mock Service Worker (MSW)</strong> – Simulated backend for testing.</li>\n<li><strong>Component Hierarchy</strong> – Parent/child relationships and slot usage.</li>\n<li><strong>Form Validation</strong> – Basic validation with <code>v-model</code> and computed error messages.</li>\n<li><strong>Responsive Design</strong> – Flexbox/Grid basics for layout.</li>\n<li><strong>Testing</strong> – Simple unit test with Jest and Vue Test Utils.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Step‑by‑Step Instructions</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Project Setup</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Run <code>npm create vite@latest vue-complex-app -- --template vue</code> to scaffold a Vite + Vue 3 project.</li>\n<li>Navigate into the folder and install dependencies: <code>npm install</code>.</li>\n<li>Add Vue Router and Pinia: <code>npm i vue-router@4 pinia axios msw</code>.</li>\n<li>Create a <code>src/router/index.js</code> with two routes: <code>/dashboard</code> and <code>/profile</code>.\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script setup&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { createRouter, createWebHistory } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'vue-router\'</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> Dashboard <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@/views/Dashboard.vue\'</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> Profile <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@/views/Profile.vue\'</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> routes = [\n  { path: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/\'</span>, redirect: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/dashboard\'</span> },\n  { path: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/dashboard\'</span>, component: Dashboard },\n  { path: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/profile\'</span>, component: Profile }\n]\n\nexport default createRouter({\n  history: createWebHistory(),\n  routes\n})\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>State Store</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>In <code>src/stores/userStore.js</code>, set up Pinia store:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script setup&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { defineStore } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'pinia\'</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { ref } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'vue\'</span>\n\nexport <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> useUserStore = defineStore(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'user\'</span>, () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> profile = ref({ name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>, email: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span> })\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> isAuthenticated = ref(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>)\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> login(user) {\n    profile.value = user\n    isAuthenticated.value = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">true</span>\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> logout() {\n    profile.value = { name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span>, email: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span> }\n    isAuthenticated.value = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">false</span>\n  }\n\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> { profile, isAuthenticated, login, logout }\n})\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Mock Backend</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Create <code>src/mocks/handlers.js</code> with MSW handlers for <code>/api/user</code> and <code>/api/profile</code>.\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script setup&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { rest } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'msw\'</span>\n\nexport <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> handlers = [\n  rest.get(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/api/user\'</span>, (req, res, ctx) => {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> res(ctx.json({ name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Alice\'</span>, email: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'alice@example.com\'</span> }))\n  }),\n  rest.post(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/api/login\'</span>, (req, res, ctx) => {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> { email } = req.body\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> res(ctx.json({ name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Alice\'</span>, email }))\n  })\n]\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>Start MSW in <code>src/main.js</code> before mounting the app.\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Dashboard View</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Build a <code>Dashboard.vue</code> that fetches data on mount and displays a list of items. Use <code>axios</code> to call <code>/api/items</code>.\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;template&gt;\n  &lt;div&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Dashboard&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;ul&gt;\n      &lt;li v-<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;(item, idx) in items&quot;</span> :key=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;idx&quot;</span>&gt;{{ item }}&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;/ul&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/template&gt;\n\n&lt;script setup&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { ref, onMounted } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'vue\'</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> axios <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'axios\'</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> items = ref([])\n\nonMounted(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">async</span> () => {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> { data } = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">await</span> axios.get(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/api/items\'</span>)\n  items.value = data\n})\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Profile Component</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Create a form that allows editing the user profile. Use <code>v-model</code> and computed validation.\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;template&gt;\n  &lt;form @submit.prevent=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;save&quot;</span>&gt;\n    &lt;label&gt;Name:&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input v-model=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;profile.name&quot;</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;text&quot;</span> required&gt;\n    &lt;label&gt;Email:&lt;/label&gt;\n    &lt;input v-model=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;profile.email&quot;</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;email&quot;</span> required&gt;\n    &lt;button <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submit&quot;</span>&gt;Save&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;/template&gt;\n\n&lt;script setup&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { useUserStore } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@/stores/userStore\'</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { computed } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'vue\'</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> userStore = useUserStore()\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> profile = computed(() => userStore.profile)\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> save() {\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Normally send to API</span>\n  console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Saved\'</span>, profile.value)\n}\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Navigation &amp; Layout</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Add a <code>NavBar.vue</code> component with links to Dashboard and Profile using <code>router-link</code>.\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;template&gt;\n  &lt;nav&gt;\n    &lt;router-link to=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;/dashboard&quot;</span>&gt;Dashboard&lt;/router-link&gt;\n    &lt;router-link to=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;/profile&quot;</span>&gt;Profile&lt;/router-link&gt;\n  &lt;/nav&gt;\n&lt;/template&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>Include <code>&lt;NavBar /&gt;</code> in <code>App.vue</code> and wrap <code>&lt;router-view /&gt;</code> in a container.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Styling &amp; Responsiveness</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Use simple CSS Grid to layout the dashboard items and make the form responsive. Add a <code>style</code> block in each component or a global <code>src/assets/styles.css</code>.\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Testing</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Write a basic unit test for <code>Profile.vue</code> that checks if the form renders and the save method logs the correct data.\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script setup&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { mount } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@vue/test-utils\'</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> Profile <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'@/components/Profile.vue\'</span>\n\ndescribe(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Profile\'</span>, () => {\n  it(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'renders form and logs data on submit\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">async</span> () => {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> wrapper = mount(Profile)\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> consoleSpy = jest.spyOn(console, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'log\'</span>)\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">await</span> wrapper.find(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'input\'</span>).setValue(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Bob\'</span>)\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">await</span> wrapper.find(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'form\'</span>).trigger(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'submit.prevent\'</span>)\n    expect(consoleSpy).toHaveBeenCalledWith(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Saved\'</span>, { name: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Bob\'</span>, email: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'\'</span> })\n  })\n})\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Run &amp; Verify</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Start the dev server: <code>npm run dev</code>.\n<li>Open <code>http://localhost:5173</code>, navigate between pages, edit the profile, and ensure data persists in the Pinia store.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Submit a GitHub repository containing the complete Vue.js application, a <code>README.md</code> that explains how to run the project, and a short video (or GIF) demonstrating the navigation, data fetching, and profile editing features.</p>\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Keep components focused: a component should do one thing well.</li>\n<li>Use <code>defineProps</code> and <code>defineEmits</code> for clarity in child components.</li>\n<li>When mocking APIs, keep the handlers in a separate file to avoid clutter.</li>\n<li>Test components in isolation; mock store state if needed.</li>\n<li>Leverage Vue DevTools for inspecting component hierarchy and store state.</li>\n<li>Commit frequently and write meaningful commit messages.</li>\n</ul>', 'Building a Complex Web Application with Vue.js', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(748, 761, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: routing and navigation in a complex web application</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=routing+and+navigation+in+a+complex+web+application\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/routing+and+navigation+in+a+complex+web+application\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/routing+and+navigation+in+a+complex+web+application/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/routing+and+navigation+in+a+complex+web+application/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=routing+and+navigation+in+a+complex+web+application\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h1>Complex Web Application Project: Setting Up Routing and Navigation</h1>\n\n<h3>Task Objective:</h3>\n<p>Today\'s task is to set up routing and navigation in a complex web application using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. You will learn how to create routes, navigate between pages, and handle URL changes.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need:</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>Routing: The process of mapping URLs to specific pages or components in an application.</li>\n    <li>Navigation: The process of moving between different pages or components in an application.</li>\n    <li>Complex Web Application: A web application that has multiple pages, components, and features.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions:</h3>\n<h4>Step 1: Create a Basic HTML Structure</h4>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n    &lt;head&gt;\n        &lt;title&gt;Complex Web Application&lt;/title&gt;\n        &lt;link rel=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;stylesheet&quot;</span> href=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;styles.css&quot;</span>&gt;\n    &lt;/head&gt;\n    &lt;body&gt;\n        &lt;header&gt;\n            &lt;nav&gt;\n                &lt;ul&gt;\n                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;z0z\n                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#&quot;&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n                    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#&quot;&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n                &lt;/ul&gt;\n            &lt;/nav&gt;\n        &lt;/header&gt;\n        &lt;main&gt;\n            &lt;section&gt;\n                &lt;p&gt;This <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> the home page.&lt;/p&gt;\n            &lt;/section&gt;\n        &lt;/main&gt;\n    &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 2: Create Routes</h4>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> routes = {\n    <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/\'</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'home\'</span>,\n    <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/about\'</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'about\'</span>,\n    <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/contact\'</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'contact\'</span>\n};\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> navigate(url) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> currentRoute = window.location.pathname;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (currentRoute === url) {\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span>;\n    }\n    window.history.pushState(<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">null</span>, <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">null</span>, url);\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> currentRouteElement = document.querySelector(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`[data-route=${currentRoute}]`</span>);\n    currentRouteElement.classList.remove(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'active\'</span>);\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> newRouteElement = document.querySelector(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`[data-route=${url}]`</span>);\n    newRouteElement.classList.add(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'active\'</span>);\n}\n</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 3: Add Event Listeners</h4>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> navLinks = document.querySelectorAll(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'nav ul li a\'</span>);\nnavLinks.forEach(link => {\n    link.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'click\'</span>, (e) => {\n        e.preventDefault();\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> url = link.href;\n        navigate(url);\n    });\n});\n</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 4: Handle URL Changes</h4>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">window.addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'popstate\'</span>, () => {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> currentRoute = window.location.pathname;\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> currentRouteElement = document.querySelector(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`[data-route=${currentRoute}]`</span>);\n    currentRouteElement.classList.add(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'active\'</span>);\n});\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable:</h3>\n<p>Complete the task by creating a basic HTML structure, defining routes, adding event listeners, and handling URL changes.</p>\n\n<h3>Tips:</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>Use the `history.pushState` method to change the URL without refreshing the page.</li>\n    <li>Use the `classList` property to add and remove classes from elements.</li>\n    <li>Use the `querySelector` method to select elements based on their data attributes.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'Complex Web Application Project: Setting Up Routing and Navigation', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(749, 762, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: vuex state management</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=vuex+state+management\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/vuex+state+management\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/vuex+state+management/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/vuex+state+management/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=vuex+state+management\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Implementing State Management in Complex Web Applications</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship task, you will learn about state management in complex web applications using Vuex and Axios. State management is a critical aspect of web development that helps to manage the global state of an application.</p>\n<h3>Concepts You Need to Know</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>State Management</li>\n    <li>Complex Web Applications</li>\n    <li>Vuex</li>\n    <li>Axios</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n<h4>Step 1: Setting Up the Project</h4>\n<p>First, create a new Vue.js project using the Vue CLI. If you haven\'t installed Vue CLI on your system, install it by running the following command:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npm install -g @vue/cli</code></pre>\n<p>Then, create a new project by running the following command:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">vue create complex-web-app</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 2: Installing Vuex and Axios</h4>\n<p>Next, install Vuex and Axios in your project by running the following command:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npm install vuex axios</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 3: Creating the Vuex Store</h4>\n<p>Now, create a new file called store.js in the src directory. In this file, import Vuex and create a new Vuex store:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> Vuex <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'vuex\'</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> store = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Vuex.Store({\n    state: {\n        count: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>\n    },\n    mutations: {\n        increment(state) {\n            state.count++\n        }\n    },\n    actions: {\n        incrementAsync({ commit }) {\n            setTimeout(() => {\n                commit(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'increment\'</span>)\n            }, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1000</span>)\n        }\n    }\n})\n\nexport default store</code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 4: Using Vuex in the Component</h4>\n<p>Next, create a new component called Counter.vue in the src/components directory. In this component, import the Vuex store and use it to display the count:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><template>\n    <div>\n        <p>Count: {{ count }}</p>\n        <button @click=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"increment\"</span>>Increment</button>\n        <button @click=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"incrementAsync\"</span>>Increment Async</button>\n    </div>\n</template>\n\n<script>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> { mapState, mapActions } <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'vuex\'</span>\n\nexport default {\n    computed: {\n        ...mapState([<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'count\'</span>])\n    },\n    methods: {\n        ...mapActions([<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'increment\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'incrementAsync\'</span>])\n    }\n}\n</script></code></pre>\n\n<h4>Step 5: Making API Calls with Axios</h4>\n<p>Finally, make API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API. For example, you can use the Axios instance to fetch data from the JSONPlaceholder API:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span> axios <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'axios\'</span>\n\nexport default {\n    data() {\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> {\n            posts: []\n        }\n    },\n    mounted() {\n        axios.get(\'https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts\')</span>\n            .then(response => {\n                <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">this</span>.posts = response.data\n            })\n            .<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">catch</span>(error => {\n                console.error(error)\n            })\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>As a deliverable, you should have a working Vue.js project with Vuex and Axios installed. You should also have implemented state management using Vuex and made API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API.</p>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n    <li>Make sure to install Vuex and Axios correctly in your project.</li>\n    <li>Use the Vuex store to manage the global state of your application.</li>\n    <li>Use Axios to make API calls to external APIs.</li>\n    <li>Test your application thoroughly to ensure that it works as expected.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<p>Here\'s a quiz to test your understanding of state management and Axios:</p>\n<ul>\n    <li>What is state management in web development?</li>\n    <li>How do you install Vuex and Axios in a Vue.js project?</li>\n    <li>How do you use Vuex to manage the global state of an application?</li>\n    <li>How do you make API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API?</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n<p>Here\'s a short search query to find an image related to state management:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">vuex state management</code></pre>\n\n<h3>HTML Content</h3>\n<p>Here\'s the HTML content for this task:</p>\n<pre><code>&lt;h3&gt;Implementing State Management in Complex Web Applications&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;In this hands-on internship task, you will learn about state management in complex web applications using Vuex and Axios. State management is a critical aspect of web development that helps to manage the global state of an application.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Concepts You Need to Know&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;State Management&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Complex Web Applications&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Vuex&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Axios&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Step-by-Step Instructions&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 1: Setting Up the Project&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;First, create a new Vue.js project using the Vue CLI. If you haven\'t installed Vue CLI on your system, install it by running the following command:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install -g @vue/cli&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Then, create a new project by running the following command:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;vue create complex-web-app&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 2: Installing Vuex and Axios&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Next, install Vuex and Axios in your project by running the following command:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install vuex axios&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 3: Creating the Vuex Store&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Now, create a new file called store.js in the src directory. In this file, import Vuex and create a new Vuex store:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;import Vuex from \'vuex\'\n\nconst store = new Vuex.Store({\n    state: {\n        count: 0\n    },\n    mutations: {\n        increment(state) {\n            state.count++\n        }\n    },\n    actions: {\n        incrementAsync({ commit }) {\n            setTimeout(()=&gt; {\n                commit(\'increment\')\n            }, 1000)\n        }\n    }\n})\n\nexport default store&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 4: Using Vuex in the Component&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Next, create a new component called Counter.vue in the src/components directory. In this component, import the Vuex store and use it to display the count:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;template&gt;\n    &lt;div&gt;\n        &lt;p&gt;Count: {{ count }}&lt;/p&gt;\n        &lt;button @click=&quot;increment&quot;&gt;Increment&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;button @click=&quot;incrementAsync&quot;&gt;Increment Async&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/template&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\nimport { mapState, mapActions } from \'vuex\'\n\nexport default {\n    computed: {\n        ...mapState([\'count\'])\n    },\n    methods: {\n        ...mapActions([\'increment\', \'incrementAsync\'])\n    }\n}\n&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 5: Making API Calls with Axios&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Finally, make API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API. For example, you can use the Axios instance to fetch data from the JSONPlaceholder API:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;import axios from \'axios\'\n\nexport default {\n    data() {\n        return {\n            posts: []\n        }\n    },\n    mounted() {\n        axios.get(\'https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts\')\n            .then(response =&gt; {\n                this.posts = response.data\n            })\n            .catch(error =&gt; {\n                console.error(error)\n            })\n    }\n}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Deliverable&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;As a deliverable, you should have a working Vue.js project with Vuex and Axios installed. You should also have implemented state management using Vuex and made API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Tips&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Make sure to install Vuex and Axios correctly in your project.&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Use the Vuex store to manage the global state of your application.&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Use Axios to make API calls to external APIs.&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Test your application thoroughly to ensure that it works as expected.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Quiz&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here\'s a quiz to test your understanding of state management and Axios:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;What is state management in web development?&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;How do you install Vuex and Axios in a Vue.js project?&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;How do you use Vuex to manage the global state of an application?&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;How do you make API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API?&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Image Query&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here\'s a short search query to find an image related to state management:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;vuex state management&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;HTML Content&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here\'s the HTML content for this task:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Implementing State Management in Complex Web Applications&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;In this hands-on internship task, you will learn about state management in complex web applications using Vuex and Axios. State management is a critical aspect of web development that helps to manage the global state of an application.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h3&gt;Concepts You Need to Know&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;State Management&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Complex Web Applications&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Vuex&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Axios&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Step-by-Step Instructions&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 1: Setting Up the Project&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;First, create a new Vue.js project using the Vue CLI. If you haven\'t installed Vue CLI on your system, install it by running the following command:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install -g @vue/cli&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Then, create a new project by running the following command:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;vue create complex-web-app&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 2: Installing Vuex and Axios&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Next, install Vuex and Axios in your project by running the following command:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm install vuex axios&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 3: Creating the Vuex Store&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Now, create a new file called store.js in the src directory. In this file, import Vuex and create a new Vuex store:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;import Vuex from \'vuex\'\n\nconst store = new Vuex.Store({\n    state: {\n        count: 0\n    },\n    mutations: {\n        increment(state) {\n            state.count++\n        }\n    },\n    actions: {\n        incrementAsync({ commit }) {\n            setTimeout(()=&gt; {\n                commit(\'increment\')\n            }, 1000)\n        }\n    }\n})\n\nexport default store&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 4: Using Vuex in the Component&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Next, create a new component called Counter.vue in the src/components directory. In this component, import the Vuex store and use it to display the count:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;template&gt;\n    &lt;div&gt;\n        &lt;p&gt;Count: {{ count }}&lt;/p&gt;\n        &lt;button @click=&quot;increment&quot;&gt;Increment&lt;/button&gt;\n        &lt;button @click=&quot;incrementAsync&quot;&gt;Increment Async&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/template&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\nimport { mapState, mapActions } from \'vuex\'\n\nexport default {\n    computed: {\n        ...mapState([\'count\'])\n    },\n    methods: {\n        ...mapActions([\'increment\', \'incrementAsync\'])\n    }\n}\n&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h4&gt;Step 5: Making API Calls with Axios&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Finally, make API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API. For example, you can use the Axios instance to fetch data from the JSONPlaceholder API:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;import axios from \'axios\'\n\nexport default {\n    data() {\n        return {\n            posts: []\n        }\n    },\n    mounted() {\n        axios.get(\'https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts\')\n            .then(response =&gt; {\n                this.posts = response.data\n            })\n            .catch(error =&gt; {\n                console.error(error)\n            })\n    }\n}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Deliverable&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;As a deliverable, you should have a working Vue.js project with Vuex and Axios installed. You should also have implemented state management using Vuex and made API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Tips&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Make sure to install Vuex and Axios correctly in your project.&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Use the Vuex store to manage the global state of your application.&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Use Axios to make API calls to external APIs.&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;Test your application thoroughly to ensure that it works as expected.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Quiz&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here\'s a quiz to test your understanding of state management and Axios:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;What is state management in web development?&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;How do you install Vuex and Axios in a Vue.js project?&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;How do you use Vuex to manage the global state of an application?&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;How do you make API calls with Axios to fetch data from an external API?&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;Image Query&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here\'s a short search query to find an image related to state management:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;vuex state management&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n&lt;h3&gt;HTML Content&lt;/h3&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here\'s the HTML content for this task:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\n', 'Complex Web Application Project: Implementing State Management', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(750, 763, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: user authentication web application</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=user+authentication+web+application\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/user+authentication+web+application\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/user+authentication+web+application/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/user+authentication+web+application/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=user+authentication+web+application\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Complex Web Application Project: Handling User Authentication</h3>\n<p>In this task, you will learn how to implement user authentication in a complex web application using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. We will cover the basics of authentication, security, and how to handle user sessions.</p>\n<h3>Authentication Basics</h3>\n<p>Authentication is the process of verifying the identity of a user. In a web application, this is typically done by submitting a username and password to the server, which then checks these credentials against a database of known users.</p>\n<h3>Security Considerations</h3>\n<p>When implementing authentication, security is crucial. You should always use HTTPS (SSL/TLS) to encrypt data transmitted between the client and server. Additionally, you should store passwords securely using a password hashing algorithm such as bcrypt or Argon2.</p>\n<h3>User Sessions</h3>\n<p>Once a user is authenticated, you need to store their session data on the server. This can be done using a session management library or by storing data in a database. You should always use a secure method to store session data, such as using a token-based system.</p>\n<h3>HTML Code</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;html&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;User Authentication&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;User Login&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;form&gt;\n      &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;username&quot;</span>&gt;Username:&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;text&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;username&quot;</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;username&quot;</span>&gt;\n      &lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;label <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;password&quot;</span>&gt;Password:&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;password&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;password&quot;</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;password&quot;</span>&gt;\n      &lt;br&gt;\n      &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submit&quot;</span> value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Login&quot;</span>&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>JavaScript Code</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Get the form elements</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> form = document.querySelector(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;form&#39;);</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> usernameInput = document.querySelector(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;#username&#39;);</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> passwordInput = document.querySelector(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;#password&#39;);</span>\n\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Add an event listener to the form</span>\nform.addEventListener(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;submit&#39;, (e) => {</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Prevent the default form submission</span>\n  e.preventDefault();\n\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Get the username and password values</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> username = usernameInput.value;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> password = passwordInput.value;\n\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Send a request to the server to authenticate the user</span>\n  fetch(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;/login&#39;, {</span>\n    method: &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;POST&#39;\",</span>\n    headers: {\n      &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Content-Type&#39;: &#39;application/json&#39;\",</span>\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify({\n      username,\n      password,\n    }),\n  })\n  .then((response) => response.json())\n  .then((data) => {\n    <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// If the user is authenticated, store their session data</span>\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">if</span> (data.authenticated) {\n      localStorage.setItem(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;sessionToken&#39;, data.token);</span>\n    }\n  })\n  .<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">catch</span>((error) => console.error(error));\n});</code></pre>\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<p>What is the primary purpose of authentication in a web application?</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>to store user data</li>\n  <li>to verify the identity of a user</li>\n  <li>to encrypt data transmitted between the client and server</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Answer: <strong>2. to verify the identity of a user</strong></p>\n<h3>Deliverables</h3>\n<p>For this task, you should have created a basic user login form using HTML and CSS. You should also have implemented a JavaScript function to send a request to the server to authenticate the user. Finally, you should have stored the user&#39;s session data in local storage using a secure method.</p>\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<p>For this task, you need to have knowledge of HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and authentication concepts. You should also have an understanding of how to use HTTPS (SSL/TLS) to encrypt data transmitted between the client and server.</p>\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n<p>short search query: user authentication web application</p>\n<h3>Quiz[]</h3>\n<p>[]</p>', 'Complex Web Application Project: Handling User Authentication', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(751, 764, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: complex web application project</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=complex+web+application+project\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/complex+web+application+project\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/complex+web+application+project/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/complex+web+application+project/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=complex+web+application+project\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div>&lt;html&gt;...&lt;/html&gt;', 'Complex Web Application Project: Final Touches and Deployment', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(752, 765, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web application security authentication authorization</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+application+security+authentication+authorization\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+application+security+authentication+authorization\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+application+security+authentication+authorization/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+application+security+authentication+authorization/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+application+security+authentication+authorization\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Implementing Authentication and Authorization in a Complex Web Application</h3>\n\n<p>In this task, you will learn how to implement authentication and authorization in a complex web application using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. You will also cover accessibility features and front-end frameworks.</p>\n\n<h4>Web Security</h4>\n\n<p>Web security is a crucial aspect of any web application. In this task, you will learn how to protect your application from common web security threats such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting (XSS).</p>\n\n<h4>Accessibility</h4>\n\n<p>Accessibility is an essential feature of any web application. In this task, you will learn how to make your application accessible to users with disabilities.</p>\n\n<h4>Front-end Frameworks</h4>\n\n<p>Front-end frameworks such as React and Angular are popular choices for building complex web applications. In this task, you will learn how to use a front-end framework to build a user interface.</p>\n\n<h4>Task Objective</h4>\n\n<p>Your task is to create a simple web application that allows users to log in and view their profile information. The application should have the following features:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Login functionality</li>\n  <li>Profile view functionality</li>\n  <li>Accessibility features</li>\n  <li>Front-end framework integration</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Concepts You Need</h4>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>HTML5</li>\n  <li>CSS3</li>\n  <li>JavaScript</li>\n  <li>Front-end frameworks (React or Angular)</li>\n  <li>Accessibility features (ARIA attributes, screen reader support)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Step-by-Step Instructions</h4>\n\n<ol>\n  <li>Create a new HTML file called <code>index.html</code> and add the following code:</pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=\"en\"&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;meta charset=\"UTF-8\"&gt;\n    &lt;meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Login Application&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;Login Application&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;form&gt;\n      &lt;label for=\"username\"&gt;Username:&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=\"text\" id=\"username\" name=\"username\"&gt;\n      &lt;label for=\"password\"&gt;Password:&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=\"password\" id=\"password\" name=\"password\"&gt;\n      &lt;button type=\"submit\"&gt;Login&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n</code></pre>\n  <li>Create a new JavaScript file called <code>script.js</code> and add the following code:</pre><code>const form = document.querySelector(\'form\');\nform.addEventListener(\'submit\', (e) =&gt; {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  const username = document.querySelector(\'#username\').value;\n  const password = document.querySelector(\'#password\').value;\n  // Call API to authenticate user\n  fetch(\'/api/login\', {\n    method: \'POST\',\n    headers: {\n      \'Content-Type\': \'application/json\',\n    },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }),\n  })\n    .then((response) =&gt; response.json())\n    .then((data) =&gt; {\n      if (data.success) {\n        // Redirect user to profile page\n        window.location.href = \'/profile\';\n      } else {\n        alert(\'Invalid username or password\');\n      }\n    })\n    .catch((error) =&gt; console.error(error));\n});\n</code></pre>\n  <li>Create a new CSS file called <code>styles.css</code> and add the following code:</pre><code>body {\n  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n  background-color: #f0f0f0;\n}\n\nform {\n  width: 300px;\n  margin: 40px auto;\n  padding: 20px;\n  border: 1px solid #ccc;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n}\n\nlabel {\n  display: block;\n  margin-bottom: 10px;\n}\n\ninput[type=\"text\"], input[type=\"password\"] {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 40px;\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\n  padding: 10px;\n  border: 1px solid #ccc;\n  border-radius: 5px;\n}\n\nbutton[type=\"submit\"] {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 40px;\n  background-color: #4CAF50;\n  color: #fff;\n  padding: 10px;\n  border: none;\n  border-radius: 5px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\nbutton[type=\"submit\"]:hover {\n  background-color: #3e8e41;\n}\n</code></pre>\n  <li>Create a new React component called <code>Login.js</code> and add the following code:</pre><code>import React, { useState } from \'react\';\n\nconst Login = () =&gt; {\n  const [username, setUsername] = useState(\'\');\n  const [password, setPassword] = useState(\'\');\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\n\n  const handleSubmit = (e) =&gt; {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    // Call API to authenticate user\n    fetch(\'/api/login\', {\n      method: \'POST\',\n      headers: {\n        \'Content-Type\': \'application/json\',\n      },\n      body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }),\n    })\n      .then((response) =&gt; response.json())\n      .then((data) =&gt; {\n        if (data.success) {\n          // Redirect user to profile page\n          window.location.href = \'/profile\';\n        } else {\n          setError(\'Invalid username or password\');\n        }\n      })\n      .catch((error) =&gt; console.error(error));\n  };\n\n  return (\n    &lt;form onSubmit={handleSubmit}&gt;\n      &lt;label&gt;Username:&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=\"text\" value={username} onChange={(e) =&gt; setUsername(e.target.value)} /&gt;\n      &lt;label&gt;Password:&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input type=\"password\" value={password} onChange={(e) =&gt; setPassword(e.target.value)} /&gt;\n      &lt;button type=\"submit\"&gt;Login&lt;/button&gt;\n      {error && &lt;p style={{ color: \'red\' }}&gt;{error}&lt;/p&gt;}\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n  );\n};\n\nexport default Login;\n</code></pre>\n  <li>Integrate the React component into your application by adding the following code to your <code>App.js</code> file:</pre><code>import React from \'react\';\nimport Login from \'./Login\';\n\nconst App = () =&gt; {\n  return (\n    &lt;div&gt;\n      &lt;Login /&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  );\n};\n\nexport default App;\n</code></pre>\n</ol>\n\n<h4>Deliverable</h4>\n\n<p>Deliver the following files:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><code>index.html</code></li>\n  <li><code>script.js</code></li>\n  <li><code>styles.css</code></li>\n  <li><code>Login.js</code></li>\n  <li><code>App.js</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Tips</h4>\n\n<p>Here are some tips to help you complete this task:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Make sure to handle errors properly by checking the response from the API.</li>\n  <li>Use a front-end framework to build your user interface.</li>\n  <li>Implement accessibility features such as ARIA attributes and screen reader support.</li>\n  <li>Test your application thoroughly to ensure it works as expected.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4>Quiz</h4>\n\n<p>What is the purpose of the <code>fetch</code> function in JavaScript?</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>To send a request to a server</li>\n  <li>To receive data from a server</li>\n  <li>To update the DOM</li>\n  <li>To handle events</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Answer: <code>1</code></p>\n\n<h4>Image Query</h4>\n\n<p>What is the best way to handle user authentication in a web application?</p>\n\n<p>Answer: Implementing authentication using a secure protocol such as OAuth or JWT.</p>\n\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n\n<p>In this task, you learned how to implement authentication and authorization in a complex web application using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. You also covered accessibility features and front-end frameworks.</p>\n\n<p>Remember to handle errors properly, use a front-end framework to build your user interface, implement accessibility features, and test your application thoroughly.</p>\n\n<p>Good luck with your next task!</p>', 'Complex Web Application Project: Implementing Authentication and Authorization', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(753, 766, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: secure web form validation accessibility react</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=secure+web+form+validation+accessibility+react\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/secure+web+form+validation+accessibility+react\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/secure+web+form+validation+accessibility+react/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/secure+web+form+validation+accessibility+react/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=secure+web+form+validation+accessibility+react\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Build a secure and accessible web form using a front-end framework (e.g., React or Vue) that implements robust input validation, sanitization, and follows web security best practices. The form should include real-time client-side validation, prevent common vulnerabilities like XSS, and meet WCAG accessibility standards.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Input Validation:</strong> Techniques to verify user input format, length, and type using HTML5 attributes, JavaScript, and server-side checks</li><li><strong>Secure Coding:</strong> Sanitizing user input to prevent XSS, using Content Security Policy (CSP) headers, and avoiding security pitfalls</li><li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Implementing ARIA attributes, semantic HTML, and keyboard navigation for screen readers</li><li><strong>Front-end Frameworks:</strong> Using React/Vue for form state management and validation</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><ol><li>Create a new React project using <code>npx create-react-app secure-form</code></li><li>Build a registration form with fields: username, email, password, and confirm password</li><li>Implement client-side validation:<ul><li>Use HTML5 attributes: <code>required</code>, <code>pattern</code>, <code>minLength</code></li><li>Add JavaScript validation for password strength and field matching</li></ul></li><li>Secure the form:<ul><li>Escape user input before displaying it</li><li>Add CSP meta tag: <code>&lt;meta http-equiv=\"Content-Security-Policy\" content=\"default-src \'self\'\"&gt;</code></li></ul></li><li>Make it accessible:<ul><li>Add <code>aria-label</code> and <code>aria-describedby</code> attributes</li><li>Use semantic elements: <code>&lt;form&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code></li></ul></li><li>Test with Lighthouse for accessibility and security audits</li></ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a GitHub repository containing:</p><ul><li>React/Vue form implementation with validation</li><li>Server-side validation (Node.js/Express) for input sanitization</li><li>Lighthouse accessibility audit report</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Example Code</h3><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;form onSubmit={handleSubmit}&gt;\n  &lt;label&gt;\n    Username:\n    &lt;input\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"text\"</span>\n      value={username}\n      onChange={(e) =&gt; setUsername(e.target.value)}\n      pattern=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"[a-zA-Z0-9_]{3,20}\"</span>\n      required\n      aria-describedby=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"username-help\"</span>\n    /&gt;\n    &lt;span id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"username-help\"</span>><span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">20</span> alphanumeric characters&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;button <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=\"submit&quot; disabled={isInvalid}&gt;Register&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Server-side sanitization (Express)</span>\napp.post(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'/register\'</span>, (req, res) =&gt; {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> sanitizedUsername = DOMPurify.sanitize(req.body.username);\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Store in database</span>\n});</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Always validate on both client and server sides</li><li>Use libraries like <code>DOMPurify</code> for HTML sanitization</li><li>Set HTTP headers: <code>X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>, <code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code></li><li>Test forms with OWASP ZAP for security vulnerabilities</li></ul>', 'Web Security Best Practices: Input Validation and Secure Coding', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(754, 767, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: Web accessibility ARIA screen reader support</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=Web+accessibility+ARIA+screen+reader+support\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/Web+accessibility+ARIA+screen+reader+support\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/Web+accessibility+ARIA+screen+reader+support/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/Web+accessibility+ARIA+screen+reader+support/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=Web+accessibility+ARIA+screen+reader+support\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Implement web accessibility standards by applying ARIA attributes and testing screen reader compatibility while ensuring secure practices in front-end development.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>ARIA (Accessible Rich Internet Applications)</strong>: Use roles, states, and properties to enhance accessibility for dynamic content.</li><li><strong>Screen Reader Support</strong>: Ensure non-visual users can interact with your web content using tools like NVDA or VoiceOver.</li><li><strong>Semantic HTML</strong>: Use native elements (e.g., <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>) to reduce reliance on ARIA.</li><li><strong>Web Security</strong>: Avoid XSS vulnerabilities when dynamically setting ARIA attributes.</li><li><strong>Front-End Frameworks</strong>: Apply accessibility practices in React, Vue, or Angular components.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><ol><li><strong>Create a Semantic Base</strong>: Build a form with native HTML elements.<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;form id=\"contact-form<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;label for=\"name&quot;</span>&gt;Name:&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"text\"</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"name\"</span> required&gt;\n  &lt;button <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=\"submit&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre></li><li><strong>Add ARIA Attributes</strong>: Enhance custom components with roles and labels.<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div role=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"button\"</span> tabindex=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"0\"</span> aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Close\"</span> onclick=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"closeModal()\"</span>>X&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre><p>Use <code>aria-describedby</code> for error messages:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"email\"</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"email\"</span> aria-describedby=\"email-error&quot;&gt;\n&lt;p id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"email-error\"</span> style=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"color:red;\"</span>&gt;Valid email required&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre></li><li><strong>Test with Screen Readers</strong>: Use VoiceOver (Mac) or NVDA (Windows) to verify announcements. For example, test if the <code>aria-live</code> region updates dynamically:<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div aria-live=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"polite\"</span> id=\"status&quot;&gt;Loading...&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre></li><li><strong>Secure Dynamic ARIA</strong>: Sanitize user input when injecting ARIA attributes in JavaScript.<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> userInput = escape(userInput); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Prevent XSS</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> element = document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'dynamic\'</span>);\nelement.setAttribute(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'aria-label\'</span>, userInput);</code></pre></li><li><strong>Framework Integration</strong>: In React, use <code>aria-</code> props directly or with libraries like <code>react-aria</code>. Example:<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;button aria-expanded={isOpen} onClick={toggleMenu}&gt;\n  Menu\n&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre></li></ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><ul><li>A working HTML form with ARIA attributes and screen reader testing results.</li><li>A short report (100-200 words) explaining how you validated accessibility and security practices.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>aria-hidden=\"true&quot;</code> to hide decorative elements from screen readers.</li><li>Avoid <code>role=\"presentation&quot;</code> for non-interactive elements to reduce cognitive load.</li><li>Test with <code>tabindex</code> values to ensure keyboard navigation works.</li><li>For security, always sanitize user-generated ARIA labels to prevent XSS attacks.</li></ul>', 'Web Accessibility Guidelines: Implementing ARIA Attributes and Screen Reader Support', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(755, 768, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web performance optimization caching minification compression</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Optimize a web application\'s performance by implementing caching strategies, minifying assets, and enabling compression. Integrate security headers and ensure accessibility compliance while using a front-end framework for efficient development.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Caching:</strong> Use browser and CDN caching to reduce server load and improve load times.</li><li><strong>Minification:</strong> Remove unnecessary characters (spaces, comments) from HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files.</li><li><strong>Compression:</strong> Enable Gzip or Brotli compression to reduce file sizes during transmission.</li><li><strong>Web Security:</strong> Add security headers like <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> to mitigate vulnerabilities.</li><li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Ensure optimized resources do not break screen readers or keyboard navigation.</li><li><strong>Front-end Frameworks:</strong> Use tools like React or Vue CLI to automate minification and bundling.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><ol><li><strong>Create a baseline project:</strong>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;html&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Optimized App&lt;/title&gt;\n    &lt;link rel=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"stylesheet\"</span> href=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"styles.css\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h1&gt;Welcome to My App&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;script src=\"app.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>Implement caching:</strong> Add HTTP headers to your server configuration:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">Cache-Control: <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">public</span>, max-age=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">31536000</span>, immutable\nContent-Security-Policy: default-src <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'self\'</span>; script-src <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'self\'</span> https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//cdn.example.com;</span></code></pre>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Minify assets:</strong> Use <code>html-minifier</code> for HTML, <code>cleancss</code> for CSS, and <code>uglify-js</code> for JavaScript:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npx html-minifier <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">--collapse-whitespace index.html -o index-min.html</span>\nnpx cleancss styles.css -o styles-min.css\nnpx uglifyjs app.js -o app-min.js</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>Enable compression:</strong> Configure your server (e.g., Nginx) to use Brotli:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">location ~ \\.(js|css)$ {\n  gzip on;\n  brotli on;\n  add_header Content-Encoding br;\n}</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>Enhance security:</strong> Add headers to prevent XSS and MIME-type sniffing:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">Content-Security-Policy: script-src <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'self\'</span> <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'unsafe-inline\'</span>;\nX-Content-Type-Options: nosniff;</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>Ensure accessibility:</strong> Validate that minification does not remove ARIA attributes or <code>alt</code> texts. Use <code>semantic-ui</code> for accessible components:</n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;button aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Close\"</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"ui icon button\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;i <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=\"close icon&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;\n&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>Use a front-end framework:</strong> Create a React app with optimized build settings:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npx create-react-app optimized-app\nnpm run build</code></pre>\nCheck the <code>build</code> folder for minified and bundled files.</li></ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a ZIP file containing:</p><ul><li>A working web app with all optimizations applied.</li><li>A <code>README.md</code> explaining how caching, minification, and compression improve performance.</li><li>Screenshots of Chrome DevTools\' <em>Network</em> tab showing reduced file sizes and cached resources.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>curl -I https://your-app.com</code> to verify HTTP headers.</li><li>Test accessibility with <code>axe DevTools</code> after optimization.</li><li>Compare load times before and after optimization using Lighthouse in Chrome DevTools.</li></ul>', 'Web Application Performance Optimization: Caching, Minification, and Compression', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(756, 769, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web app security accessibility design</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+app+security+accessibility+design\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+app+security+accessibility+design\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+app+security+accessibility+design/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+app+security+accessibility+design/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+app+security+accessibility+design\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Today’s task focuses on refining a complex web application by implementing UI/UX improvements, ensuring accessibility compliance, and adding security measures. You will also test the application for usability and performance.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Web Security:</strong> Implement HTTP security headers (e.g., <code>X-Content-Type-Options</code>, <code>Content-Security-Policy</code>).</li><li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Add ARIA attributes, semantic HTML, and keyboard navigation support.</li><li><strong>Front-end Frameworks:</strong> Use React or Vue.js to create reusable UI components and optimize rendering.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><ol><li><strong>Add Security Headers</strong><p>Update your server configuration to include security headers. For example, in an <code>.htaccess</code> file:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;IfModule mod_headers.c&gt;\n  Header set X-Content-Type-Options <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;nosniff&quot;</span>\n  Header set Content-Security-Policy &quot;default-src <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'self\'</span>; script-src <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'self\'</span> https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//trusted-cdn.com&quot;</span>\n&lt;/IfModule&gt;</code></pre></li>\n\n<li><strong>Improve Accessibility</strong><p>Enhance accessibility using semantic HTML and ARIA roles. Example:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;nav aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Main Navigation\"</span> role=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"navigation\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#home\" tabindex=\"0&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=\"<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#about\" tabindex=\"0&quot;&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</span>\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/nav&gt;</code></pre><p>Test keyboard navigation by tabbing through interactive elements.</p></li>\n\n<li><strong>Build a Reusable Component</strong><p>Create a React component for a form input with validation:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> TextInput({ label, value, onChange }) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;div className=\"form-group&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;label&gt;{label}&lt;/label&gt;\n      &lt;input\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"text\"</span>\n        value={value}\n        onChange={onChange}\n        aria-required=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"true\"</span>\n      /&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  );\n}</code></pre></li>\n\n<li><strong>Test UI/UX with Tools</strong><p>Run audits using Chrome DevTools Lighthouse for accessibility and performance. Example command for automated testing:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npx lighthouse http:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//localhost:3000 --view</span></code></pre><p>Fix issues like low contrast ratios or missing alt text.</p></li>\n\n<li><strong>Conduct Manual Usability Testing</strong><p>Invite peers to test the application. Document feedback on navigation flow, responsiveness, and error messages.</p></li></ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><ul><li>Updated code with security headers, accessibility fixes, and framework components.</li><li>A report summarizing test results and improvements made (e.g., &quot;Contrast ratio improved from 3:1 to 4.5:1&quot;).</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>role=\"alert&quot;</code> for dynamic error messages to notify screen readers.</li><li>Validate security headers with <a href=\"https://securityheaders.com/\">securityheaders.com</a>.</li><li>Use <code>tabindex=\"-1&quot;</code> to manage focus traps in modal dialogs.</li></ul>', 'Final Touches on the Complex Web Application: UI/UX Design and Testing', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(757, 770, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web application project review and feedback</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+application+project+review+and+feedback\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+application+project+review+and+feedback\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+application+project+review+and+feedback/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+application+project+review+and+feedback/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+application+project+review+and+feedback\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Today’s task focuses on reviewing a complex web application project for <strong>web security vulnerabilities</strong>, <strong>accessibility compliance</strong>, and <strong>best practices in front-end frameworks</strong>. You will analyze existing code, identify improvements, and document actionable feedback.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><p>Before starting, ensure you understand:</p><ul><li><strong>Web Security:</strong> Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF), input validation, and secure HTTP headers.</li><li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Semantic HTML, ARIA roles, keyboard navigation, and contrast ratios.</li><li><strong>Front-End Frameworks:</strong> Component structure, state management, and performance optimization in frameworks like React, Vue, or Angular.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><p>Follow these steps to conduct a thorough review:</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li><h4>Review for Web Security</h4><p>Inspect the application for common vulnerabilities:</p><ul><li>Check if user inputs are sanitized. For example, ensure user-submitted data is escaped before rendering:</li></ul><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;!<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">-- Example: Escaping user input in a template --&gt;</span>\n&lt;p&gt;User message: {{ userMessage | escape }}&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre><p>Verify that CSRF tokens are used for forms and API requests:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;form method=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"POST\"</span> action=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"/submit\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"hidden\"</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"csrf_token\"</span> value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"{{ generate_csrf_token() }}\"</span> /&gt;\n  &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"text\"</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"data\"</span> /&gt;\n  &lt;button <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"submit\"</span>>Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre></li>\n\n<li><h4>Test Accessibility</h4><p>Use tools like <code>axe</code> or browser Lighthouse audits. Manually verify:</p><ul><li>Semantic HTML usage (e.g., <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>).</li><li>ARIA roles for dynamic content:</li></ul><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div role=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"alert\"</span> aria-live=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"assertive\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Your form has been submitted successfully.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre><p>Ensure keyboard navigation works for all interactive elements:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;button tabindex=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"0\"</span> onkeypress=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"handleKeyPress()\"</span>>Click Me&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre></li>\n\n<li><h4>Analyze Front-End Framework Usage</h4><p>For frameworks like React, check component structure and state management:</p><ul><li>Avoid prop drilling by using context or state management libraries:</li></ul><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> UserContext = React.createContext();\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> App() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;UserContext.Provider value={user}&gt;\n      &lt;ChildComponent /&gt;\n    &lt;/UserContext.Provider&gt;\n  );\n}</code></pre><p>Optimize performance with lazy loading:</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> LazyComponent = React.lazy(() =&gt; <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">import</span>(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'./LazyComponent\'</span>));\n\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> App() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;React.Suspense fallback=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Loading...\"</span>&gt;\n      &lt;LazyComponent /&gt;\n    &lt;/React.Suspense&gt;\n  );\n}</code></pre></li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a <strong>review report</strong> (500–700 words) including:</p><ul><li>A summary of security, accessibility, and framework improvements.</li><li>Code snippets demonstrating fixes (e.g., sanitized inputs, ARIA attributes).</li><li>Recommendations for tools (e.g., ESLint for accessibility, Helmet for security headers).</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><p><strong>Security:</strong> Use OWASP ZAP for automated vulnerability scanning. <strong>Accessibility:</strong> Test with screen readers like NVDA or VoiceOver. <strong>Frameworks:</strong> Leverage linters to enforce component naming and structure conventions.</p>', 'Project Review and Feedback: Complex Web Application', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(758, 771, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web security accessibility frameworks</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+security+accessibility+frameworks\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+security+accessibility+frameworks\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+security+accessibility+frameworks/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+security+accessibility+frameworks/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+security+accessibility+frameworks\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Day 77: Project Submission and Next Steps: Final Capstone Project Preparation</h3>\n<p><strong>Task Objective:</strong> Prepare a secure, accessible, and responsive final project using a front-end framework, incorporating best practices in web development.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Web Security:</strong> Implement HTTPS, sanitize user inputs, and use secure headers.</li>\n  <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Add ARIA roles, semantic HTML, and keyboard navigation.</li>\n  <li><strong>Front-end Frameworks:</strong> Build components using React, Vue, or Angular.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Secure Your Project:</strong>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Ensure all API calls use HTTPS. Example:</li>\n      <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\nfetch(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;https://api.example.com/data&#39;)</span>\n  .then(response =&gt; response.json())\n  .then(data =&gt; console.log(data));\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>\n      <li>Add HTTP headers to prevent XSS. Example:</li>\n      <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">Content-Security-Policy: default-src &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;self&#39;;</span></code></pre>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Improve Accessibility:</strong>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Use semantic tags like <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>.</li>\n      <li>Add ARIA roles for dynamic content. Example:</li>\n      <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div role=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;alert&quot;</span> aria-live=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;assertive&quot;</span>&gt;Form submitted successfully!&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>\n      <li>Provide descriptive <code>alt</code> text for images:</li>\n      <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;img src=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;logo.png&quot;</span> alt=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Company logo&quot;</span> /&gt;</code></pre>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Build with a Front-end Framework:</strong>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Create a React component for a form:</li>\n      <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> LoginForm() {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> [username, setUsername] = useState(&<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;&#39;);</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> (\n    &lt;form&gt;\n      &lt;input\n        <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;text&quot;</span>\n        value={username}\n        onChange={(e) =&gt; setUsername(e.target.value)}\n      /&gt;\n      &lt;button <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submit&quot;</span>&gt;Login&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/form&gt;\n  );\n}</code></pre>\n      <li>Use Vue.js for dynamic content:</li>\n      <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;template&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;{{ message }}&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/template&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\nexport default {\n  data() {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> { message: &<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#39;Hello, Vue!&#39; };</span>\n  }\n};\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Test and Optimize:</strong>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Run Lighthouse in Chrome DevTools for accessibility and performance.</li>\n      <li>Validate HTML using the W3C Markup Validator.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Submit a ZIP file containing:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>HTML/CSS/JS files with security and accessibility fixes.</li>\n  <li>A short README explaining your security choices and framework usage.</li>\n  <li>A screenshot of Lighthouse accessibility score (minimum 90/100).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>Use <code>&lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1&quot;&gt;</code> for responsive design.</li>\n  <li>Test keyboard navigation by disabling your mouse.</li>\n  <li>For React, use <code>npm run build</code> to optimize production code.</li>\n</ul>', 'Project Submission and Next Steps: Final Capstone Project Preparation', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(759, 772, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web performance optimization tools</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+performance+optimization+tools\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+performance+optimization+tools\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+performance+optimization+tools/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+performance+optimization+tools/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+performance+optimization+tools\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3>\n<p>By the end of this day you will understand how to identify performance bottlenecks in a web page, use industry‑standard tools to measure them, and apply basic best‑practices to improve load times and responsiveness. You will also produce a short report that documents the findings and the steps you took to optimize the page.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Web Performance Metrics</strong> – First Contentful Paint (FCP), Largest Contentful Paint (LCP), Total Blocking Time (TBT), Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS), and Time to Interactive (TTI).</li>\n<li><strong>Performance Auditing Tools</strong> – Chrome DevTools Performance panel, Lighthouse, WebPageTest, GTmetrix, and the PageSpeed Insights API.</li>\n<li><strong>Optimization Techniques</strong> – Resource minification, compression (gzip/ Brotli), HTTP/2 multiplexing, caching headers, image optimization, lazy loading, and code splitting.</li>\n<li><strong>Browser Performance API</strong> – <code>performance.timing</code>, <code>performance.getEntriesByType(\"resource\")</code>, and <code>performance.mark</code> for custom measurements.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step‑by‑Step Instructions</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Choose a Sample Page</strong>\n<p>Select a simple public website or create a minimal HTML page that loads a few images, CSS files, and a JavaScript bundle. Save the file as <code>index.html</code> and open it in Chrome.</p></li>\n<li><strong>Run a Baseline Audit with Lighthouse</strong>\n<p>Open Chrome DevTools (F12), go to the <code>Lighthouse</code> tab, choose the <strong>Performance</strong> category, and click <strong>Generate report</strong>. Note the scores for FCP, LCP, TBT, CLS, and TTI. Copy the numeric values into a text file for later comparison.</p></li>\n<li><strong>Analyze the Performance Panel</strong>\n<p>Navigate to the <code>Performance</code> tab, click <code>Record</code>, reload the page, and stop recording after the page stabilizes. Inspect the flame chart and the <code>Network</code> sub‑tab to identify long tasks, large resource downloads, and render‑blocking scripts.</p></li>\n<li><strong>Identify Bottlenecks</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Look for resources that take >200 ms to download.</li>\n<li>Check for render‑blocking CSS/JS that prevents the browser from painting early.</li>\n<li>Spot large images that could be compressed or resized.</li>\n<li>Verify that the server is serving compressed content (gzip/Brotli).</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Apply Basic Optimizations</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preload critical resources</strong> – Add <code>&lt;link rel=\"preload\" as=\"style\" href=\"style.css\"&gt;</code> in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> for the main stylesheet.</li>\n<li><strong>Defer non‑essential JavaScript</strong> – Change <code>&lt;script src=\"app.js\"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code> to <code>&lt;script src=\"app.js\" defer&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Lazy‑load images</strong> – Replace <code>&lt;img src=\"photo.jpg\"&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"photo.jpg\"&gt;</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Compress images</strong> – Use a tool like <code>imagemin</code> or an online compressor to reduce file size while keeping quality.</li>\n<li><strong>Enable caching headers</strong> – Add <code>Cache‑Control: public, max-age=31536000</code> for static assets in your server configuration.</li>\n<li><strong>Minify CSS/JS</strong> – Run <code>uglifyjs</code> or <code>cssnano</code> on your bundles.</li>\n</ul></li>\n<li><strong>Re‑audit the Page</strong>\n<p>Repeat the Lighthouse audit and compare the new scores with the baseline. Record the improvements in a table.</p></li>\n<li><strong>Use the Performance API for Custom Metrics</strong>\n<p>Add the following snippet to the page to log the time taken to load the main image:</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\n  performance.mark(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'image-start\'</span>);\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> img = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">new</span> Image();\n  img.src = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'photo.jpg\'</span>;\n  img.onload = () =&gt; {\n    performance.mark(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'image-end\'</span>);\n    performance.measure(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Image Load Time\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'image-start\'</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'image-end\'</span>);\n    console.log(performance.getEntriesByName(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'Image Load Time\'</span>)[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>].duration + <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\' ms\'</span>);\n  };\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<li><strong>Document Your Findings</strong>\n<p>Create a markdown or plain text report that includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial Lighthouse scores.</li>\n<li>Key bottlenecks identified.</li>\n<li>Optimizations applied.</li>\n<li>Post‑optimization Lighthouse scores.</li>\n<li>Custom metric results from the Performance API.</li>\n<li>Recommendations for further improvements.</li>\n</ul></li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Submit the following files:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>index.html</code> – the optimized page.</li>\n<li><code>report.txt</code> – the performance audit comparison and explanation.</li>\n<li><code>performance.log</code> – console output from the custom Performance API script.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Always run audits on a fresh browser session to avoid cached data skewing results.</li>\n<li>Use the <strong>Network Conditions</strong> panel in DevTools to simulate slower connections (e.g., 3G) and see how your page behaves.</li>\n<li>When adding <code>preload</code> tags, ensure you specify the correct <code>as</code> attribute (e.g., <code>as=\"style\"</code> for CSS).</li>\n<li>Lazy loading works best for images that are not immediately visible in the viewport. Use <code>loading=\"lazy\"</code> on all non‑hero images.</li>\n<li>For JavaScript, consider splitting large bundles with dynamic imports so that only the code needed for the initial view is loaded first.</li>\n<li>Always test after each change; small tweaks can have a big impact on metrics like CLS.</li>\n<li>Keep an eye on <strong>Time to Interactive</strong> – it reflects how quickly the page becomes usable, not just how fast it renders.</li>\n</ul>', 'Introduction to Web Performance Optimization Tools', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(760, 773, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web vitals metrics performance optimization</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+vitals+metrics+performance+optimization\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+vitals+metrics+performance+optimization\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+vitals+metrics+performance+optimization/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+vitals+metrics+performance+optimization/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+vitals+metrics+performance+optimization\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><html>\n  <head>\n    <title>Web Vitals Metrics for Performance Optimization</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <h3>Introduction to Web Vitals Metrics</h3>\n    <p>Web Vitals is a set of metrics that measure the user experience of a web page. It includes metrics such as page load time, first contentful paint, and largest contentful paint. In this task, we will learn how to implement these metrics and optimize the performance of our web page.</p>\n    \n    <h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Page Load Time</li>\n      <li>First Contentful Paint (FCP)</li>\n      <li>Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)</li>\n      <li>First Input Delay (FID)</li>\n      <li>Time to Interactive (TTI)</li>\n      <li>Speed Index</li>\n    </ul>\n    \n    <h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n    <ol>\n      <li><strong>Step 1: Measure Page Load Time</strong>\n        <p>Page load time is the time it takes for a web page to fully load. We can measure it using the <code>performance.now()</code> function in JavaScript.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> startTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// code that loads the page</span>\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> endTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> pageLoadTime = endTime - startTime;\n          console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Page load time: ${pageLoadTime}ms`</span>);\n        </code></pre>\n      </li>\n      \n      <li><strong>Step 2: Measure First Contentful Paint (FCP)</strong>\n        <p>FCP is the time it takes for the first content to be painted on the screen. We can measure it using the <code>performance.now()</code> function in JavaScript and the <code>paintWorklet</code> API.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> startTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// code that paints the first content</span>\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> endTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> fcp = endTime - startTime;\n          console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`First Contentful Paint: ${fcp}ms`</span>);\n        </code></pre>\n      </li>\n      \n      <li><strong>Step 3: Measure Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)</strong>\n        <p>LCP is the time it takes for the largest content to be painted on the screen. We can measure it using the <code>performance.now()</code> function in JavaScript and the <code>paintWorklet</code> API.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> startTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// code that paints the largest content</span>\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> endTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> lcp = endTime - startTime;\n          console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Largest Contentful Paint: ${lcp}ms`</span>);\n        </code></pre>\n      </li>\n      \n      <li><strong>Step 4: Measure First Input Delay (FID)</strong>\n        <p>FID is the time it takes for the user to interact with the page after the page has loaded. We can measure it using the <code>performance.now()</code> function in JavaScript and the <code>requestIdleCallback</code> API.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> startTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// code that loads the page</span>\n          requestIdleCallback(() => {\n            <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> endTime = performance.now();\n            <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> fid = endTime - startTime;\n            console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`First Input Delay: ${fid}ms`</span>);\n          });\n        </code></pre>\n      </li>\n      \n      <li><strong>Step 5: Measure Time to Interactive (TTI)</strong>\n        <p>TTI is the time it takes for the page to become interactive. We can measure it using the <code>performance.now()</code> function in JavaScript and the <code>requestIdleCallback</code> API.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> startTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// code that loads the page</span>\n          requestIdleCallback(() => {\n            <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> endTime = performance.now();\n            <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> tti = endTime - startTime;\n            console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Time to Interactive: ${tti}ms`</span>);\n          });\n        </code></pre>\n      </li>\n      \n      <li><strong>Step 6: Measure Speed Index</strong>\n        <p>Speed Index is a measure of how quickly a page\'s content is visible to users. We can measure it using the <code>performance.now()</code> function in JavaScript and the <code>speed-index</code> library.</p>\n        <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> speedIndex = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">require</span>(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'speed-index\'</span>);\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> startTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// code that loads the page</span>\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> endTime = performance.now();\n          <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> speedIndexValue = speedIndex(startTime, endTime);\n          console.log(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">`Speed Index: ${speedIndexValue}ms`</span>);\n        </code></pre>\n      </li>\n    </ol>\n    \n    <h3>Deliverable</h3>\n    <p>Implement all the metrics mentioned above and measure their values in a web page.</p>\n    \n    <h3>Quiz</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>What is the purpose of Web Vitals metrics?</li>\n      <li>How do you measure page load time?</li>\n      <li>What is the difference between FCP and LCP?</li>\n      <li>How do you measure FID and TTI?</li>\n      <li>What is Speed Index and how do you measure it?</li>\n    </ul>\n  </body>\n</html>', 'Implementing Web Vitals Metrics for Performance Optimization', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(761, 774, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web performance optimization caching minification compression</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+performance+optimization+caching+minification+compression\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Web Performance Optimization: Caching, Minification, and Compression</h3>\n\n<p>As a web developer, it\'s essential to optimize the performance of your website to ensure a smooth user experience. In this task, we\'ll focus on three key techniques: caching, minification, and compression.</p>\n\n<h3>Caching</h3>\n\n<p>Caching is the process of storing frequently-used data in a temporary location, such as a user\'s browser or a proxy server, to reduce the time it takes to retrieve that data. This can significantly improve the performance of your website.</p>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Example of caching using the Cache API</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> cache = caches.open(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'my-cache\'</span>);\ncache.addAll([\n  \'https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//example.com/style.css\',</span>\n  \'https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//example.com/script.js\',</span>\n]);\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Minification</h3>\n\n<p>Minification is the process of removing unnecessary characters from your code, such as whitespace and comments, to reduce its size and improve loading times.</p>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Example of minification using the UglifyJS library</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> uglify = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">require</span>(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'uglify-js\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> code = `\n  <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// This is a sample function</span>\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> add(a, b) {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> a + b;\n  }\n`;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> minifiedCode = uglify.minify(code).code;\nconsole.log(minifiedCode);\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Compression</h3>\n\n<p>Compression is the process of reducing the size of your files by representing them in a more compact form. This can be achieved using algorithms like Gzip or Brotli.</p>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Example of compression using the zlib library</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> zlib = <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">require</span>(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'zlib\'</span>);\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> data = <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'This is a sample string\'</span>;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> compressedData = zlib.deflateSync(data);\nconsole.log(compressedData);\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Example Use Case</h3>\n\n<p>Let\'s say we have a website that loads 10 different JavaScript files, each weighing around 100KB. By applying minification and compression to these files, we can reduce their size to around 50KB each, resulting in a total size reduction of 50%.</p>\n\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Example of loading compressed and minified files</span>\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> script = document.createElement(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\'script\'</span>);\nscript.src = \'https:<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">//example.com/script.min.js.gz\';</span>\ndocument.head.appendChild(script);\n&lt;/script&gt;\n</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n\n<p>In conclusion, caching, minification, and compression are essential techniques for optimizing the performance of your website. By applying these techniques, you can significantly improve the loading times and user experience of your website.</p>\n\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n\n<p>What is the main purpose of caching in web development?</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Reducing the size of files</li>\n  <li>Improving loading times</li>\n  <li>Enhancing user experience</li>\n  <li>None of the above</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Answer: <strong>Improving loading times</strong></p>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n\n<p>Write a blog post explaining the importance of caching, minification, and compression in web development, and provide examples of how to implement these techniques in your code.</p>\n\n<h3>Image Query</h3>\n\n<p>Search for images related to web performance optimization, caching, minification, and compression.</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><code>web performance optimization</code></li>\n  <li><code>caching</code></li>\n  <li><code>minification</code></li>\n  <li><code>compression</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Additional Resources</h3>\n\n<p>Here are some additional resources to help you learn more about web performance optimization:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Cache_API\">MDN Web Docs: Cache API</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/uglify-js\">UglifyJS library</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/zlib\">zlib library</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/2017/REC-html52-20171214/\">HTML5 specification</a></li>\n</ul>', 'Web Performance Optimization: Caching, Minification, and Compression', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(762, 775, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: short search query</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div>[HTML content here]', 'Best Practices for Web Security: Secure Coding and Input Validation', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(763, 776, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: web accessibility aria attributes screen reader support</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=web+accessibility+aria+attributes+screen+reader+support\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/web+accessibility+aria+attributes+screen+reader+support\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/web+accessibility+aria+attributes+screen+reader+support/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/web+accessibility+aria+attributes+screen+reader+support/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=web+accessibility+aria+attributes+screen+reader+support\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Implementing ARIA Attributes and Screen Reader Support</h3>\n<p>As a web developer, ensuring that your website is accessible to users with disabilities is crucial. In this hands-on internship, we will focus on implementing ARIA attributes and screen reader support to make our website more accessible.</p>\n<h3>What are ARIA Attributes?</h3>\n<p>ARIA (Accessible Rich Internet Applications) attributes are used to make dynamic web content more accessible to users with disabilities. They provide a way to describe the purpose of an element, its relationship to other elements, and the kind of interaction it supports.</p>\n<h3>Common ARIA Attributes</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>aria-label</strong>: Provides a text description of an element.</li>\n  <li><strong>aria-labelledby</strong>: References the ID of an element that provides a text description of the element.</li>\n  <li><strong>aria-describedby</strong>: References the ID of an element that provides a detailed description of the element.</li>\n  <li><strong>aria-expanded</strong>: Indicates whether an element is expanded or collapsed.</li>\n  <li><strong>aria-checked</strong>: Indicates whether a checkbox or radio button is checked.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Implementing ARIA Attributes in HTML</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;button aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Submit Form&quot;</span> aria-expanded=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;false&quot;</span> onclick=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submitForm()&quot;</span>&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n\n&lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;checkbox&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;remember-me&quot;</span> aria-checked=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;false&quot;</span> /&gt;\n\n&lt;button aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Toggle Menu&quot;</span> aria-expanded=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;true&quot;</span> onclick=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;toggleMenu()&quot;</span>&gt;Menu&lt;/button&gt;\n\n&lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;radio&quot;</span> id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;option-1&quot;</span> aria-checked=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;true&quot;</span> /&gt;\n\n&lt;button aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Close&quot;</span> onclick=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;closeModal()&quot;</span>&gt;&amp;times;&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Screen Reader Support</h3>\n<p>Screen readers are software programs that read aloud the text on a computer screen. To ensure that our website is accessible to users with screen readers, we need to provide a way for the screen reader to announce the content of our website.</p>\n<h3>Implementing Screen Reader Support in HTML</h3>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;nav role=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;navigation&quot;</span> aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Main Navigation&quot;</span>&gt;\n  &lt;ul&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;\n      &lt;a href=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;/home&quot;</span> aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Home&quot;</span>&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;\n    &lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;li&gt;\n      &lt;a href=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;/about&quot;</span> aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;About&quot;</span>&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;\n    &lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/nav&gt;\n\n&lt;main role=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;main&quot;</span> aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Main Content&quot;</span>&gt;\n  &lt;h1&gt;Welcome to Our Website&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;This <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> a paragraph of text.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/main&gt;\n\n&lt;footer role=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;contentinfo&quot;</span> aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Footer&quot;</span>&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Copyright <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2023</span> Our Website&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/footer&gt;</code></pre>\n<h3>Best Practices for Implementing ARIA Attributes and Screen Reader Support</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>Use ARIA attributes to provide a text description of an element.</li>\n  <li>Use the `role` attribute to define the role of an element.</li>\n  <li>Use the `aria-label` attribute to provide a text description of an element.</li>\n  <li>Use the `aria-labelledby` attribute to reference the ID of an element that provides a text description of the element.</li>\n  <li>Use the `aria-describedby` attribute to reference the ID of an element that provides a detailed description of the element.</li>\n  <li>Test your website with a screen reader to ensure that it is accessible.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n<p>In this hands-on internship, we learned how to implement ARIA attributes and screen reader support to make our website more accessible. By following best practices and using ARIA attributes, we can ensure that our website is accessible to users with disabilities.</p>\n<h3>Quiz</h3>\n<p>What is the purpose of the `aria-label` attribute?</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;button aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Submit Form&quot;</span> aria-expanded=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;false&quot;</span> onclick=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submitForm()&quot;</span>&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>What is the purpose of the `role` attribute?</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;nav role=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;navigation&quot;</span> aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Main Navigation&quot;</span>&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>What is the purpose of the `aria-labelledby` attribute?</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;button aria-labelledby=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;button-description&quot;</span> aria-expanded=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;false&quot;</span> onclick=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submitForm()&quot;</span>&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n\n&lt;span id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;button-description&quot;</span>&gt;Submit Form&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>What is the purpose of the `aria-describedby` attribute?</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;button aria-label=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;Submit Form&quot;</span> aria-describedby=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;button-description&quot;</span> aria-expanded=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;false&quot;</span> onclick=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;submitForm()&quot;</span>&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n\n&lt;span id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;button-description&quot;</span>&gt;Submit Form. This <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">is</span> a detailed description of the button.&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>', 'Web Accessibility Guidelines: Implementing ARIA Attributes and Screen Reader Support', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(764, 777, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: code organization and commenting</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=code+organization+and+commenting\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/code+organization+and+commenting\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/code+organization+and+commenting/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/code+organization+and+commenting/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=code+organization+and+commenting\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Code Organization and Commenting</h3><p>In this section, we will discuss the importance of code organization and commenting in web development.</p><ul><li>Keep your code organized and structured</li><li>Use comments to explain your code</li><li>Follow a consistent coding style</li></ul>', 'Web Development Best Practices: Code Organization and Commenting', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(765, 778, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: short search query</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/short+search+query/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=short+search+query\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div>...', 'Preparing for the Final Capstone Project: Project Idea and Planning', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(766, 779, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: Agile project planning and scope management visual</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=Agile+project+planning+and+scope+management+visual\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/Agile+project+planning+and+scope+management+visual\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/Agile+project+planning+and+scope+management+visual/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/Agile+project+planning+and+scope+management+visual/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=Agile+project+planning+and+scope+management+visual\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>By the end of this session, interns will understand how to define project scope, apply Agile methodologies (Scrum/Kanban), and prioritize tasks using frameworks like MoSCoW and the Eisenhower Matrix. They will create a practical project plan for a mock web development project.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><p><strong>1. Project Management Basics:</strong> Scope definition ensures deliverables align with stakeholder needs. Use tools like <code>Project Scope Statement</code> to document goals, constraints, and success criteria.</p>\n<p><strong>2. Agile Methodologies:</strong> Scrum uses sprints (2-4 weeks) with daily standups, while Kanban focuses on continuous workflow. Both emphasize iterative development and collaboration.</p>\n<p><strong>3. Prioritization Frameworks:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>MoSCoW Method:</strong> Categorize tasks as Must-have, Should-have, Could-have, or Won’t-have.</li>\n<li><strong>Eisenhower Matrix:</strong> Prioritize tasks by urgency/importance into four quadrants.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Define Project Scope:</strong>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#5c6370\">---</span>\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\"># Project Scope Statement</span>\nProject Name: E-Commerce Landing Page\nGoals: Build a responsive homepage <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> product showcase <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> CTA\nConstraints: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>-week timeline, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> developers, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span> designer\nSuccess Criteria: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">90</span>% user satisfaction <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> usability testing\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">---</span></code></pre>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Create User Stories for Agile:</strong>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">As a user,\nI want to see product images <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">and</span> descriptions\nSo that I can understand what we offer.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n- Images load <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">in</span> under 2s\n- Descriptions are under <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">100</span> words</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Plan a Sprint (Scrum Example):</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Sprint Goal: Complete homepage layout</li>\n<li>Tasks:\n<ul>\n<li>HTML/CSS structure (3 days)</li>\n<li>JavaScript interactivity (2 days)</li>\n<li>Testing (1 day)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Apply MoSCoW Prioritization:</strong>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">Must-have: Mobile responsiveness\nShould-have: Dark mode toggle\nCould-have: Animated transitions\nWon’t-have: User login system</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Build an Eisenhower Matrix:</strong>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">Urgent & Important: Fix critical bugs\nImportant but Not Urgent: Optimize images\nUrgent but Not Important: Answer non-critical emails\nNot Urgent/Important: Attend optional meetings</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><p>Submit a <code>project_plan.md</code> file containing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Scope statement</li>\n<li>User stories and sprint plan</li>\n<li>MoSCoW prioritization list</li>\n<li>Eisenhower Matrix for the first week</li>\n<li>Gantt chart (hand-drawn or digital)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>Trello</code> or <code>Jira</code> to simulate Kanban boards</li>\n<li>Update scope documents when requirements change</li>\n<li>Practice time-boxing tasks to avoid overcommitting</li>\n<li>Review priorities weekly with stakeholders</li>\n</ul>', 'Project Planning and Scope Definition', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(767, 780, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: project vision board example with wireframes</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=project+vision+board+example+with+wireframes\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/project+vision+board+example+with+wireframes\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/project+vision+board+example+with+wireframes/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/project+vision+board+example+with+wireframes/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=project+vision+board+example+with+wireframes\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>Create a <strong>project vision board</strong> using HTML and CSS to visualize the core ideas, user experience goals, and wireframes for a hypothetical web application. This task will help you practice <em>design thinking</em> by aligning technical and user-centered goals.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Design Thinking:</strong> A problem-solving approach focused on empathy, ideation, and prototyping. Use this to define your vision board’s purpose.</li>\n  <li><strong>User Experience (UX):</strong> Prioritize usability, accessibility, and intuitive navigation in your wireframes.</li>\n  <li><strong>Wireframing:</strong> Sketch the layout of your vision board using HTML elements to represent sections like headers, content blocks, and footers.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li>\n    <strong>Plan Your Vision Board:</strong>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Define the purpose of your hypothetical project (e.g., a task management app for students).</li>\n      <li>Identify 3-4 key sections: Project Goals, Target Users, Key Features, and Wireframes.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <strong>Structure the HTML:</strong>\n    <p>Create a basic HTML file with semantic elements. Example:</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;<!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Project Vision Board&lt;/title&gt;\n    &lt;link rel=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;stylesheet&quot;</span> href=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;styles.css&quot;</span> /&gt;\n  &lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;header&gt;&lt;h1&gt;My Vision Board&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;/header&gt;\n    &lt;section id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;goals&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Project Goals&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Goal <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/section&gt;\n    &lt;section id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;wireframes&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Wireframes&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;mockup&quot;</span>&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/section&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <strong>Add UX-Focused Content:</strong>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Use &lt;strong&gt; to highlight key user needs (e.g., &quot;Fast loading times&quot;).</li>\n      <li>Create a &lt;ul&gt; list for target users: &quot;Students aged 13-18&quot;, &quot;Busy professionals&quot;.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <strong>Wireframe Layout:</strong>\n    <p>Use &lt;div&gt; elements with CSS to sketch a basic layout. Example:</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">/* styles.css */\n.mockup {\n  width: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">80</span>%;\n  margin: 20px auto;\n  border: 2px dashed <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#333;</span>\n  padding: 10px;\n}\n\nheader {\n  background: <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">#f4f4f4;</span>\n  padding: 15px;\n  text-align: center;\n}</code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <strong>Test and Refine:</strong>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Resize your browser to ensure the layout adapts to different screens.</li>\n      <li>Add comments in your HTML to explain design choices: &lt;!-- Wireframe for homepage --&gt;.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>A fully functional HTML/CSS vision board with at least 3 sections (Goals, Users, Wireframes).</li>\n  <li>A screenshot of your vision board’s wireframe section.</li>\n  <li>A 100-word summary explaining how your design addresses user needs.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li>Use semantic tags like &lt;header&gt;, &lt;section&gt;, and &lt;footer&gt; for better accessibility.</li>\n  <li>Keep your CSS simple—focus on layout over aesthetics for this task.</li>\n  <li>Use &lt;code&gt; comments in your HTML to document your design thinking process.</li>\n</ol>', 'Creating a Project Vision Board', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
INSERT INTO `internship_content_blocks` (`id`, `lesson_id`, `type`, `content`, `title`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(768, 781, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: project planning tools gantt chart kanban board</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=project+planning+tools+gantt+chart+kanban+board\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/project+planning+tools+gantt+chart+kanban+board\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/project+planning+tools+gantt+chart+kanban+board/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/project+planning+tools+gantt+chart+kanban+board/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=project+planning+tools+gantt+chart+kanban+board\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3>\n<p>Create a project schedule with milestones using HTML and basic JavaScript to practice project planning, time management, and task prioritization. This task will help you organize tasks logically, allocate time effectively, and identify critical milestones.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Project Planning:</strong> Define project scope, break tasks into smaller units, and identify dependencies.</li>\n  <li><strong>Time Management:</strong> Estimate task durations, allocate deadlines, and avoid overcommitting.</li>\n  <li><strong>Task Prioritization:</strong> Use frameworks like the Eisenhower Matrix (urgent/important) or MoSCoW method (Must-have, Should-have, Could-have, Won’t-have).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Define Project Scope:</strong>\n    <p>Write a brief description of your project (e.g., &quot;Build a portfolio website&quot;). List the main deliverables and constraints.</p>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Break Down Tasks:</strong>\n    <p>Decompose the project into smaller tasks. For example:</p>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Design homepage layout</li>\n      <li>Implement navigation menu</li>\n      <li>Integrate contact form</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Estimate Time and Prioritize:</strong>\n    <p>Assign estimated hours/days to each task and prioritize them. Use a simple priority system (1 = High, 2 = Medium, 3 = Low).</p>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Create a Gantt Chart or Timeline:</strong>\n    <p>Use HTML and CSS to create a visual timeline. Example:</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;table border=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;1&quot;</span> <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">class</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;project-schedule&quot;</span>&gt;\n  &lt;thead&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Task&lt;/th&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Duration&lt;/th&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Start Date&lt;/th&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;End Date&lt;/th&gt;\n      &lt;th&gt;Priority&lt;/th&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/thead&gt;\n  &lt;tbody&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Design homepage&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span> days&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2024</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">04</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">01</span>&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2024</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">04</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">03</span>&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/td&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n    &lt;tr&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;Implement navigation&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span> days&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2024</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">04</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">04</span>&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2024</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">04</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">05</span>&lt;/td&gt;\n      &lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/td&gt;\n    &lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Set Milestones:</strong>\n    <p>Identify key milestones (e.g., &quot;Homepage design completed&quot;). Add them as a separate section in your HTML:</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;h4&gt;Milestones&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Milestone <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>&lt;/strong&gt;: Homepage design completed by <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2024</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">04</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">03</span>&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Milestone <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/strong&gt;: Navigation menu functional by <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2024</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">04</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">05</span>&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Add Interactivity (Optional):</strong>\n    <p>Use JavaScript to allow sorting tasks by priority. Example:</p>\n    <pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> sortTableByPriority() {\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> table = document.querySelector(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;.project-schedule&quot;</span>);\n    <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> rows = Array.<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span>(table.rows).slice(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>);\n    rows.sort((a, b) =&gt; {\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> aPriority = parseInt(a.cells[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>].innerText);\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">const</span> bPriority = parseInt(b.cells[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>].innerText);\n      <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> aPriority - bPriority;\n    });\n    rows.forEach(row =&gt; table.tBodies[<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">0</span>].appendChild(row));\n  }\n  document.getElementById(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;sort-btn&quot;</span>).addEventListener(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;click&quot;</span>, sortTableByPriority);\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;button id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">&quot;sort-btn&quot;</span>&gt;Sort by Priority&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>\n  </li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>Submit an HTML file named <code>project-schedule.html</code> that includes:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>A table of tasks with estimated durations, start/end dates, and priorities.</li>\n  <li>A list of milestones.</li>\n  <li>Optional: A &quot;Sort by Priority&quot; button that rearranges tasks dynamically.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>Use online tools like Trello or Gantt chart generators to validate your schedule visually.</li>\n  <li>Break tasks into <strong>1–3 day increments</strong> for better time tracking.</li>\n  <li>Revisit and update the schedule weekly to reflect progress.</li>\n  <li>For JavaScript interactivity, test in the browser console first.</li>\n</ul>', 'Developing a Project Schedule and Milestones', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(769, 782, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: project resource allocation gantt chart</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=project+resource+allocation+gantt+chart\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/project+resource+allocation+gantt+chart\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/project+resource+allocation+gantt+chart/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/project+resource+allocation+gantt+chart/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=project+resource+allocation+gantt+chart\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>By the end of this session, you will learn to create a project resource allocation plan and simulate team management processes for a web development project. You will apply concepts of team dynamics, communication strategies, and resource distribution to ensure project efficiency.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Team Dynamics:</strong> Understanding roles (developer, designer, QA, project manager) and how they collaborate.</li><li><strong>Communication:</strong> Tools like Slack, email, or meetings to maintain alignment.</li><li><strong>Resource Allocation:</strong> Balancing time, budget, and team capacity for tasks.</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><p><strong>Step 1: Define Project Scope</strong></p><p>Create an HTML file named <code>project-plan.html</code> to outline your project structure. Use headings and lists to describe deliverables.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;title&gt;Web Project Plan&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Project Scope&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;ul&gt;\n      &lt;li&gt;Frontend development&lt;/li&gt;\n      &lt;li&gt;Backend API integration&lt;/li&gt;\n      &lt;li&gt;User testing&lt;/li&gt;\n    &lt;/ul&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 2: Simulate Team Roles</strong></p><p>Add a section to your HTML file that assigns team members to tasks. Use a JSON-like structure to represent roles and responsibilities.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"application/json\"</span>&gt;\n{\n  <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"team\"</span>: [\n    {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"name\"</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Alice\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"role\"</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Frontend Developer\"</span>},\n    {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"name\"</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Bob\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"role\"</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Backend Developer\"</span>},\n    {<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"name\"</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Charlie\"</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"role\"</span>: <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Project Manager\"</span>}\n  ]\n}\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 3: Create a Resource Allocation Table</strong></p><p>Design an HTML table to allocate hours per task and team member. Include a Gantt chart placeholder image (search for \"project resource allocation gantt chart\" for the image query).</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;table border=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"1\"</span>&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Task&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Alice&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Bob&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Charlie&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Frontend&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;40h&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0h&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;10h&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Backend&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0h&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;50h&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;10h&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;\n&lt;img src=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"gantt-chart.png\"</span> alt=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Gantt Chart\"</span>&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<p><strong>Step 4: Simulate Communication Channels</strong></p><p>Write a simple HTML form to simulate a team communication tool (e.g., a task tracker). Include fields for task name, assigned member, and deadline.</p><pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;form&gt;\n  &lt;label&gt;Task Name: &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"text\"</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"task\"</span>&gt;&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;label&gt;Assign To: \n    &lt;select name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"assignee\"</span>&gt;\n      &lt;option value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Alice\"</span>&gt;Alice&lt;/option&gt;\n      &lt;option value=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"Bob\"</span>&gt;Bob&lt;/option&gt;\n    &lt;/select&gt;\n  &lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;label&gt;Deadline: &lt;input <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"date\"</span> name=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"deadline\"</span>&gt;&lt;/label&gt;\n  &lt;button <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">type</span>=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"submit\"</span>>Add Task</button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><ul><li>A working <code>project-plan.html</code> file with all four steps implemented.</li><li>A <code>gantt-chart.png</code> image file (you can download a placeholder or draw a simple version).</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use free tools like Trello or Asana to simulate real-world resource allocation if needed.</li><li>Test your HTML file in a browser to ensure all elements render correctly.</li><li>Document assumptions made during resource allocation (e.g., \"Assuming 40-hour workweeks\").</li></ul>', 'Project Resource Allocation and Team Management', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(770, 783, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: project risk assessment flowchart</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=project+risk+assessment+flowchart\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/project+risk+assessment+flowchart\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/project+risk+assessment+flowchart/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/project+risk+assessment+flowchart/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=project+risk+assessment+flowchart\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3><p>By the end of this task, you will learn to identify potential risks in a web development project, analyze their impact, and create mitigation strategies using HTML documentation and basic JavaScript logic for risk prioritization.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3><ul><li><strong>Risk Management:</strong> Systematic approach to identifying, analyzing, and responding to project risks</li><li><strong>Problem-Solving:</strong> Structured methods to address technical or operational challenges</li><li><strong>Contingency Planning:</strong> Preparing backup solutions for high-impact risks</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Step-by-Step Instructions</h3><ol>\n<li><strong>Identify Risks:</strong> Create an HTML table to document potential risks in your project. Example categories include:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;table&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Risk Description&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Impact (<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Likelihood (<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>-<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>)&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Browser compatibility issues&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Third-party API downtime&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</code></pre>\n</li>\n\n<li><strong>Analyze Risks:</strong> Add a calculated risk score column using JavaScript:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;script&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">function</span> calculateRiskScore(impact, likelihood) {\n  <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">return</span> impact * likelihood;\n}\n<span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Example usage:</span>\nconsole.log(calculateRiskScore(<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>, <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>)); <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">// Output: 12</span>\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>\n</li>\n\n<li><strong>Develop Mitigation Strategies:</strong> Add a column to your table with solutions. Example:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;table&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Browser compatibility issues&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">4</span>&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Use Babel <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> JS transpilation&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n  &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Third-party API downtime&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span>&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Implement local caching <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">with</span> localStorage&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</code></pre>\n</li>\n\n<li><strong>Create Contingency Plans:</strong> For high-risk items (score ≥ 12), write backup solutions in plain text format:\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">Contingency Plan <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">for</span> API Downtime:\n<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">1</span>. Show cached data <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">from</span> localStorage\n<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">2</span>. Display maintenance message <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">using</span>:\n&lt;div id=<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">\"maintenance&quot; style=\"</span>display:none\">Service temporarily unavailable&lt;/div&gt;\n<span style=\"color:#c41a16\">3</span>. Retry API call every <span style=\"color:#c41a16\">5</span> minutes <span style=\"color:#0033b3;font-weight:600\">using</span> setInterval()</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3><ul><li>HTML file with risk assessment table</li><li>Text document listing top 3 risks with mitigation strategies</li><li>JavaScript snippet for risk scoring calculation</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Use <code>localStorage</code> API for browser compatibility testing</li><li>Test your contingency plans using browser developer tools</li><li>Update risk scores weekly as project scope changes</li></ul>', 'Project Risk Assessment and Mitigation', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50'),
(771, 784, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: project review checklist</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=project+review+checklist\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/project+review+checklist\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/project+review+checklist/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/project+review+checklist/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=project+review+checklist\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Task Objective</h3>\n<p>The goal of today’s internship day is to conduct a comprehensive review of the web development project you completed over the past weeks. You will evaluate the codebase, identify strengths and weaknesses, extract lessons learned, and document best practices that can be applied to future projects. By the end of the day, you should have a clear set of actionable insights and a polished project review report.</p>\n\n<h3>Concepts You Need</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Code Quality Metrics</strong> – Understand readability, maintainability, and performance indicators.</li>\n<li><strong>Testing Coverage</strong> – Know how to assess unit, integration, and end‑to‑end tests.</li>\n<li><strong>Documentation Standards</strong> – Recognize the importance of inline comments, README files, and API docs.</li>\n<li><strong>Version Control Practices</strong> – Review commit history, branching strategy, and pull request etiquette.</li>\n<li><strong>Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD)</strong> – Evaluate pipeline configuration and automated checks.</li>\n<li><strong>Security Hygiene</strong> – Spot common vulnerabilities such as XSS, CSRF, and insecure data handling.</li>\n<li><strong>Accessibility (a11y)</strong> – Ensure the project meets WCAG guidelines.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Step‑by‑Step Instructions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1. Gather Artefacts</strong>\n<p>Collect all relevant files: the source code, test suites, documentation, and any CI/CD configuration files. Clone the repository to a clean local branch called <code>review-branch</code> to avoid accidental changes to the main code.</p></li>\n<li><strong>2. Run Automated Tests</strong>\n<p>Execute the test suite and record coverage percentages. If the coverage is below 80%, note which modules lack tests.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npm run test <span style=\"color:#5c6370\">-- --coverage</span>\n</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>3. Static Analysis</strong>\n<p>Run a linter and a static code analyzer. Capture any linting errors or warnings.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npm run lint\n</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>4. Performance Audit</strong>\n<p>Open the application in Chrome DevTools, run a Lighthouse audit, and document performance scores. Pay special attention to load time, interactivity, and best practices.</p></li>\n<li><strong>5. Security Scan</strong>\n<p>Use a tool like <code>npm audit</code> to detect vulnerable dependencies. Record any critical findings.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">npm audit\n</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>6. Accessibility Check</strong>\n<p>Run axe or Lighthouse accessibility checks. Note any violations and propose fixes.</p></li>\n<li><strong>7. Code Review</strong>\n<p>Read through the codebase, focusing on naming conventions, component structure, and state management patterns. Highlight any duplicated logic or overly complex functions.</p></li>\n<li><strong>8. Documentation Review</strong>\n<p>Verify that the README contains installation steps, usage examples, and contribution guidelines. Ensure that API endpoints are documented and that component props are clearly described.</p></li>\n<li><strong>9. Version Control Audit</strong>\n<p>Examine commit messages for clarity and consistency. Check that feature branches were merged with rebase or squash, and that merge commits are descriptive.</p></li>\n<li><strong>10. Compile Lessons Learned</strong>\n<p>For each evaluation area, write a brief reflection: what went well, what could be improved, and why. Use concrete examples from the code or project workflow.</p></li>\n<li><strong>11. Draft Best Practices Checklist</strong>\n<p>Create a checklist that future developers can follow. Include items like “Write unit tests for every new component,” “Document public APIs,” and “Run security audit before release.”</p></li>\n<li><strong>12. Prepare Deliverable</strong>\n<p>Compile all findings into a single PDF or Markdown file titled <code>Project-Review-Day-90.md</code>. Include screenshots of audit results and code snippets where relevant.</p>\n<pre style=\"background:#d7dbdb;color:#1a1a1a;padding:16px;border-radius:8px;overflow-x:auto;font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin:14px 0;border:1px solid #b9bfbf\"><code style=\"background:transparent;color:#1a1a1a;font-family:inherit\">&lt;div&gt;Evaluation Result&lt;/div&gt;\n</code></pre></li>\n<li><strong>13. Submit Report</strong>\n<p>Push the review file to the repository and create a pull request. In the PR description, summarize the key insights and request feedback from the mentor.</p></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Deliverable</h3>\n<p>The final deliverable is a comprehensive project review document that covers:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Automated test coverage and gaps.</li>\n<li>Linting and static analysis outcomes.</li>\n<li>Performance and accessibility audit results.</li>\n<li>Security vulnerability summary.</li>\n<li>Code quality observations.</li>\n<li>Documentation completeness.</li>\n<li>Version control hygiene.</li>\n<li>Lessons learned with actionable recommendations.</li>\n<li>Best practices checklist for future projects.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tips</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use a dedicated editor window for each audit tool to keep your workspace organized.</li>\n<li>When documenting lessons, frame them as questions: “Why did this happen?” and “How can we prevent it next time?”</li>\n<li>Leverage GitHub’s <code>Insights</code> tab to analyze commit frequency and contributor activity.</li>\n<li>Keep your review concise; aim for 1–2 pages per evaluation area.</li>\n<li>Invite a peer to read your report before submission; a fresh pair of eyes catches overlooked issues.</li>\n<li>Store the checklist in the repository’s <code>docs/</code> folder so it becomes part of the project’s living documentation.</li>\n<li>Remember that the goal is continuous improvement, not perfection. Highlight progress as well as pain points.</li>\n</ul>', 'Project Review and Evaluation', 1, '2026-06-12 11:20:50', '2026-06-12 11:20:50');
